E["npc:elder-runetotem"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Runetotem",z="durotar",s="Elder Runetotem is an ancestral tauren spirit appearing outside Razor Hill in Durotar during the Lunar Festival. As one of the revered elders of the Horde, she offers wisdom and her blessing to travelers who seek her out across the red canyons.",h="Elder Runetotem is an ancestral tauren spirit appearing outside Razor Hill in Durotar during the Lunar...",sec={{t="A Spirit in Durotar",b="Though ancestral tauren spirits are typically tied to the grassy plains and sacred burial grounds of Mulgore, Elder Runetotem lingers far from the pastures of her people. She manifests beside the dusty settlement of Razor Hill in Durotar. To young orcs and wandering adventurers, her ethereal presence serves as a bridge between the ancient traditions of the Shu'halo and the harsh new home the Horde has carved along the Great Sea.",sp=0},{t="Ancestral Honors",b="During the Lunar Festival, the spirits of great leaders, shamans, and heroes manifest throughout the world to commune with the living. Elder Runetotem represents the Runetotem line—a lineage known for deep reverence for the Earth Mother and spiritual communion. Travelers honoring her presence are granted ancestral tokens and her spiritual blessing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Runetotem?",a="Elder Runetotem is a ghostly tauren ancestor who manifests near Razor Hill in Durotar. She is one of the honored elders who returns during the Lunar Festival to greet travelers and grant ancestral blessings.",al={"elder runetotem lore","who is the tauren ghost in razor hill","runetotem ghost"}},{q="Why is a tauren spirit located in Durotar?",a="While most tauren ancestral spirits are rooted in Mulgore, the spirits of the Lunar Festival wander far and wide across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Her presence in Razor Hill allows Horde travelers passing through Durotar to pay their respects to the wisdom of the Earth Mother's children.",al={"why is runetotem in razor hill","tauren ghost durotar"}},{q="What connection does she have to the Runetotem tribe?",a="She bears the name of the Runetotem clan, one of the prominent tauren lineages renowned for their shamans, spiritual guides, and connections to the natural world.",al={"runetotem tribe elder","runetotem family"}},{q="What does speaking with her grant?",a="Speaking with Elder Runetotem honors her memory during the Lunar Festival, rewarding adventurers with a Coin of Ancestry and a temporary blessing from the spirits.",al={"what does elder runetotem give","runetotem reward"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Finding a venerable ancestor of the Runetotem tribe so far from Mulgore is a humbling reminder that the spirits of the Shu'halo watch over their allies across all lands.",["faction:Horde"]="Standing outside the heavily fortified settlement of Razor Hill, her presence embodies the spiritual alliance between the orcs of Durotar and the tauren of Mulgore."},kw={"coin of ancestry","durotar","elder runetotem","lunar festival","razor hill","runetotem","tauren ghost"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:8670","topic:tauren","zone:mulgore","subzone:red-rocks"},src={"Elder Runetotem"}}
E["npc:furl-scornbrow"] = {t="npc",n="Furl Scornbrow",z="durotar",s="Furl Scornbrow is an aging orc lookout stationed in the watchtower northwest of Razor Hill. No longer able to fight on the front lines due to his advancing years, he keeps watch over the red canyons of Durotar and crafts sturdy packs for young travelers setting out across the land.",h="Furl Scornbrow is an aging orc lookout stationed in the watchtower northwest of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="Watchman of the Ridge",b="Perched high in the wooden watchtower just northwest of Razor Hill, Furl Scornbrow keeps a quiet vigil over the central plains of Durotar. In the tense early days following the founding of Orgrimmar, sentries like Furl were vital for sounding signal horns against hostile quilboar, centaur, and Kul Tiras interlopers. As Durotar has stabilized and Razor Hill has established firmer borders, emergencies have grown rarer, leaving Furl plenty of quiet hours at his post.",sp=0},{t="A Useful Pair of Hands",b="Furl freely admits that his old bones and fading strength render him useless in battle, but an orc does not easily surrender their purpose. Rather than sitting idle, he puts his hands to work fashioning canvas sacks and packs for fresh recruits who need to carry their supplies. In exchange for coarse thread and practical materials, he equips green adventurers venturing out to prove their worth to the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furl Scornbrow?",a="Furl Scornbrow is an elderly orc watchman stationed in the lookout tower perched atop the bluffs northwest of Razor Hill. Unable to serve as a front-line warrior due to his age, he watches the horizon for danger and crafts bags for young travelers.",al={"who is furl","furl scornbrow lore","furl in razor hill"}},{q="What is Furl's role in Durotar?",a="He mans the signal horn tower watching for invaders approaching Razor Hill. Because Durotar has grown increasingly secure under Horde control, he sounds the alarm far less often, spending his spare time helping incoming recruits organize their gear.",al={"what does furl do","furl purpose"}},{q="Why does Furl ask travelers for materials?",a="Furl believes every member of the Horde must carry their weight, regardless of circumstance. Since he can no longer fight, he stitches practical travel packs to aid newer warriors, asking only for basic materials like coarse thread to finish the work.",al={"carry your weight quest lore","why does furl want thread"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Furl embodies the orcish belief that even when age robs a warrior of their martial strength, an honorable life means finding another way to serve the clan and Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="Stationed along the ridges outside Razor Hill, Furl represents the vigilance required to protect Durotar's fledgling settlements against lingering threats."},kw={"carry your weight","durotar","furl scornbrow","lookout","orc","razor hill","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:791"},src={"Furl Scornbrow"}}
E["npc:gar-thok"] = {t="npc",n="Gar'Thok",z="durotar",s="Gar'Thok is a veteran orc warrior and outpost commander stationed at Razor Hill in Durotar. Having fought at Mount Hyjal and survived the initial Kul Tiras landings on Durotar's coast, he now coordinates local defense against human encroachers and native threats. He directs young Horde recruits stepping out of the Valley of Trials to secure the red wastes of the new homeland.",h="Gar'Thok is a veteran orc warrior and outpost commander stationed at Razor Hill in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Veteran of the Red Wastes",b="Before settling in Razor Hill, Gar'Thok defended the orc encampment during the apocalyptic Battle of Mount Hyjal. Following the Third War, he marched to Durotar under Warchief Thrall and served as a lieutenant under Nazgrel during the earliest days of building the new homeland. When the Mok'Nathal wanderer Rexxar first arrived in Durotar, it was Gar'Thok who alerted him to the aggressive quilboar raiding their perimeter, enlisting the beastmaster to safeguard the fragile new settlement.",sp=0},{t="Surviving the Admiral's Invasion",b="Gar'Thok's resolve was tested when Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet landed along the eastern shores of Durotar. Stationed at an outlying watch post, Gar'Thok witnessed his garrison overwhelmed and brutally slaughtered by naval marines. Though his forces were decimated, Gar'Thok survived the onslaught. The memory of that surprise assault cemented his vigilance against the surviving marines who still occupy Tiragarde Keep and the coastal shipwrecks.",sp=0},{t="Defense of Razor Hill",b="Today, Gar'Thok oversees the martial defense of central Durotar from the barracks of Razor Hill. He wastes no time with pleasantries, immediately tasking emerging Horde warriors, shamans, and scouts with clearing out hostile Kul Tiran remnants, repossessing salvaged supplies, and recovering military orders left in the coastal ruins. To him, the safety of Durotar is far from guaranteed, requiring constant pressure against any who question the Horde's right to this soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gar'Thok?",a="Gar'Thok is an orc officer stationed in Razor Hill who organizes the local military response against hostile forces in Durotar. He is a veteran of the Third War who served under Nazgrel during the founding of Orgrimmar.",al={"garthok lore","who is garthok","razor hill commander"}},{q="Where did Gar'Thok fight before coming to Razor Hill?",a="He fought at the Battle of Mount Hyjal, guarding the orc fortifications against the Burning Legion and the Scourge. Later, he served at a frontier outpost in Durotar, working with Rexxar to quell early quilboar raids.",al={"garthok past","garthok mount hyjal","garthok history"}},{q="Why does Gar'Thok hate the humans in Durotar so much?",a="During the invasion led by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, sailors from Kul Tiras ambushed Gar'Thok's outpost on the coast, butchering his men. He survived the assault and remains dedicated to eradicating the remaining marine encampments.",al={"why garthok hates kul tiras","garthok humans","tiragarde keep garthok"}},{q="What threats does Gar'Thok send adventurers to fight?",a="Gar'Thok sends recruits to fight the hostile Kul Tiran sailors entrenched at Tiragarde Keep, reclaim supplies from coastal shipwrecks, push back invading quilboar, and uncover any orders left behind by human commanders.",al={"garthok quests","what does garthok want","razor hill quests"}},{q="What is his relationship with Nazgrel and Thrall?",a="Gar'Thok served as a trusted lieutenant under Nazgrel during the initial colonizing expeditions in Durotar, operating directly under the authority of Warchief Thrall to secure the borders of the newly claimed territory.",al={"garthok nazgrel","garthok thrall","garthok rank"}},{q="Where can Gar'Thok be found?",a="Gar'Thok stands outside the main watchtower and barracks in Razor Hill, the central settlement of Durotar located south of Orgrimmar.",al={"garthok location","where is garthok","find garthok"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs leaving the Valley of Trials, Gar'Thok represents the stern, unyielding discipline of the veteran generation that bled at Mount Hyjal to win Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="Gar'Thok ensures that fresh recruits of all Horde races understand the precariousness of their new territory, directing them to repel invasive Alliance remnants.",["class:Warrior"]="As a frontline commander who survived both demonic legions and brutal naval ambushes, Gar'Thok expects martial fortitude and unhesitating obedience from fellow warriors."},kw={"daelin","durotar","gar'thok","garthok","kul tiras","nazgrel","razor hill","rexxar","tiragarde"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:kul-tiras","quest:784","quest:830","quest:825","topic:quilboar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Gar'Thok"}}
E["npc:gornek"] = {t="npc",n="Gornek",z="durotar",s="Gornek is an orc overseer stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He serves as the primary point of intake for fresh orc and Darkspear troll recruits preparing to prove their worth to the New Horde.",h="Gornek is an orc overseer stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="Welcoming the Unproven",b="Standing directly at the heart of the Valley of Trials, Gornek represents the initial test of discipline for aspiring Horde warriors, scouts, and spellcasters. Under Warchief Thrall's order, every youth and newcomer must earn their place through grit and perseverance rather than entitlement. Gornek assesses those stepping into the valley, reading their introductory orders and directing them to trainers throughout the compound. Whether an initiate carries an encrypted scrawl, a glyphic parchment, or a simple tablet, it is Gornek who receives their credentials and sets them upon their harsh path of survival.",sp=0},{t="A Life in Service to Durotar",b="The arid canyons of the valley test more than battle prowess; they instill the communal ethos of the New Horde. Gornek ensures that novices do not linger aimlessly, pointing them toward the trials of the nearby scorpid burrows, the dens of feral boars, and the watchful eyes of veteran instructors. For those who survive the training grounds and slay the threats lurking in the red rock gullies, Gornek offers the final acknowledgment before dispatching them outward into the wider, perilous landscape of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an orc greeter and taskmaster in the Valley of Trials. He oversees new recruits of the Horde, reading their induction documents and guiding them to their respective class trainers.",al={"gornek","who is this orc","who is gornek"}},{q="Where can I find Gornek?",a="He stands near the center of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar, just outside the Den where young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their journeys.",al={"gornek location","where is gornek","gornek map"}},{q="Why do new recruits report to him?",a="New arrivals carry training scrolls and tablets designating their chosen discipline. Gornek evaluates these letters of introduction, confirms their eligibility, and sends them to the appropriate mentors within the valley.",al={"why visit gornek","parchment quest","tablet quest"}},{q="What is his role in the New Horde?",a="He acts as an entry coordinator for Thrall's New Horde. His duty is to ensure no recruit enters the broader lands of Durotar without first learning the basic tenets of honor, survival, and martial readiness.",al={"gornek horde role","what does gornek do"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, reporting to Gornek is the very first step toward shedding childhood and earning an honorable place in Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="As allies sheltered by Thrall, Darkspear trolls present their credentials to Gornek to prove they stand as capable equals alongside their orc brothers."},kw={"den","durotar","gornek","parchment","the new horde","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:787","quest:1089","quest:98576","topic:new-horde","topic:horde"},src={"Gornek"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-grosk"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Grosk",z="durotar",s="Innkeeper Grosk manages the inn at Razor Hill, providing weary travelers with food, drink, and a place to rest in central Durotar. Located on the bustling road between the Valley of Trials and Orgrimmar, his establishment serves as the primary resting point for young Horde adventurers setting out into the wider world.",h="Innkeeper Grosk manages the inn at Razor Hill, providing weary travelers with food, drink, and a place to...",sec={{t="Hospitality in the Red Wastes",b="Razor Hill serves as the vital crossroad settlement connecting the southern training grounds of Durotar to the high walls of Orgrimmar. At the center of this waystation stands Innkeeper Grosk, an orc tasked with sheltering warriors, scouts, and peons alike. His inn offers a respite from the harsh desert heat, stocked with basic provisions, hearty meats, and cool water for any traveler passing beneath its sturdy timbers.",sp=0},{t="A Peon's Respite",b="Beyond serving passing travelers, Grosk assists the local labor force that keeps Durotar running. In the quest 'A Peon's Burden', overseers rely on Grosk's establishment to source much-needed supplies and food rations for the exhausted peons working the regional lumber and mining operations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Innkeeper Grosk located?",a="Innkeeper Grosk stands inside the inn at Razor Hill, situated right in the center of Durotar along the primary road leading north toward Orgrimmar.",al={"innkeeper grosk location","where is grosk","razor hill innkeeper"}},{q="What services does Innkeeper Grosk provide?",a="Grosk acts as an innkeeper where Horde adventurers can bind their Hearthstone to Razor Hill. He also sells basic food, water, and meat to replenish health and mana between travels.",al={"what does grosk do","grosk vendor","can i bind hearthstone at razor hill"}},{q="Does Innkeeper Grosk offer any quests?",a="He is involved in the quest 'A Peon's Burden', aiding in organizing supplies and provisions intended to sustain the hardworking peons toiling across Durotar.",al={"innkeeper grosk quests","a peons burden turn in"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For newly blooded orcs, trolls, and visiting tauren traveling north from the Valley of Trials or Sen'jin Village, Grosk's inn marks the first true town and hearth location on the road toward Orgrimmar."},kw={"durotar","grosk","innkeeper","innkeeper grosk","orgrimmar","peon's burden","razor hill"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:2161","zone:orgrimmar","npc:magga"},src={"Innkeeper Grosk"}}
E["npc:kali-remik"] = {t="npc",n="Kali Remik",z="durotar",s="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll hunter who spends her time lending guidance to travelers across the Horde's heartland. Familiar with the ways of tracking and survival in Durotar, she directs young hunters toward greater teachers in Orgrimmar.",h="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll hunter who spends her time lending guidance to travelers across the Horde's...",sec={{t="A Guide for the Hunt",b="Kali Remik is a seasoned jungle troll tracker well-acquainted with the arid wastes of Durotar and the bustling hubs of the Horde. In coastal settlements like Sen'jin Village, she watches over young scouts taking their first steps outside the Valley of Trials. Knowing when a novice outgrows the local training grounds, she steps in to direct promising marksmen and beastmasters toward the grand halls of Orgrimmar, ensuring the Horde's frontier ranks stay sharp and disciplined.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kali Remik?",a="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll scout and quest giver. She helps guide fledgling Horde adventurers, especially hunters ready to advance their training beyond local outposts.",al={"kali remik lore","who is kali remik","kali remik npc"}},{q="Where can Kali Remik be found?",a="She can be found aiding her people in Durotar, notably around Sen'jin Village.",al={"where is kali remik","kali remik location","find kali remik"}},{q="What guidance does she offer to hunters?",a="Through 'The Hunter's Path', Kali directs young orc and troll hunters who have proven their basic skills to travel to Orgrimmar, seeking advanced instruction from the veteran hunters stationed there.",al={"the hunters path quest","kali remik hunter quest","what does kali teach"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For young orc and troll marksmen, Kali acts as a stepping stone, recognizing when your skills outstrip village drills and sending you forward to the master trainers in Orgrimmar.",["race:Troll"]="A fellow member of the Darkspear tribe, Kali keeps watch over her kin as they rebuild their lives along Durotar's coast and settle within Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","kali remik","sen'jin village","the hunter's path","tracker","valley of spirits"},rel={"quest:6065","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:troll","topic:horde","quest:8355"},src={"Kali Remik"}}
E["npc:kor-ghan"] = {t="npc",n="Kor'ghan",z="durotar",s="Kor'ghan is a Darkspear jungle troll who can be found lingering in the murky caverns of the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar. Positioned right outside Rekkul's Poisons, he seeks assistance in concocting remedies against venomous wilderness predators.",h="Kor'ghan is a Darkspear jungle troll who can be found lingering in the murky caverns of the Cleft of Shadow...",sec={{t="A Troll in the Shadows",b="Standing before Rekkul's Poisons in the cavernous depths of the Cleft of Shadow, Kor'ghan keeps close watch over remedies and toxins alike. Although he once frequented Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar, he now resides in the capital, dispatching adventurers across the red canyons to gather venomous components from Durotar's scorpids in order to prepare vital antidotes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kor'ghan?",a="Kor'ghan is a Darkspear troll located in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar, standing outside Rekkul's poison shop.",al={"kor'ghan","who is kor'ghan","korghan npc"}},{q="Where can I find Kor'ghan?",a="He is located in the subterranean Cleft of Shadow beneath central Orgrimmar, stationed directly in front of Rekkul's Poisons.",al={"kor'ghan location","where is korghan","find korghan"}},{q="What does Kor'ghan need help with?",a="He enlists travelers to gather poison sacs from the venomtail scorpids roaming near the entrance of Orgrimmar to help formulate antidotes.",al={"kor'ghan quest","finding the antidote quest","korghan venom"}},{q="Was Kor'ghan ever found in Durotar?",a="Yes, Kor'ghan originally spent his time in Sen'jin Village on the Durotar coastline before taking up his spot near the poison suppliers in Orgrimmar.",al={"kor'ghan sen'jin","korghan old location"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Positioned directly outside Rekkul's Poisons in the Cleft of Shadow, Kor'ghan is a familiar sight to rogues visiting the underbelly of Orgrimmar for reagents and venoms.",["race:Troll"]="Like many Darkspear kin who have left Sen'jin Village, Kor'ghan puts his practical knowledge of Durotar's wild hazards to use in the Horde's fortified capital."},kw={"antidote","cleft of shadow","kor'ghan","korghan","orgrimmar","rekkul's poisons","scorpid venom","sen'jin village"},rel={"subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","quest:813","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Kor'ghan"}}
E["npc:lar-prowltusk"] = {t="npc",n="Lar Prowltusk",z="durotar",s="Lar Prowltusk is a Darkspear troll sentinel stationed southwest of Sen'jin Village in Durotar. From his post on the frontier, he keeps watch over encroaching threats to the young troll settlement, directing adventurers to blunt the advances of nearby enemies.",h="Lar Prowltusk is a Darkspear troll sentinel stationed southwest of Sen'jin Village in Durotar.",sec={{t="Watcher on the Coast",b="Situated southwest of Sen'jin Village along the rugged Durotar coastline, Lar Prowltusk stands as one of the Darkspear tribe's forward sentinels. With the trolls still working to secure a permanent home after fleeing their sunken island chain, Sen'jin Village faces constant harassment from hostile neighbors. Lar coordinates scouts and warriors to monitor coastal movements and curb the aggression of hostile forces—particularly the Kolkar centaur—ensuring the fragile settlement has room to breathe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lar Prowltusk?",a="Lar Prowltusk is a Darkspear troll quest giver stationed just southwest of Sen'jin Village in Durotar. He helps guard the settlement's outskirts by enlisting capable Horde travelers to strike at regional threats before they reach the village proper.",al={"lar prowltusk","who is lar prowltusk","lar prowltusk durotar"}},{q="What threats does Lar Prowltusk focus on?",a="Lar focuses on frontier dangers that threaten southern Durotar, notably the marauding Kolkar centaur packs pushing into troll territory.",al={"lar prowltusk quests","what does lar prowltusk want"}},{q="Where can Lar Prowltusk be found?",a="He is located in southern Durotar, keeping watch along the paths southwest of Sen'jin Village.",al={"lar prowltusk location","where is lar prowltusk"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, scouts like Lar Prowltusk are vital to safeguarding the tribe's fragile new home in Durotar against aggressive centaur clans and encroaching human forces.",["faction:Horde"]="Lar Prowltusk represents the Horde's struggle to secure the borders of Durotar against external threats right outside their fledgling capital's backyard."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","kolkar","lar prowltusk","northwatch","sen'jin village","troll"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","quest:786","topic:troll","topic:alliance"},src={"Lar Prowltusk"}}
E["npc:magga"] = {t="npc",n="Magga",z="durotar",s="Magga is an orc resident living in the dusty settlement of Razor Hill within Durotar. Stationed near the town's lively tavern, she serves as a welcoming face for newly arrived Horde adventurers making their way out of the Valley of Trials.",h="Magga is an orc resident living in the dusty settlement of Razor Hill within Durotar.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Face in Razor Hill",b="Razor Hill serves as the first real taste of the wider world for young orcs and darkspear trolls emerging from the Valley of Trials. Positioned right beside the local inn, Magga helps orient new arrivals to the outpost, introducing them to local amenities and the hospitality of Innkeeper Grosk. While she keeps a low profile among the outpost's busy grunts and tradespeople, she helps bind the small settlement together.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Magga?",a="Magga is an orc civilian stationed in Razor Hill, Durotar. She stands near the inn, welcoming new Horde travelers and pointing them toward lodging and rest.",al={"magga durotar","magga razor hill","who is magga"}},{q="What is Magga's connection to Innkeeper Grosk?",a="Magga directs weary travelers to Innkeeper Grosk inside the Razor Hill inn so they can bind their hearthstones and rest after their journey from the Valley of Trials.",al={"magga and grosk","magga innkeeper"}},{q="Does Magga offer any quests?",a="Yes, Magga offers a brief introductory greeting task titled 'Welcome!', which directs new adventurers to speak directly with the local innkeeper.",al={"magga quests","welcome quest"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For fresh recruits leaving the harsh trials of the Valley of Trials behind, Magga provides a reassuring welcome to Durotar's first true settlement."},kw={"durotar","horde","innkeeper grosk","magga","orc","razor hill","welcome"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","npc:innkeeper-grosk","quest:5805"},src={"Magga"}}
E["npc:mai-ah"] = {t="npc",n="Mai'ah",z="durotar",s="Mai'ah is a jungle troll mage trainer stationed within the sun-scorched basin of the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She mentors fledgling spellcasters among the Darkspear trolls who step into the red canyons to hone their command of the arcane. For young trolls beginning the path of wizardry, she offers early guidance and instruction in the foundational arts of magic.",h="Mai'ah is a jungle troll mage trainer stationed within the sun-scorched basin of the Valley of Trials in...",sec={{t="Arcane Mentor of the Den",b="While orcs overwhelmingly favor the primal call of the elements or the physical dominance of the warrior, Darkspear trolls possess a rare affinity for arcane study. Standing within the Valley of Trials, Mai'ah serves as an instructor for young troll mages arriving to undertake their rites of adulthood. She receives candidates carrying glyphic inscriptions and begins shaping their chaotic raw power into disciplined incantations, ensuring they learn the control required to survive Durotar's perils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mai'ah?",a="Mai'ah is a Darkspear troll mage trainer situated in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She provides initial guidance, training, and foundational spells to newly arrived troll spellcasters before they venture out into the wider lands of the Horde.",al={"who is maiah","maiah lore","troll mage trainer"}},{q="Why is there a troll mage trainer in an orc starting area?",a="Following the destruction of the Darkspear Isles and their relocation to Durotar alongside Thrall's orcs, young Darkspear trolls undergo their coming-of-age trials alongside orc youths. Because orc culture largely shuns arcane magic due to past demon corruption, troll mages like Mai'ah step in to guide their own kind.",al={"why troll mage here","valley of trials troll trainer","troll mage durotar"}},{q="What role does she play in training new mages?",a="Mai'ah welcomes new troll mages bearing written instructions such as glyphic parchments. She initiates their formal training, teaching the fundamentals of spellcasting so they can defend the Valley of Trials from local beasts and rogue Burning Blade infiltrators.",al={"what does maiah do","glyphic parchment maiah","maiah quests"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For Darkspear spellcasters, Mai'ah represents the beginning of their magical journey, teaching the discipline needed to weave fire, frost, and arcane energy under the harsh sun of Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="Mai'ah provides Darkspear youths in the Valley of Trials with cultural mentorship in an art rarely practiced by their orcish allies."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","mage trainer","mai'ah","maiah","troll","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:98576","topic:troll"},src={"Mai'ah"}}
E["npc:master-gadrin"] = {t="npc",n="Master Gadrin",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin is an elderly jungle troll and the venerable chief witch doctor of the Darkspear tribe, currently residing in Sen'jin Village. Having mentored both Chieftain Vol'jin and the renegade witch doctor Zalazane, he now coordinates efforts to aid his displaced people and break the dark curse gripping their stolen home on the Echo Isles.",h="Master Gadrin is an elderly jungle troll and the venerable chief witch doctor of the Darkspear tribe...",sec={{t="Mentor of the Darkspear",b="Long before the Darkspear arrived on Kalimdor, Master Gadrin served as the chief witch doctor of his tribe in their ancestral South Seas islands. Known affectionately to his closest pupils as 'Gad', he guided the mystical training of generations of priests, mages, and witch doctors. Among his most gifted students were two inseparable youths: Vol'jin, the son of their chieftain, and Zalazane. It was Gadrin who welcomed them back from their coming-of-age trials, bearing the heavy news of Sen'jin's death and the alliance with Thrall's orcs.",sp=0},{t="The Betrayal of Zalazane",b="When the Darkspear settled the Echo Isles alongside the Horde, Gadrin and Zalazane continued training the tribe's spiritual practitioners together. Tragically, Zalazane succumbed to madness, intoxicated by the dark voodoo forces he sought to wield. The rogue practitioner enslaved his brethren's minds and drove Vol'jin and the uncorrupted Darkspear onto the mainland of Durotar. Now based in Sen'jin Village, Gadrin carries the personal sorrow of seeing a former student become a tyrannical monster, working tirelessly to lay slain tribesfolk to rest and end Zalazane's reign.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of Ancient Lore",b="Beyond the crisis on the Echo Isles, Gadrin stands as one of the Horde's greatest living authorities on troll spiritualism and loa lore. Scholars, shamans, and even the Royal Apothecary Society seek his insight on arcane and alchemical mysteries. When strange threats like the Burning Blade brush against Durotar, or distant researchers require forgotten rituals—such as deciphering ancient tablets in Zul'Farrak to invoke Shadra the spider loa—it is Gadrin who possesses the knowledge to craft the necessary bindings.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Gadrin?",a="Master Gadrin is the chief witch doctor and an elder spiritual leader of the Darkspear trolls. Located in Sen'jin Village on the coast of Durotar, he serves as a senior advisor to Chieftain Vol'jin.",al={"master gadrin lore","who is gadrin","gadrin npc"}},{q="What is Gadrin's history with Zalazane?",a="Gadrin was Zalazane's mentor in the South Seas and on the Echo Isles. He personally trained the young troll in voodoo and mysticism alongside Vol'jin, only to watch in horror as Zalazane fell to dark magic, went mad, and drove the Darkspear from their island home.",al={"gadrin and zalazane","how does gadrin know zalazane","zalazane mentor"}},{q="Why is Gadrin staying in Sen'jin Village?",a="When Zalazane's curse drove the Darkspear off the Echo Isles, the survivors established Sen'jin Village on the southern coast of Durotar as a refuge. Gadrin remains in the village to counsel refugees, track local threats, and direct strikes against Zalazane's forces.",al={"why is gadrin here","what is gadrin doing in senjin village"}},{q="Who is Minshina?",a="Minshina was Master Gadrin's brother. He perished during the turmoil on the Echo Isles, and his restless spirit began calling to Gadrin in dreams. Gadrin asks trusted adventurers to recover his brother's skull so his soul may finally find peace.",al={"minshina brother","minshinas skull quest lore","who was minshina"}},{q="Does Gadrin help with the Burning Blade cult?",a="Yes. After receiving word from Zureetha Fargaze about the Burning Blade infiltrating the Valley of Trials, Gadrin monitors the cult's presence near Sen'jin Village. Seeing the wider danger to Durotar, he sends recruits north to report to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.",al={"burning blade durotar gadrin","orgnil soulscar gadrin"}},{q="What does Gadrin know about the loa Shadra?",a="Gadrin is a master of ancient troll theology. When the Forsaken Apothecary Lydon seeks a potent venom used by the Hinterlands Witherbark trolls, Gadrin identifies it as a gift from Shadra the spider loa, directing adventurers to Zul'Farrak to obtain the tablet needed to prepare a summoning ritual.",al={"shadra spider loa gadrin","gadrin spider god"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Master Gadrin is a living connection to your ancestral home and the traditions of Sen'jin. He has shaped your tribe's spiritual leadership for generations and feels a fatherly grief over the tragedy of the Echo Isles.",["class:Priest"]="As the elder who instructed Darkspear priests in communing with the spirits and the loa, Gadrin embodies the shadow and faith traditions of the jungle trolls.",["class:Mage"]="Gadrin broke ground by tutoring Darkspear trolls in the arcane arts after the Third War, proving that troll magic could expand far beyond raw ritual mojo.",["faction:Horde"]="Master Gadrin is one of Thrall's trusted local advisors, keeping watchful eyes on coastal Durotar and warning Razor Hill when dark cults threaten the fledgling nation of Durotar."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","gadrin","master gadrin","minshina","sen'jin village","vol'jin","witch doctor","zalazane"},rel={"npc:vol-jin","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:826","subzone:echo-isles","quest:808","npc:orgnil-soulscar","topic:darkspear-tribe","zone:durotar"},src={"Master Gadrin"}}
E["npc:master-vornal"] = {t="npc",n="Master Vornal",z="durotar",s="Master Vornal is an elderly Darkspear jungle troll who resides in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar. Despite his advancing years and extensive knowledge of alchemical concoctions, he stubbornly refuses to take on any apprentices.",h="Master Vornal is an elderly Darkspear jungle troll who resides in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of...",sec={{t="The Stubborn Brewer of Sen'jin",b="Master Vornal is a fixture of Sen'jin Village, known for brewing potent draughts and spirits for his fellow Darkspear trolls. Though age is visibly catching up with him, Vornal remains intensely independent and stubbornly refuses to train any apprentices, preferring to mix his remedies and volatile mixtures entirely by his own hand.",sp=0},{t="A Solvent Spirit",b="Vornal occasionally tasks young adventurers with gathering harsh or peculiar ingredients from the surrounding lands, such as potent materials needed for solvents and mixtures. While he is willing to reward those who assist him, he keeps his precise methods and recipes guarded, treating his craft as a solitary pursuit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Vornal?",a="Master Vornal is an elderly Darkspear jungle troll residing in Sen'jin Village. He brews potent spirits and remedies for the tribe but insists on working without an apprentice.",al={"master vornal","vornal","sen'jin master vornal","who is vornal"}},{q="Where can I find Master Vornal?",a="He can be found standing among the huts in Sen'jin Village, situated along the southern coast of Durotar just north of the Echo Isles.",al={"vornal location","where is master vornal","find master vornal"}},{q="Why does Master Vornal refuse to take apprentices?",a="Vornal is famously stubborn. Despite his advanced age and the community's need for his craft, he prefers to handle his concoctions alone rather than pass his secrets down to headstrong novices.",al={"vornal apprentice","why no apprentice","vornal students"}},{q="What tasks does he offer adventurers?",a="Vornal sends wanderers to gather raw components across the region for his solvent mixtures, relying on travelers for materials while keeping the brewing process strictly to himself.",al={"master vornal quest","a solvent spirit","vornal quest"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Master Vornal represents the stubborn, elder craftspeople who helped establish Sen'jin Village after the tribe fled their island home.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Those skilled with raw flora will recognize Vornal's keen eye for rare catalysts and harsh natural reagents required for his solvents."},kw={"a solvent spirit","darkspear","durotar","master vornal","sen'jin village","troll","vornal"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:818","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Master Vornal"}}
E["npc:misha-tor-kren"] = {t="npc",n="Misha Tor'kren",z="durotar",s="Misha Tor'kren is an orc mother dwelling at the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, southeast of Thunder Ridge. Plagued by anxiety over her missing son Kron, she appeals to passing travelers for aid in discovering his fate.",h="Misha Tor'kren is an orc mother dwelling at the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, southeast of Thunder Ridge.",sec={{t="A Mother's Vigil",b="Tucked away near the edge of Thunder Ridge, Misha Tor'kren works her isolated farmstead while enduring a parent's worst fear. Her son Kron ventured west toward the Southfury River to hunt crocolisks and prove his mettle, but he never returned. With Durotar's frontier dangers stretching orcish watchtowers thin, Misha is left alone to hope for word of his whereabouts, desperate for anyone willing to search the riverbanks for signs of her boy.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Token",b="The Southfury River is unforgiving to young hunters. Those who comb the muddy banks inevitably discover that Kron fell victim to the river's vicious crocolisks. Returning his salvaged amulet is the only closure Misha can receive—a bitter reminder of the brutal trials young orcs face to establish their strength in Kalimdor's harsh wilderness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Misha Tor'kren?",a="Misha Tor'kren is an orc settler residing at the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, situated just southeast of Thunder Ridge.",al={"misha torkren","who is misha","torkren farm owner"}},{q="Where did her son Kron go?",a="Kron traveled west toward the Southfury River to hunt river crocolisks, eager to prove himself as an able hunter, but failed to return home.",al={"where is kron","what happened to kron","misha son"}},{q="What happens when you look for Kron?",a="A search of the Southfury River reveals that Kron did not survive his hunt. Slain by the beasts of the river, only his amulet remains to be recovered and brought back to his mother.",al={"is kron dead","find kron","lost but not forgotten"},sp=1},{q="Is she related to Rexxar's bear Misha?",a="No. While they share the name Misha, she is an orc farmer living in Durotar, entirely distinct from Rexxar's loyal bear companion.",al={"misha bear","rexxar bear misha","is she the bear"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Kron's reckless desire to prove his warrior prowess against Durotar's wildlife serves as a somber reminder of the steep cost of youthful pride.",["class:Hunter"]="The fate of Misha's son shows the danger of underestimating river predators before a hunter has truly mastered the wild."},kw={"crocolisk","kron","lost but not forgotten","misha","misha tor'kren","southfury river","thunder ridge","tor'kren farm"},rel={"quest:816","subzone:tor-kren-farm","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:durotar","npc:misha"},src={"Misha Tor'kren"}}
E["npc:orgnil-soulscar"] = {t="npc",n="Orgnil Soulscar",z="durotar",s="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc investigator stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar. He serves as an informal officer of the peace, coordinating defense and intelligence against internal threats to the fledgling nation. His primary concern is the shadow cast by the Burning Blade cult within Durotar's canyons.",h="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc investigator stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar.",sec={{t="Watcher of Razor Hill",b="Positioned at Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar takes on the grim responsibility of tracking subversion and insidious threats across Durotar. While grunt patrols look outward toward Alliance footholds and centaur raiding parties, Orgnil focuses on rot brewing from within. He collects reports from scouts across the region, piecing together evidence of ritual corruption and illicit gatherings.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Shadow Council's Remnants",b="Orgnil's chief focus is the clandestine resurgence of the Burning Blade cult, whose warlocks hide in caves such as Skull Rock. Knowing the devastation fel magic brought upon the orcish people in past generations, Orgnil refuses to let demon worship gain another foothold near Orgrimmar. He directs trusted recruits to strike down cultists, gather ritual talismans, and consult with local hermits and shamans like Margoz to understand the dark magics at play.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Orgnil Soulscar?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc official based in Razor Hill who acts as an investigator and coordinator for Durotar's defense. He directs warriors and scouts against covert dangers threatening the newly settled orc lands.",al={"who is orgnil","orgnil soulscar lore","razor hill quest giver"}},{q="What threat is Orgnil most worried about?",a="Orgnil is dedicated to rooting out the Burning Blade cult. He sees their presence in Durotar's hidden caverns and their corruptive fel magic as a lethal threat to the fresh start Thrall envisions for the Horde.",al={"what does orgnil want","orgnil enemies","who does orgnil fight"}},{q="Why does Orgnil send travelers to Margoz?",a="Margoz is a knowledgeable hermit living north of Razor Hill who understands the dark signs and rituals of the Burning Blade. Orgnil directs scouts to Margoz to decipher the cult's movements and unravel the brewing magical corruption.",al={"why margoz","orgnil and margoz","who is margoz to orgnil"}},{q="Where can Orgnil Soulscar be found?",a="Orgnil is stationed outdoors in the settlement of Razor Hill, near the central crossroads of Durotar.",al={"orgnil location","where is orgnil","find orgnil soulscar"}},{q="What is the Burning Blade in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade is a sinister cult beholden to demonic masters and the Shadow Council. They hide in ravines like Skull Rock and the Dustwind Cave, attempting to poison Durotar's wildlife and seduce young orcs back to demonic subservience.",al={"burning blade durotar","burning blade cult","who are burning blade"}},{q="Does Orgnil work directly for Thrall?",a="Orgnil operates as part of the regional defense apparatus centered in Razor Hill, carrying out the Warchief's mandate to safeguard Durotar from sedition and demonic influence.",al={"orgnil thrall","is orgnil warchief guard"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, Orgnil represents the frontline against the demonic taint that once enslaved the clans, reminding new recruits of the vigilance required to keep their new homeland pure.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks must tread carefully around Orgnil, as his entire focus is hunting down and eradicating unchecked demonic corruption within Durotar's borders.",["faction:Horde"]="Orgnil ensures that while the Horde looks outward to build a new nation, its heartland is not hollowed out by cultists from within."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","margoz","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","shadow council","skull rock"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:828","quest:823","quest:806"},src={"Orgnil Soulscar"}}
E["npc:ormak-grimshot"] = {t="npc",n="Ormak Grimshot",z="durotar",s="Ormak Grimshot is an experienced orc hunter trainer residing in the Hunter's Hall within Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. Accompanied by his loyal wolf, Grimfang, he instructs young hunters of the Horde in tracking, marksmanship, and bonding with wild beasts.",h="Ormak Grimshot is an experienced orc hunter trainer residing in the Hunter's Hall within Orgrimmar's Valley...",sec={{t="Master of the Hunt",b="Stationed within the Hunter's Hall in the Valley of Honor, Ormak Grimshot serves as a cornerstone of martial instruction for the Horde's trackers and marksmen. Alongside his companion wolf, Grimfang, Ormak imparts the foundational discipline needed to survive Kalimdor's harsh wilderness. For orc and troll hunters arriving from their trials in Durotar, he provides vital guidance on the sacred art of taming and commanding wild beasts, ensuring every hunter forms an enduring bond with their animal partner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ormak Grimshot?",a="Ormak Grimshot is a veteran orc hunter trainer stationed in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. He teaches new Horde hunters advanced skills in ranged combat and beast mastery.",al={"who is ormak","ormak grimshot lore","ormak hunter trainer"}},{q="Where can I find Ormak Grimshot?",a="Ormak is located inside the Hunter's Hall, nestled in the Valley of Honor in eastern Orgrimmar. He stands near his pet wolf, Grimfang.",al={"ormak location","where is grimshot","find ormak"}},{q="Who is the wolf beside him?",a="The wolf at his side is Grimfang, Ormak's loyal companion animal, illustrating the tight bond between a skilled hunter and their pet.",al={"ormak wolf","grimfang","ormak pet"}},{q="What role does he play for new hunters?",a="Ormak directs novice orc and troll hunters on how to train, feed, and manage their newly tamed beasts once they finish their basic trials in Durotar.",al={"hunter pet quest orgrimmar","taming quest ormak","training the beast ormak"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Ormak is an essential mentor for Horde hunters, guiding them through the responsibilities of taming and maintaining a loyal animal companion.",["race:Orc"]="Reflecting classic orcish survival skills, Ormak exemplifies how orcs work alongside wolves and native predators to defend Durotar."},kw={"beast training","grimfang","hunter trainer","hunter's hall","orgrimmar","ormak grimshot","valley of honor"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-honor","quest:6081","topic:horde","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Ormak Grimshot"}}
E["npc:rezlak"] = {t="npc",n="Rezlak",z="durotar",s="Rezlak is a goblin entrepreneur and member of the Tinkers' Union stationed along the dusty roads of Durotar south of Orgrimmar. He hires traveling adventurers to salvage his missing supplies and clear out the harpy nests disrupting regional communications.",h="Rezlak is a goblin entrepreneur and member of the Tinkers' Union stationed along the dusty roads of Durotar...",sec={{t="A Pragmatic Tinkers' Union Agent",b="Perched beside the canyon roads connecting Razor Hill to Orgrimmar, Rezlak represents the Tinkers' Union—a goblin syndicate focused on engineering, supply lines, and industrial pragmatism. Rezlak cares little for the factional tensions of Kalimdor so long as business runs smoothly. When the fierce Dustwind harpies raided his cargo caravans and disrupted local communication lines, Rezlak stayed put, preferring to contract out the dangerous work of extermination and recovery to any passerby willing to turn a profit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is an independent goblin merchant and engineer affiliated with the Tinkers' Union. Stationed along the main northern road through Durotar, he seeks willing mercenaries to secure his supply lines and reclaim lost gear from regional pests.",al={"rezlak lore","who is rezlak","rezlak durotar"}},{q="What is Rezlak doing in Durotar?",a="Rezlak works along the trade routes between the central plains and the canyon pass leading to Orgrimmar. His supply caravans were ambushed by the Dustwind harpies, leaving his cargo strewn across the arid canyons and his vital communication lines severed.",al={"why is rezlak in durotar","rezlak purpose","rezlak mission"}},{q="Which quests does Rezlak offer?",a="Rezlak offers two primary tasks: 'Winds in the Desert', which tasks adventurers with retrieving sacks of lost supplies scattered across the canyon floor, and 'Securing the Lines', which requires thinning out the aggressive Dustwind harpies nesting nearby.",al={"rezlak quests","what quests does rezlak give"}},{q="What is the Tinkers' Union?",a="The Tinkers' Union is an enterprising goblin trade organization that oversees mechanics, inventors, and logistical operations. Like many goblin cartels and guilds, its members prioritize profitable commerce and practical problem-solving above political loyalty.",al={"tinkers union","rezlak faction"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As a representative of the Tinkers' Union, Rezlak values mechanical efficiency, practical tools, and salvaged components above all else.",["faction:Horde"]="Though stationed right outside Orgrimmar, Rezlak represents the purely transactional relationship between neutral goblin guilds and the fledgling Horde."},kw={"durotar","dustwind harpies","rezlak","securing the lines","tinkers union","winds in the desert"},rel={"quest:834","quest:835","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:goblin","topic:horde"},src={"Rezlak"}}
E["npc:rhinag"] = {t="npc",n="Rhinag",z="durotar",s="Rhinag is an afflicted jungle troll seeking shelter within a modest homestead at Rocktusk Farm in Durotar. Paralyzed by the harsh venom of the region's scorpions, he relies entirely on passing travelers to secure him a timely remedy.",h="Rhinag is an afflicted jungle troll seeking shelter within a modest homestead at Rocktusk Farm in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Venomous Peril",b="While traversing the arid terrain of Durotar, Rhinag fell victim to the vicious sting of a local Venomtail Scorpid. Overwhelmed by the potent poison, he managed to drag himself into the dilapidated shelter at Rocktusk Farm. Incapacitated and isolated, his survival hinges on anyone who happens by with the resolve to procure a venomtail antidote before the toxins take their final toll.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhinag?",a="Rhinag is a jungle troll traveler who found himself stranded and paralyzed at Durotar's Rocktusk Farm after suffering a venomous sting from a native scorpion.",al={"who is rhinag","rhinag lore","troll at rocktusk"}},{q="Where can Rhinag be found?",a="He is resting inside the small building at Rocktusk Farm, situated in central Durotar south of Razor Hill.",al={"rhinag location","where is rhinag","rocktusk farm troll"}},{q="What happened to him?",a="While traversing the plains of Durotar, Rhinag was stung by a dangerous Venomtail Scorpid. The virulent toxin left him incapacitated, requiring an antidote to neutralize the poison before it proves fatal.",al={"why is rhinag sick","what poisoned rhinag","need for a cure backstory"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Finding a kinsman struck down by native wildlife in the arid wastes of Durotar is a stark reminder of the trials the Darkspear tribe faces in carving out a home alongside the Horde."},kw={"antidote","durotar","need for a cure","rhinag","rocktusk farm","venomtail scorpid"},rel={"quest:812","subzone:rocktusk-farm","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Rhinag"}}
E["npc:thotar"] = {t="npc",n="Thotar",z="durotar",s="Thotar is a seasoned orc hunter trainer stationed in the settlement of Razor Hill in Durotar. He guides aspiring Horde scouts and marksmen in the ancient traditions of tracking, archery, and bonding with wild beasts. For young orcs and trolls taking their first steps outside the Valley of Trials, he provides the foundational rites needed to master Kalimdor's rugged fauna.",h="Thotar is a seasoned orc hunter trainer stationed in the settlement of Razor Hill in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Mentor in Razor Hill",b="Perched within the fortified hub of Razor Hill, Thotar serves as a veteran instructor for marksmen of the Horde. While new recruits learn the very basics in the Valley of Trials, it falls to Thotar to guide hunters as they face the harsher predatory wilderness of Durotar. Drawing upon traditions passed down through countless generations of orcs, he teaches not only marksmanship, but the deeper respect required to live alongside and direct Kalimdor's deadliest creatures.",sp=0},{t="Taming the Wilds",b="Thotar plays a crucial role in introducing young hunters to the ancient art of beast taming. Through a sequence of trials, he sends novices into the arid canyons to pacify and commune with native beasts, such as venomous scorpid, savage crocolisks, and cunning boars. By guiding these young scouts through the sacred rites of taming, Thotar ensures the Horde's trackers build a loyal bond with nature rather than merely attempting to dominate it by force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thotar?",a="Thotar is a veteran orc hunter trainer stationed in Razor Hill in Durotar. He educates young hunters in traditional wilderness lore, marksmanship, and animal taming.",al={"who is thotar","thotar lore","what does thotar do"}},{q="Where can Thotar be found?",a="He is located in the Horde settlement of Razor Hill, situated in central Durotar just north of the Valley of Trials.",al={"thotar location","where is thotar","find thotar"}},{q="What traditions does Thotar teach?",a="Thotar teaches the ancient survival and tracking traditions passed down through generations of orcs. He emphasizes weapon mastery, wilderness survival, and learning to bond with animal companions through patience and ritual.",al={"what does thotar teach","hunter traditions","thotar training"}},{q="Does Thotar only train orcs?",a="While he is an orc steeped in his people's ways, Thotar instructs any hunter aligned with the Horde who arrives in Razor Hill, regularly mentoring Darkspear trolls and wandering tauren passing through Durotar.",al={"can trolls train with thotar","thotar tauren","who does thotar train"}},{q="What tasks does Thotar give to young hunters?",a="Thotar directs novice hunters on the rites of 'Taming the Beast,' tasking them with tracking down native Durotar wildlife—such as scorpids and crocolisks—and using a taming rod to earn their trust and obedience.",al={"thotar quests","taming the beast thotar","what does thotar send you to do"}},{q="Why is beast taming so important in his training?",a="For Horde hunters, a beast companion is a vital partner on the battlefield and in the wild. Thotar teaches that properly bonding with a beast ensures mutual survival, transforming raw predators into loyal defenders of the Horde.",al={"why tame beasts","hunter pet lore","purpose of beast taming"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Thotar represents a key milestone for young Horde hunters, teaching the vital rites of beast taming and wilderness mastery once novices step out of the starter valleys.",["race:Orc"]="Thotar preserves and passes down traditional orcish hunting customs, ensuring that life on Kalimdor remains anchored in deep ancestral respect for tracking and beast companionship.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear hunters setting out from Sen'jin Village, Thotar offers vital instruction that blends ancestral Horde survival skills with the predatory challenges of Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="As a frontline trainer in Razor Hill, Thotar ensures that scouts and marksmen patrolling Durotar's borders are disciplined, sharp-eyed, and well-bonded with combat beasts."},kw={"durotar","hunter","hunter trainer","kaplak","orc","razor hill","taming the beast","thotar"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:6061","quest:6081","quest:6065","npc:kaplak","topic:troll","topic:tauren"},src={"Thotar"}}
E["npc:ukor"] = {t="npc",n="Ukor",z="durotar",s="Ukor is an orc peon resting near the eastern path outside the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Eager to help his people, he carried supplies all the way from Razor Hill, only to find the training grounds already had plenty of provisions.",h="Ukor is an orc peon resting near the eastern path outside the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Peon's Errand",b="While many orc peons spend their lives under the watchful eye of harsh taskmasters cutting lumber or hauling rocks, Ukor attempted to perform a service of his own initiative. Tasked or inspired to bring food from Razor Hill to the recruits training in the Valley of Trials, he made the dangerous trek across Durotar's red plains past prowling scorpid and boars. Upon arrival, he discovered the Valley was already well-stocked and had no need for his bundle. Exhausted and somewhat disheartened by the roadside, he relies on passing young adventurers to return the unused provisions back north to Innkeeper Grosk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ukor?",a="Ukor is an earnest orc peon stationed along the road leading east out of the Valley of Trials in southern Durotar.",al={"ukor lore","who is ukor","what does ukor do"}},{q="Why is Ukor standing by the road with a sack of food?",a="Ukor carried a heavy bundle of rations down from Razor Hill to feed the young warriors training in the Valley of Trials. When he arrived, he found they had no shortage of provisions, leaving him stranded with unneeded food.",al={"why is ukor here","ukor quest reason","ukor food bundle"}},{q="What does Ukor ask passing travelers to do?",a="Too weary to haul the heavy sack all the way back up the trail himself, Ukor asks fledgling adventurers heading north toward Razor Hill to return the bundle to Innkeeper Grosk.",al={"ukor task","what does ukor want","peons burden quest"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orc peons bear the hard physical labor that builds the new Horde, and Ukor shows that even humble laborers possess a strong desire to support the warriors of Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="For new recruits emerging from their trials, aiding Ukor marks one of the first opportunities to support everyday Horde logistics between settlements."},kw={"a peon's burden","durotar","grosk","peon","razor hill","ukor","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:2161","npc:innkeeper-grosk","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar"},src={"Ukor"}}
E["npc:vol-jin"] = {t="npc",n="Vol'jin",z="durotar",s="Vol'jin is the chieftain of the Darkspear trolls and a master shadow hunter. Residing in Grommash Hold alongside Warchief Thrall, he acts as a trusted advisor to the Horde while working to secure his displaced people a permanent home in Durotar.",h="Vol'jin is the chieftain of the Darkspear trolls and a master shadow hunter.",sec={{t="Chieftain of the Darkspear",b="Vol'jin took up leadership of the Darkspear tribe following the tragic death of his father, Sen'jin, on their ancestral island home. When sea witch-worshipping murlocs and human forces nearly destroyed the isolated tribe, Thrall's orcs intervened, forging a deep bond between the two peoples. After evacuating the ruins of their islands, Vol'jin pledged his trolls to the New Horde and brought them across the Great Sea to Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Council in the Valley of Strength",b="Though the Darkspear established settlements in Durotar, internal betrayals—namely the treachery of Zalazane on the Echo Isles—forced many refugees to the mainland at Sen'jin Village. Vol'jin spends much of his time inside Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar, lending his sharp strategic counsel and shadow hunter prowess directly to Thrall. From the heart of the orcish capital, he watches over the fledgling Horde while striving to reclaim his people's rightful lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vol'jin?",a="Vol'jin is the leader and chieftain of the Darkspear troll tribe. He is a skilled shadow hunter who represents his people within the Horde leadership, serving as one of Warchief Thrall's closest counselors in Orgrimmar.",al={"who is the troll leader","voljin lore","darkspear leader"}},{q="Where does Vol'jin live?",a="Vol'jin is located in Grommash Hold, in the Valley of Wisdom within Orgrimmar, standing right beside Warchief Thrall.",al={"where is voljin","voljin location","find voljin"}},{q="Why did the Darkspear join the Horde?",a="During the Third War, Thrall's fleet washed ashore on the Darkspear Islands. The orcs allied with the trolls against hostile humans and a fanatical murloc army. When Sen'jin fell in battle, Vol'jin honored his father's vision by pledging his tribe to Thrall and accompanying the orcs to Kalimdor.",al={"why are trolls horde","darkspear horde history","thrall and voljin"}},{q="Why aren't the Darkspear living on their own islands?",a="After settling off the coast of Durotar on the Echo Isles, Vol'jin's childhood friend and witch doctor Zalazane was driven mad by dark magic. Zalazane enslaved his fellow tribesmen, forcing Vol'jin and the surviving Darkspear to flee to the mainland at Sen'jin Village.",al={"what happened to echo isles","why are trolls in senjin village","zalazane betrayal"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Vol'jin is your chieftain, guiding the Darkspear through displacement and hardship with spiritual wisdom and tactical resolve.",["faction:Horde"]="Alongside Thrall, Vol'jin serves as a pillar of the New Horde, offering cunning advice and the fierce loyalty of the jungle trolls."},kw={"darkspear","grommash hold","orgrimmar","sen'jin","shadow hunter","thrall","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:troll","zone:orgrimmar","quest:826","npc:master-gadrin","topic:horde","zone:durotar"},src={"Vol'jin"}}
E["npc:zjolnir"] = {t="npc",n="Zjolnir",z="durotar",s="Zjolnir is a Darkspear troll mount breeder stationed in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar. He provides trained riding raptors to the Darkspear and trustworthy champions of the Horde. For troll riders, his stable of vicious, loyal beasts is a point of deep cultural pride.",h="Zjolnir is a Darkspear troll mount breeder stationed in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar.",sec={{t="Breeder of the Darkspear Raptors",b="Situated near the pens of Sen'jin Village, Zjolnir tends to the fierce raptors favored as mounts by the Darkspear trolls. Raptors are temperamental and predatory by nature, requiring an expert hand to raise and saddle for war. Zjolnir freely provides these prized whistled mounts to fellow trolls who have learned the necessary riding arts. Outsiders belonging to the wider Horde must first earn the exalted trust of the Darkspear tribe before Zjolnir will consider trusting them with one of his pack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Zjolnir?",a="Zjolnir is located in Sen'jin Village, a coastal Darkspear settlement found in the southern reaches of Durotar, standing beside the village's raptor pens.",al={"zjolnir location","where is zjolnir","raptor vendor location"}},{q="What does Zjolnir sell?",a="Zjolnir sells whistle-summoned raptors, the signature racial mounts of the Darkspear trolls. His stock includes various breeds and colors suited for both newly trained riders and experienced veterans.",al={"zjolnir vendor","what does he sell","troll mount vendor"}},{q="Can non-trolls buy raptors from him?",a="Yes, but non-trolls must earn exalted standing with the Darkspear Trolls before Zjolnir will sell to them. Trolls can purchase from him immediately once they possess the required riding skill.",al={"can orcs buy raptors","who can buy mounts from zjolnir","horde raptor mount"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Zjolnir provides the swift, clawed beasts central to their heritage and fighting traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="Any Horde warrior who proves their steadfast devotion to the Darkspear tribe can earn the privilege of riding one of Zjolnir's raptors into battle."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","mount","raptor","sen'jin village","troll mount","zjolnir"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:7664","quest:7665"},src={"Zjolnir"}}
E["npc:zureetha-fargaze"] = {t="npc",n="Zureetha Fargaze",z="durotar",s="Zureetha Fargaze is an orc mentor stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar alongside Foreman Thazz'ril. Vigilant against corruption, she directs young Horde recruits to investigate and root out the dark influence of the Burning Blade cult hiding within the valley.",h="Zureetha Fargaze is an orc mentor stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar alongside Foreman Thazz'ril.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Valley",b="While Foreman Thazz'ril oversees the labor and discipline of young orcs and Darkspear trolls, Zureetha Fargaze keeps watch for subtler, more insidious threats. The Burning Blade cult has secretly infiltrated the Valley of Trials, corrupting lesser demons and gathering strength in the nearby cavern of Burning Blade Coven. Zureetha tasks untested adventurers with retrieving medallions from the cultists to confirm their presence and dismantle their early operations before directing seasoned recruits outward into Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zureetha Fargaze?",a="Zureetha Fargaze is an orc questgiver stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She stands near Foreman Thazz'ril and monitors the hidden threats creeping into the training grounds.",al={"zureetha fargaze lore","who is zureetha","fargaze valley of trials"}},{q="Why is she concerned about the Burning Blade?",a="The demonic Burning Blade cult has taken root inside a nearby cave, drawing foul familiars and corrupting the peaceful trial grounds. Zureetha seeks proof of their presence through their cultist medallions and sends recruits to thin their numbers.",al={"burning blade valley of trials","why does zureetha want medallions","burning blade cult durotar"}},{q="Where does she send recruits after their initial trials?",a="Once young orcs and trolls prove their competence against the local threats, Zureetha dispatches them southeast across the ridge to Sen'jin Village to aid the Darkspear tribe.",al={"where do i go after zureetha","zureetha next quest","report to sen'jin"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs taking their first steps into the world, Zureetha represents the watchful vigilance required to keep the demonic taint of the past from polluting their new homeland.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks in the Valley of Trials cross paths with Zureetha's tasks early on, dealing with the loose, corrupt vile familiars tied to the Burning Blade's dark summonings."},kw={"burning blade","burning blade medallion","durotar","foreman thazz'ril","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","subzone:sen-jin-village"},src={"Zureetha Fargaze"}}
E["quest:1525"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="durotar",s="This trial marks the critical preparation in a shaman's communion with fire, tasking the initiate with gathering the volatile ingredients needed to brew a Fire Sapta. Telf Joolam requires components saturated with heat and magical power: tar from Razormane geomancers and a pouch of dark reagents from Burning Blade cultists hiding in Durotar.",h="This trial marks the critical preparation in a shaman's communion with fire, tasking the initiate with...",sec={{t="Brewing the Fire Sapta",b="To perceive and speak to the spirits of fire, a shaman cannot rely on mortal vision alone. Just as earth required its own draught, opening the senses to the Eternal Flame demands a specialized Fire Sapta. The potion requires reagents innately bound to heat and flame. The hermit Telf Joolam sends initiates across Durotar and into the eastern Barrens to harvest these specific elements from those who wield primal heat and corrupting sorcery.",sp=0},{t="Enemies and Elements",b="The required ingredients reveal how different factions tap into fire. The Razormane quilboar spellcasters of the eastern Barrens carry fire tar, a viscous, flammable byproduct of their earthy rituals. In contrast, the reagent pouch must be seized from the Burning Blade cultists lurking in Dustwind Cave, nestled in the ravines northeast of Razor Hill. Though the warlock cultists wield fire as an instrument of destruction and demonic chaos, the raw reagents in their pouches remain naturally resonant with the element itself.",sp=0},{t="The Nature of Flame",b="Upon brewing the sapta, Telf Joolam imparts an essential truth of the elements: fire is far more than mere destruction and ruin. While it burns and consumes, it is also the heart of warmth, light, and creation. True balance requires understanding that opposing forces give one another meaning, and that a wise shaman uses contrasting elemental powers in tandem rather than treating fire solely as a weapon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Fire Sapta?",a="A sapta is a ritual draught prepared by shamans using ingredients tied to a specific element. Drinking a Fire Sapta temporarily aligns the shaman's spirit and vision with the plane of fire, allowing them to perceive and speak with elemental fire spirits that are otherwise invisible to ordinary senses.",al={"what is fire sapta","fire sapta meaning","why drink sapta"}},{q="Where do I find the Fire Tar?",a="Fire tar is carried by Razormane quilboar spellcasters inhabiting the eastern plains of the Barrens, just across the Southfury River from Durotar. Geomancers, Seers, Mystics, and Thornweavers frequently carry pots of this thick, flammable concoction for their tribal rituals.",al={"fire tar location","who drops fire tar","fire tar quilboar"}},{q="Where is the Reagent Pouch found?",a="The reagent pouch is carried by Burning Blade cultists in Dustwind Cave. This cave is located above the ravines northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar, not to be confused with Skull Rock further to the north near the coast.",al={"reagent pouch location","which cave has reagent pouch","burning blade pouch"}},{q="Why does a shaman use items from warlocks?",a="Saptas require ingredients that are naturally saturated with the targeted element. Because Burning Blade cultists constantly invoke destructive demonic flames, their spell pouches are densely packed with potent reagents tied directly to fire, providing the exact catalyst Telf Joolam needs to craft the draught.",al={"why use burning blade reagents","warlock items for shaman","warlock fire"}},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is a solitary troll shaman who makes his camp atop the crags of Durotar, south of Razor Hill. He oversees the harsh trials of fire for Horde initiates, guiding them in mastering the dangerous balance between destruction and creation.",al={"telf joolam lore","who is telf joolam"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="Once Telf Joolam crafts the Fire Sapta from the gathered reagents, he sends you up to the fiery heights of the dormant peak nearby. There, you must drink the concoction to face the elemental spirit and earn your fire totem.",al={"next quest call of fire","after getting reagents","what to do with fire sapta"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This rite tests a young shaman's ability to balance opposing forces, demonstrating that flame is not merely fuel for wrath, but an instrument of vitality and light when guided by wisdom.",["faction:Horde"]="The trial sends Horde defenders to strike at two pressing threats right on their borders: encroaching Razormane quilboar in the Barrens and the insidious Burning Blade cultists burrowed within Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, dealing with the Burning Blade is a bitter reminder of the dark warlock magic that once corrupted their people, making reclaiming fire as a pure, natural element a vital act of cultural restoration."},kw={"burning blade","call of fire","dustwind cave","fire sapta","fire tar","razormane","reagent pouch","telf joolam"},rel={"npc:telf-joolam","subzone:dustwind-cave","subzone:razor-hill","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","quest:1524","quest:827"},m={start="Telf Joolam",level="12",faction="Horde",id=1525},src={"Call of Fire (3)"}}
E["quest:1526"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="durotar",s="This trial marks the critical moment in a shaman's attunement to fire atop the peaks of Durotar. Guided by the hermit Telf Joolam, the initiate must drink a potent fire sapta to perceive and confront a Minor Manifestation of Fire. Slaying the spirit yields a glowing ember, used to kindle the brazier at the Shrine of Eternal Flame and light the ceremonial torch.",h="This trial marks the critical moment in a shaman's attunement to fire atop the peaks of Durotar.",sec={{t="Eyes of the Flame",b="Fire spirits rarely linger in plain sight for the uninitiated. To commune with them, a shaman must alter their perception using a fire sapta, an elemental draught steeped from reagents gathered across the barrens and coast. Imbibing the draught opens the senses to the unseen, revealing minor spirits and manifestations dancing across the crags of the summit.",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Manifestation",b="Fire does not yield to passive devotion; it demands strength, decisiveness, and respect. Waiting atop the mountain is a Minor Manifestation of Fire. Aware of the shaman's piercing gaze once the sapta takes hold, the spirit waits for the challenge to begin. Initiates are taught to strike swiftly and without hesitation, as elemental fire feeds on lingering combat, swelling in ferocity and heat the longer the contest drags on.",sp=0},{t="The Brazier of the Dormant Flame",b="With the manifestation subdued, the shaman claims its lingering heat in the form of a glowing ember. Returning to the summit shrine, the ember is placed into the Brazier of the Dormant Flame. Despite being exposed to the harsh sun and winds of Durotar, the inscribed metal remains pristine and cool until the ember meets the bowl, bursting into a rhythmic, white-hot blaze that ignites the ritual torch.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="This trial tests an aspiring shaman's worthiness to command elemental fire. By confronting a manifestation and capturing its raw heat in a ritual torch, the initiate proves their strength and earns the right to fashion a Fire Totem.",al={"why do call of fire","fire totem quest meaning","call of fire trial"}},{q="Why do I need to drink the fire sapta?",a="Elemental spirits often dwell slightly beyond ordinary mortal sight. Drinking the fire sapta thins the veil, allowing the shaman to perceive and physically interact with the fire elementals gathered atop the mountain.",al={"what does fire sapta do","why sapta","cant see fire elemental"}},{q="Where is the Minor Manifestation of Fire found?",a="The manifestation resides at the absolute peak of the mountain ridge above Telf Joolam's perch in Durotar, near the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",al={"manifestation location","where is the fire elemental","where do i go"}},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is an eccentric shaman hermit living high on a rocky ridge in Durotar. He guides young Horde initiates through the dangerous and temperamental rites required to understand fire.",al={"telf joolam role","telf joolam lore","who is the hermit"}},{q="Why does the manifestation grow stronger during the fight?",a="Fire naturally builds, spreads, and feeds on energy over time. Shamans are cautioned to strike decisively because prolonged hesitation allows the spirit to gather strength and burn ever hotter.",al={"why is the fire elemental so strong","manifestation scaling","swift strike fire"}},{q="What happens after the brazier is lit?",a="Lighting the brazier kindles the ceremonial torch. The initiate carries this sacred flame back down the mountain to complete the creation of their Fire Totem.",al={"what after dormant flame","next quest call of fire","where to take lit torch"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Unlike the solid, unyielding earth, fire is volatile and destructive. This trial teaches that fire will consume an indecisive caller, demanding unwavering focus and authority to master.",["faction:Horde"]="Orc and troll shamans make the pilgrimage up the red crags of Durotar to prove their communion with the fiery spirits of the land."},kw={"brazier of the dormant flame","call of fire","durotar","fire sapta","fire totem","minor manifestation of fire","shaman trial","shrine of eternal flame","telf joolam"},rel={"npc:telf-joolam","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Telf Joolam",["end"]="Brazier of the Dormant Flame",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1526},src={"Call of Fire (4)"}}
E["quest:1842"] = {t="quest",n="Satyr Hooves",z="durotar",s="Satyr Hooves is a quest given by the troll craftsman Ula'elek in Sen'jin Village. In pursuit of forging a pair of empowered brutal gauntlets, warriors must journey north into Ashenvale to hunt satyrs and harvest their magically bloated, uncloven hooves.",h="Satyr Hooves is a quest given by the troll craftsman Ula'elek in Sen'jin Village.",sec={{t="Harnessing Corrupted Essence",b="To forge armor capable of rivaling the most brutal forces on Kalimdor, the Darkspear craftsman Ula'elek looks beyond mundane iron and leather. He directs aspiring warriors north to the ancient woods of Ashenvale, where lingering demonic corruption festers within the local satyr covens.",sp=0},{t="The Bloat of Ashenvale's Magic",b="According to Ula'elek, the satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale sustain themselves by leeching the forest's latent purity and twisting it into foul power. Those demons that have gorged themselves the deepest on this borrowed life manifest abnormal, swollen hooves that have lost their natural cloven split. Ula'elek intends to drain this concentrated magical energy and weave it directly into the gauntlets he crafts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ula'elek need satyr hooves?",a="Ula'elek requires the hooves to empower the brutal gauntlets he is crafting. He intends to siphon the concentrated forest magic that the satyrs have drained and corrupted into their swollen feet.",al={"why satyr hooves","hoof purpose","what are the hooves for"}},{q="Where are the satyrs found?",a="They inhabit northeastern Ashenvale, where they roost among corrupted ancient ruins and leech off the residual magical energy of the deep forest.",al={"where are satyrs","satyr location","where to find satyr hooves"}},{q="What makes an uncloven hoof special?",a="The lack of a cloven split indicates that a satyr has engorged itself on excessive amounts of Ashenvale's pure magic, swelling its extremities with stolen power.",al={"uncloven hoof lore","why uncloven","swollen hooves"}},{q="Who is Ula'elek?",a="Ula'elek is a skilled Darkspear troll armor craftsman residing in Sen'jin Village in southern Durotar, known for assisting warriors with crafting trial gear.",al={"who is ulaelek","quest giver","troll in senjin"}},{q="What armor is Ula'elek forging?",a="He is preparing to craft a pair of Brutal Gauntlets, heavy protective handwear imbued with stolen magical potency for rising Horde warriors.",al={"what are brutal gauntlets","gauntlet quest","reward armor"}},{q="Do the satyrs serve the Burning Legion here?",a="Yes. Satyrs are ancient night elves transformed by demonic pacts, and the lingering covens in Kalimdor's woodlands continue to practice fel corruption in service to demonic powers.",al={"satyr allegiance","are satyrs legion"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="This task is part of a warrior's rite of progression, testing their martial resilience against cunning demonic ambushers to earn personalized armor.",["faction:Horde"]="Undertaking this hunt pushes Horde warriors out of Durotar's arid plains and deep into contested night elf territory in Ashenvale.",["race:Troll"]="Ula'elek's methods demonstrate the pragmatic nature of Darkspear craftsmanship, siphoning raw essence from fallen magical foes rather than relying purely on conventional smithing."},kw={"ashenvale","brutal gauntlets","durotar","hooves","satyr","sen'jin village","ula'elek","uncloven"},rel={"npc:ula-elek","quest:1843","quest:1839","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:ashenvale","zone:durotar","topic:satyr"},m={start="Ula'elek",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1842},src={"Satyr Hooves"}}
E["quest:1843"] = {t="quest",n="Brutal Gauntlets",z="durotar",s="Brutal Gauntlets is the culmination of an artisan's craft for seasoned Horde warriors. After gathering rare components across distant lands, the craftsman Ula'elek fashions a formidable pair of handguards designed to bring honor to both the maker and the bearer.",h="Brutal Gauntlets is the culmination of an artisan's craft for seasoned Horde warriors.",sec={{t="A Craftsman's Masterpiece",b="Forging armor fit for a seasoned frontline warrior is more than simple metalworking—it is a spiritual undertaking for Horde artisans. Ula'elek, a craftsman residing in Durotar, pours his lineage and skill into shaping these brutal gauntlets. By employing hardened trophies harvested from dangerous adversaries, he constructs armor tailored to withstand ferocious blows while enhancing the wearer's offensive might.",sp=0},{t="Ancestral Honor",b="In orcish and troll traditions, fine arms and armor carry the prestige of the forge and the spirit of the maker into battle. When Ula'elek presents the finished gauntlets to a warrior, he entrusts them with the legacy of his ancestors. A champion who wears them into combat is expected to display courage, martial discipline, and strength worthy of the craftsmanship.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ula'elek?",a="Ula'elek is a craftsman based in Durotar who aids Horde warriors in securing tailored, high-grade armor. He demands exotic materials to ensure that his smithing honors both his trade and his ancestral traditions.",al={"ulaelek","who gives brutal gauntlets","quest giver"}},{q="Why were satyr hooves needed for these gauntlets?",a="The satyrs' swollen, uncloven hooves hold the power they leeched from Ashenvale's magic. Ula'elek draws that power out of the hooves and harnesses it into his crafting, so the gauntlets hold great magic.",al={"why satyr hooves","satyr parts","materials used"}},{q="What does wearing the gauntlets signify to Ula'elek?",a="To Ula'elek, crafting these gauntlets represents his pinnacle work. Entrusting them to a worthy warrior brings deep honor to his craft and his ancestors, linking his labor directly to the Horde's martial victories.",al={"honor ancestors","ula'elek honor"}},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="The forging concludes in Durotar, the arid heartland of the orcs and Darkspear trolls, where Ula'elek inspects the recovered materials and presents the completed armor.",al={"location","where is brutal gauntlets turned in"}},{q="Is this trial intended for all adventurers?",a="This path is forged specifically for frontline warriors who have proven their stamina and martial dedication, marking their ascent into more seasoned combat roles within the Horde.",al={"is this warrior only","class requirement"}},{q="What comes after receiving the gauntlets?",a="The delivery of the gauntlets marks the completion of this specific crafting trial, leaving the warrior fully equipped to face greater threats across Azeroth's war-torn battlefields.",al={"next quest","brutal gauntlets follow up"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="These gauntlets represent a warrior's transition into disciplined martial leadership, serving as a trusted piece of protective kit forged specifically for heavy melee engagements.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde craftsmanship relies on enduring tradition and martial pride, ensuring champions carry the spiritual weight and honor of their craftspeople into battle."},kw={"armor forging","brutal gauntlets","durotar","horde","satyr hooves","ula'elek","warrior armor"},rel={"quest:1842","npc:ula-elek","zone:durotar"},m={start="Ula'elek",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1843},src={"Brutal Gauntlets (quest)"}}
E["quest:2161"] = {t="quest",n="A Peon's Burden",z="durotar",s="A Peon's Burden is an introductory delivery task given by Ukor, an anxious orc laborer stranded along the trail outside the Valley of Trials. After attempting to deliver provisions to new recruits who turned out not to need them, Ukor entrusts travelers with returning the heavy load safely to Razor Hill.",h="A Peon's Burden is an introductory delivery task given by Ukor, an anxious orc laborer stranded along the...",sec={{t="A Misplaced Delivery",b="Ukor is an earnest peon who set out from Razor Hill with good intentions, hauling a heavy pack of provisions toward the Valley of Trials. Believing the fresh recruits training in the red canyon were in dire need of rations, he braved the road only to be turned away. The taskmasters overseeing the trials deliberately keep supplies lean—as Innkeeper Grosk later notes, surviving on meager sustenance is seen as a way to forge discipline and endurance in young Horde warriors.",sp=0},{t="Perils of the Red Waste",b="Though he managed to make it to the pass, Ukor finds himself terrified of retracing his steps across the sun-baked soil of Durotar. The crags along the trail teem with aggressive scorpids, venomous spiders, and prowling boars. Lacking weapons, armor, or the fighting spirit expected of orcish grunts, the frightened laborer waits along the path, pleading for any passing adventurer departing the proving grounds to shoulder his burden and return it to the inn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ukor?",a="Ukor is an orc peon stationed along the road leading out of the Valley of Trials. Well-meaning but timid, he ventured out to deliver provisions from Razor Hill before realizing he was too terrified of local wildlife to make the return journey on his own.",al={"ukor","who is the peon on the road","peon near valley of trials"}},{q="Why didn't the trainers in the Valley of Trials want the food?",a="The overseers in the Valley of Trials believe in rigorous discipline for fledgling recruits. As Innkeeper Grosk humorously points out, the instructors prefer to keep the trainees hungry to test their mettle and build their spirit, rendering Ukor's charitable shipment unwelcome.",al={"why refuse food","why did ukor carry food","innkeeper grosk starvation"}},{q="Where does this delivery need to go?",a="The burden must be carried north along Durotar's main thoroughfare to Razor Hill, where it is handed over to Innkeeper Grosk inside the settlement's tavern.",al={"where is razor hill","who do i give the food to","where to deliver ukor's burden"}},{q="What makes the journey dangerous for a peon?",a="Durotar's rocky wastes are filled with territorial scorpids, venomous crawler spiders, and wild boars. While seasoned recruits can handle such vermin, an unarmored and untrained laborer like Ukor stands little chance if set upon.",al={"why is ukor scared","durotar road dangers"}},{q="What is the role of peons in the Horde?",a="Peons occupy the lowest rung of orcish society, handling menial labor such as hauling supplies, chopping timber, and erecting fortifications. While grunts and champions receive praise and glory, peons are often overlooked despite keeping settlements fed and maintained.",al={"orc peons lore","peon status","what are peons"}},{q="Who is Innkeeper Grosk?",a="Innkeeper Grosk runs the inn in Razor Hill. He manages the town's lodgings and supplies, offering food, drink, and hearth to traveling warriors and reminding recruits that resting is vital before taking on the wider world.",al={"innkeeper grosk","grosk razor hill","razor hill innkeeper"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orcish culture prizes physical might and courage, leaving peons like Ukor at the very bottom of the social hierarchy; taking on his errand shows how even humble labor keeps the fledgling nation of Durotar functioning.",["faction:Horde"]="This trek serves as a transition out of the proving grounds, introducing travelers to Razor Hill, the central hub for Horde defense and logistics in southern Durotar."},kw={"durotar","food","innkeeper grosk","peon","razor hill","supplies","ukor","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:ukor","npc:innkeeper-grosk","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Ukor",["end"]="Innkeeper Grosk",level="5",faction="Horde",id=2161},src={"A Peon's Burden"}}
E["quest:5843"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome!",z="durotar",s="This errand directs arriving Horde adventurers carrying a distinctive voucher to seek out Magga in Razor Hill. In exchange for the token, she offers a rare traveling companion to walk alongside them on their travels across Kalimdor and beyond.",h="This errand directs arriving Horde adventurers carrying a distinctive voucher to seek out Magga in Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Special Delivery",b="Newly arrived travelers stepping into Durotar with a gift voucher are pointed directly toward the central settlement of Razor Hill. Rather than sending recruits into battle against quillboars or centaur, this message directs them straight into the settlement to meet Magga, an orc eager to honor extraordinary commendations.",sp=0},{t="A Companion on the Road",b="Magga accepts the voucher with high praise, recognizing the bearer as a noteworthy traveler embarking on a long journey. In exchange, she provides a small creature to serve as a constant companion throughout the perilous trials awaiting Horde champions in the untamed wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this voucher for?",a="The voucher marks an adventurer deemed exceptional upon their arrival. Delivering it to Magga in Razor Hill allows you to choose a small creature to accompany you on your travels across Azeroth.",al={"razor hill gift voucher","what is voucher","why do i have voucher"}},{q="Who is Magga?",a="Magga is an orc located in Razor Hill in central Durotar. She welcomes travelers and honors special arrival vouchers.",al={"who is magga","where is magga"}},{q="Where do I turn this in?",a="The voucher is brought to Razor Hill, the major Horde hub directly north of the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Magga waits inside the inn.",al={"where turn in","where is turn in welcome"}},{q="Do Alliance players have an equivalent?",a="Yes, Alliance adventurers receive a similar voucher upon setting out, directing them to contacts in their own settlements, such as Goldshire, Kharanos, or Dolanaar.",al={"alliance version","is there alliance welcome"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers receive this warm welcome upon passing through Razor Hill, establishing an early bond with the central outpost of Durotar."},kw={"collector's edition","companion","durotar","magga","pet","razor hill","voucher","welcome"},rel={"npc:magga","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar"},m={start="Razor Hill Gift Voucher",["end"]="Magga",level="1",faction="Horde",id=5843},src={"Welcome! (Razor Hill)"}}
E["quest:6062"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="This trial marks a young Horde hunter's first step into the art of beast taming. Guided by the veteran Thotar in Razor Hill, aspiring hunters use an enchanted taming rod to subdue and bond with a vicious dire mottled boar.",h="This trial marks a young Horde hunter's first step into the art of beast taming.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Rite of Passage",b="For orc and Darkspear troll hunters coming of age in Durotar, surviving alone in the wilderness is only half the battle. A true master of the wilds must learn to project authority over nature itself, turning hostile beasts into loyal allies. Hunter trainer Thotar entrusts novices with an enchanted taming rod, challenging them to face down a fierce wild boar without resorting to a lethal arrow.",sp=0},{t="The Boars of Durotar",b="Dire mottled boars roam the arid brush surrounding Razor Hill. Though brutish and ill-tempered, their resilience and ferocity make them ideal introductory subjects for taming. Withstanding their charges and enduring their aggression while channeling the rod's power requires patience and iron resolve—virtues essential for any tracker of the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="It serves as the first practical test for young hunters in Durotar, teaching them how to channel their will through a taming rod to subdue a wild creature rather than simply slaying it.",al={"why do this quest","boar taming quest reason","taming the beast point"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer stationed in Razor Hill, offers this assignment once you have proven your basic survival skills across Durotar.",al={"quest giver","who gives taming the beast","where to get boar quest"}},{q="Where are the dire mottled boars found?",a="Dire mottled boars can be found wandering the dry scrublands just outside the palisades of Razor Hill in central Durotar.",al={"boar location","where is dire mottled boar","where to find boar"}},{q="Do you keep the boar permanently after this quest?",a="No. The boar tamed during this initial exercise serves only as practice. It departs once returned to Thotar, as you must continue your training with other creatures before forming a lasting bond.",al={"do i keep the boar","is the boar my permanent pet","keep dire mottled boar"}},{q="What comes after this task?",a="Once you return to Thotar, he will test your command over other deadly predators found in Durotar, including surf crawlers and armored scorpid beasts.",al={"next quest","what after boar taming","taming chain next step"}},{q="Why use a taming rod instead of pure instinct?",a="Novice hunters lack the refined spiritual and physical discipline required to bond with beasts directly. The enchanted taming rod acts as a focus, helping novices project authority over a wild beast's spirit until they master the art permanently.",al={"why taming rod","what does the rod do","lore of taming rod"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite of passage bridges the gap between a simple marksman and a true master of beasts, unlocking the hunter's defining bond with animal companions.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, commanding a beast reflects strength of will and authority over the harsh wilderness of their new home in Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear hunters use this training to attune their spirits to the rugged wildlife of Kalimdor, continuing their ancient stalking traditions."},kw={"dire mottled boar","durotar","hunter quest","pet taming","razor hill","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:6065","quest:6061","quest:6081","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",["end"]="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6062},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 1)"}}
E["quest:6068"] = {t="quest",n="The Hunter's Path",z="durotar",s="The Hunter's Path is a rite of passage directing young orc and troll hunters to Razor Hill. Under the guidance of master hunter Thotar, fledgling trackers learn the vital discipline of binding wild predators to their will.",h="The Hunter's Path is a rite of passage directing young orc and troll hunters to Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Awakening",b="Up to this point, an apprentice hunter in Durotar relies solely on their own bow and cunning. Tracking prey through red clay canyons and harsh scrubland teaches patience, but true mastery in the Horde requires bonding with the untamed fauna of the land. Class trainers recognize when a student has grown capable enough to walk this road, directing them straight to Razor Hill.",sp=0},{t="The Master at Razor Hill",b="Waiting at Razor Hill is Thotar, a veteran hunter steeped in the wild lore of Durotar. Thotar serves as the mentor who instructs novitiates in the perilous ritual of subduing ferocious beasts without breaking their spirit. Meeting him is the first step toward walking the wilderness with a loyal companion at one's side.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of The Hunter's Path?",a="It serves as the introductory summons that sends orc and troll hunters to Razor Hill so they can begin their beast taming training.",al={"why do hunters path","hunter path quest purpose","what does this quest do"}},{q="Who is Thotar?",a="Thotar is a seasoned hunter located in Razor Hill who oversees the trials required for young Horde trackers to bond with and command wild beasts.",al={"thotar who is he","who is thotar","thotar razor hill"}},{q="Why can't young hunters tame pets immediately?",a="Controlling a dangerous predator requires deep discipline, patience, and specialized taming techniques. Until a hunter demonstrates basic survival skills, attempting to bind a wild beast would result in mauling or death.",al={"why no pet at level 1","why must hunters wait for pets","when do hunters get pets"}},{q="Which races undertake this specific trial?",a="This particular version of the path is meant for orcs and Darkspear trolls coming of age in Durotar, while tauren hunters undertake a similar trial in Mulgore.",al={"who gets this quest","is this for orcs and trolls only","what races do this"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Thotar?",a="Thotar immediately tasks the hunter with tracking down and subjugating various native predators across Durotar to prove their taming prowess.",al={"what comes next","after hunters path","next quest after thotar"}},{q="Where does this training take place?",a="The trial centers around Razor Hill, the primary settlement in central Durotar situated between the Valley of Trials and Orgrimmar.",al={"where is razor hill","thotar location","where to go"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This summons marks the most defining threshold in your journey: moving from a lone marksman to a true master of beasts.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, partnering with a ferocious companion echoes ancient traditions that stretch back to the wolf riders of Draenor.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear hunters regard learning to tame local raptors and boars as essential for securing their footing in Durotar's treacherous wilds.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on its scouts and trackers to tame regional predators, turning the unforgiving ecology of Durotar into an asset."},kw={"durotar","hunter trainer","hunter's path","pet quest","razor hill","tame beast","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","quest:6061","quest:6081","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={["end"]="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6068},src={"The Hunter's Path (Orc and Troll)"}}
E["quest:6081"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="durotar",s="Training the Beast is the culminating rite of passage for young orc and troll hunters in Durotar. After demonstrating mastery over the wild beasts of the plains, hunters are sent from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar to study under veteran master hunter Ormak Grimshot. Completing this journey teaches the novice how to care for, feed, and hone the skills of their lifelong animal companion.",h="Training the Beast is the culminating rite of passage for young orc and troll hunters in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Journey Beyond the Wilderness",b="In the arid canyon lands of Durotar, mastering a bow and surviving the harsh elements is only half of a hunter's duty. After proving their resilience by taming Durotar's fierce boars, crab scavengers, and armored scorpid stalkers, young hunters are ready for the true responsibility of stewardship. Thotar, stationed in Razor Hill, dispatches them north through the red clay gulches straight to the fortified gates of Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="The Valley of Honor",b="Within the bustling capital, aspiring track-masters must seek out the Valley of Honor, an enclave where warrior spirits and veteran stalkers hone their craft. There dwells Ormak Grimshot, one of the Horde's most revered master hunters. Ormak looks past raw youth to see whether a hunter possesses the patience required not just to command a beast, but to sustain and nurture it through famine, battle, and loss.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="A beast won through force of will remains wild until an understanding is forged between hunter and companion. Ormak imparts the sacred traditions required to maintain that bond: the knowledge of which foods nourish each creature's spirit, the discipline needed to teach them lethal techniques, and the spiritual focus required to revive a fallen beast should it collapse in the line of duty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Training the Beast?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer situated outside the barracks in Razor Hill, offers this task once you have successfully subdued all three test creatures across Durotar.",al={"quest giver","who gives training the beast","where to start training the beast"}},{q="Where can I find Ormak Grimshot?",a="Ormak Grimshot resides in the Valley of Honor, an eastern district within the capital city of Orgrimmar, alongside other veteran hunter and warrior mentors.",al={"ormak grimshot location","find ormak grimshot","where is ormak"}},{q="What skills does Ormak Grimshot teach you?",a="Ormak teaches you how to train your companion with active and passive abilities, how to feed your pet to keep it loyal and content, and how to revive it if it dies in combat.",al={"what do i learn","quest reward skills","hunter pet abilities"}},{q="Why do orc and troll hunters have to visit Orgrimmar for this?",a="Local trainers like Thotar can teach basic wilderness survival, but advanced beast mastery is preserved by the Horde's elder scouts and venerated trackers like Ormak Grimshot in the capital.",al={"why go to orgrimmar","why orgrimmar","valley of honor visit"}},{q="Do other Horde races undertake this exact quest?",a="No. This specific rite is designed for orc and troll hunters starting in Durotar. Tauren hunters undertake a parallel ritual in Mulgore under their own tribal masters.",al={"can tauren do this","is this orc only","undead hunter"}},{q="What happens if a hunter neglects to complete this training?",a="Without finishing this instruction, a hunter cannot feed, properly train, or resurrect their companion, rendering any captured beast unhappy, weak, and ultimately prone to abandoning them.",al={"do i need to do this","can i skip training the beast"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This quest marks the moment your pet becomes a permanent, dependable ally rather than a fleeting summon, unlocking the essential Feed Pet and Revive Pet arts.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs view the bond with their hunting companion as a matter of martial honor and duty, a partnership tested in battle across the harsh frontiers of Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls carving out a new home in Kalimdor, learning to commune with Durotar's savage creatures is vital for scouting and surviving in unfamiliar soil.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on its scouts and beasts to secure the fragile borders of Durotar and the Barrens against centaur, quilboar, and Alliance incursions."},kw={"durotar","hunter pet","orgrimmar","ormak grimshot","razor hill","thotar","training the beast","valley of honor"},rel={"quest:6061","quest:6065","npc:ormak-grimshot","npc:thotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-honor","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",["end"]="Ormak Grimshot",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6081},src={"Training the Beast (Orc and Troll)"}}
E["quest:6082"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="This quest marks the final trial in a young Horde hunter's basic rites of passage in Durotar. Guided by the veteran hunter Thotar in Razor Hill, an aspiring tracker must confront and tame a dangerous armored scorpid. Conquering this armored predator proves mastery over wild beasts and unlocks the lifelong ability to tame, call, and dismiss a true companion.",h="This quest marks the final trial in a young Horde hunter's basic rites of passage in Durotar.",sec={{t="The Final Trial",b="Before a hunter is permitted to roam Kalimdor with a loyal animal companion, they must prove they can command the harshest wildlife Durotar has to offer. Razor Hill's hunter trainer, Thotar, sends trainees to subdue three distinct creatures with an enchanted taming rod. Having previously tested their mettle against dire boars and swift surf crawlers, hunters are tasked with facing the armored scorpid—a venomous, heavily plated predator that embodies resilience and lethal speed.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="Subduing an armored scorpid is not an act of mere slaughter, but a demonstration of focus and dominance while under relentless assault. Thotar urges hunters to emulate the beast's quick, confident strikes. Returning to Razor Hill after successfully charming the venomous arachnid proves that the hunter possesses the calm will necessary to maintain control. With the taming rod returned, Thotar imparts the innate techniques of the wild, allowing the hunter to seek out and bind a permanent companion of their own choosing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creature do I need to tame for this trial?",a="You must seek out an armored scorpid roaming the arid red crags of Durotar and use Thotar's taming rod to pacify and control it.",al={"what beast to tame","target beast","scorpid quest"}},{q="Do I get to keep the armored scorpid after finishing the quest?",a="No. The armored scorpid tamed during the trial is temporary and vanishes once the training rod is handed back. Completing the task, however, teaches you the permanent ability to tame whichever wild beast you desire.",al={"keep scorpid","do i keep the pet","scorpid permanent"}},{q="Who initiates this rite of passage?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer situated in Razor Hill within central Durotar, oversees this rite of passage for young orc and troll hunters.",al={"quest giver","who gives taming the beast","thotar location"}},{q="Why does Thotar want hunters to tame an armored scorpid specifically?",a="Thotar considers the armored scorpid an ideal creature to emulate due to its confident, swift strikes and natural resilience. Mastering such a dangerous predator proves a hunter is ready to command any beast in the wild.",al={"why scorpid","purpose of scorpid"}},{q="What skills do you learn upon completing this quest?",a="Completing this trial grants the foundational abilities of a seasoned beast master: Tame Beast, Call Pet, and Dismiss Pet.",al={"rewards","what spells do i get","taming skills unlocked"}},{q="What comes after this trial?",a="Once you have learned how to tame and call your own companion, Thotar directs you toward training that pet, sending you on the follow-up quest 'Training the Beast' to master feeding and commanding your ally.",al={"next quest","what's next","after taming 3"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite of passage is the defining milestone of a hunter's early journey, granting permanent access to the core techniques of taming, calling, and commanding animal companions.",["faction:Horde"]="Orc and troll youths in Durotar must survive the barren land's most vicious predators to earn their place as true scouts and providers for the Horde.",["race:Orc"]="Subduing Durotar's scorpids honors the orcish philosophy of overcoming harsh terrain through unyielding willpower and martial discipline.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear hunters draw upon their keen instincts and deep connection to wild spirits to pacify venomous predators that would strike others down."},kw={"armored scorpid","durotar","hunter trial","pet quest","razor hill","tame beast","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","quest:6081","quest:6061","quest:6065","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6082},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 3)"}}
E["quest:6083"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="The second trial in a young hunter's rite of mastery in Durotar, directed by the trainer Thotar in Razor Hill. Aspiring orc and troll hunters are sent to the coastline near the Echo Isles to pacify a surf crawler, expanding their bond beyond terrestrial beasts to coastal wildlife.",h="The second trial in a young hunter's rite of mastery in Durotar, directed by the trainer Thotar in Razor Hill.",sec={{t="Bonding with the Coast",b="Having successfully mastered a dire mottled boar, a fledgling hunter is tasked by Thotar to turn their attention toward the sea. Durotar's harsh environment includes jagged coasts and shallow reefs teeming with armored crustaceans. Facing a surf crawler requires patience and fortitude, as these armored crabs resist intrusion into their coastal domain.",sp=0},{t="The Extension of Will",b="Thotar teaches that any beast a hunter binds must become an extension of their own strength. By subduing an aquatic creature like the surf crawler with the taming rod, the hunter learns to adapt their commanding presence across different temperaments and environments, proving their readiness for permanent companions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are surf crawlers found?",a="Surf crawlers skitter along the eastern shores of Durotar, specifically in the shallows across from Sen'jin Village near the waters leading out toward the Echo Isles.",al={"surf crawler location","where is surf crawler","crab location"}},{q="What is the purpose of taming a surf crawler?",a="Thotar assigns the surf crawler to teach hunters how to command diverse beasts. Learning to tame an armored aquatic creature broadens a hunter's control, proving they can master animals from water as easily as those from dry land.",al={"why tame crab","surf crawler quest purpose"}},{q="Do I keep the surf crawler permanently?",a="No. The beasts tamed during these initial trials are temporary practice subjects subdued through the magic of Thotar's taming rod. Only after completing the entire trial series will you learn the permanent taming skill.",al={"do i keep the crab","is surf crawler permanent"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer situated in Razor Hill, offers this trial after you prove your ability to tame a dire mottled boar.",al={"quest giver","who starts taming the beast 2"}},{q="What comes after taming the surf crawler?",a="Upon returning the rod to Thotar, he will test you with a third and final trial, tasking you to track down and tame an Armored Scorpid before teaching you permanent beast mastery.",al={"next quest","what's next in the chain"}},{q="Why use a taming rod instead of natural skills?",a="Novice hunters have not yet cultivated the innate spiritual authority required to bond wild beasts permanently. The taming rod acts as a conduit, allowing beginners to safely practice channeling their will before learning the true technique.",al={"why taming rod","what is taming rod"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This trial instills the foundational discipline required to command defensive beasts, demonstrating how a creature's natural armor and tenacity complement a ranged marksman.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs carving out a permanent home in Durotar, subduing the shoreline's hardy fauna reinforces their mastery over the rugged landscape.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls are deeply familiar with the waters near the Echo Isles and Sen'jin Village, making this trial an encounter with the familiar wildlife of their coastal refuge."},kw={"durotar","echo isles","pet taming","razor hill","sen'jin village","surf crawler","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","quest:6061","quest:6081","quest:6065"},m={start="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6083},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 2)"}}
E["quest:7664"] = {t="quest",n="Ivory Raptor Replacement",z="durotar",s="Ivory Raptor Replacement is a service offered by the troll raptor handler Zjolnir in Durotar. It allows veteran Horde riders who bonded with the rare ivory-scaled raptor to trade their old mount's whistle for an armored, swift beast bred for war.",h="Ivory Raptor Replacement is a service offered by the troll raptor handler Zjolnir in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Change of Mounts",b="The Darkspear troll handlers at Sen'jin Village take great pride in rearing the finest hunting raptors in Kalimdor. As riding techniques and armor smithing advanced, Darkspear beast handlers began outfitting their swiftest predators with heavy barding and sharpened claws suited for full-scale conflict. Zjolnir offers riders carrying the whistle of an ivory raptor the chance to exchange their companion for one of these updated, armored war raptors.",sp=0},{t="The Old Breeds",b="Ivory raptors were among the early prized mounts seen carrying champions across Durotar and the Barrens. Lacking the heavy plates and gear of contemporary war mounts, these beasts relied purely on raw speed and instinct. While breeders like Zjolnir are eager to provide modern armor, some riders choose to keep their original companions as a symbol of early service to the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the ivory raptor exchange?",a="Zjolnir, the raptor handler stationed outside Sen'jin Village in Durotar, manages the exchange of older mounts for freshly equipped swift raptors.",al={"who gives quest","raptor handler durotar","zjolnir"}},{q="Why would someone trade in their raptor?",a="The newer swift raptors are raised and equipped with armored plating, sharpened talons, and updated harnesses tailored for frontline battle, giving champions a modern combat appearance without losing the speed of their old mount.",al={"why trade raptor","mount exchange reason","what do you get"}},{q="Do I have to give up my Ivory Raptor?",a="No. The exchange is entirely voluntary. Riders who appreciate the historic, unarmored appearance of the ivory raptor may simply keep their whistle and ride as they always have.",al={"keep ivory raptor","is exchange required","must i trade"}},{q="Where does this take place?",a="The trade occurs at the raptor pens just east of Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar.",al={"where is zjolnir","replacement location"}},{q="What happens to the old raptor whistle?",a="Handing over the whistle of the ivory raptor is permanent. Zjolnir takes the original beast into the pens and issues a new mount whistle in return.",al={"lose old whistle","can i get it back"}},{q="Can Alliance characters make this trade?",a="No. Zjolnir serves only the Horde, and troll-bred raptors are kept strictly within Horde stables and territories.",al={"alliance raptor trade","is this horde only"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The raptors bred near Sen'jin Village represent the bond between the Darkspear and Kalimdor's fiercest predators, proving their skill at beast mastery in their new island home.",["faction:Horde"]="Armored mounts reflect the Horde's hardening military stance across Kalimdor, turning wild hunting predators into formidable weapons of war."},kw={"durotar","ivory raptor","sen'jin village","swift raptor","troll mount","whistle","zjolnir"},rel={"npc:zjolnir","zone:durotar"},m={start="Zjolnir",level="1",faction="Horde",id=7664},src={"Ivory Raptor Replacement"}}
E["quest:7665"] = {t="quest",n="Red Raptor Replacement",z="durotar",s="Red Raptor Replacement is an exchange offered by Zjolnir at Sen'jin Village in Durotar. It allows seasoned troll riders to trade their original mottled red riding raptor for an updated, armor-clad swift beast.",h="Red Raptor Replacement is an exchange offered by Zjolnir at Sen'jin Village in Durotar.",sec={{t="The Raptor Breeders of Sen'jin",b="Sen'jin Village serves as the primary home and training ground for the Darkspear tribe's domesticated raptors. Under the keen eye of handlers like Zjolnir, these aggressive jungle predators are conditioned into dependable battle mounts for the Horde. As riding traditions have developed, handlers began outfitting their swiftest stock with protective saddles, leg wrappings, and reinforced battle gear.",sp=0},{t="A Trade of Claws",b="Zjolnir offers a direct exchange for warriors who acquired older breeding stock. Riders returning with a Mottled Red Raptor can hand over their whistle in return for a mount with freshly sharpened claws and seasoned armor. While the new raptor matches the speed of the veteran beast, its appearance displays the martial readiness expected of the Horde's frontline scouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zjolnir?",a="Zjolnir is a Darkspear troll mount trainer and handler stationed in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar. He manages the tribe's stable of riding raptors and provides experienced riders with swift mounts.",al={"zjolnir","who is the quest giver","raptor handler"}},{q="What mount is needed for this exchange?",a="You need the Whistle of the Mottled Red Raptor, an older breed of swift raptor mount. Zjolnir accepts this mount and replaces it with a newer swift raptor variant.",al={"what raptor do i need","whistle requirement","mottled red raptor"}},{q="Where does this exchange take place?",a="The exchange takes place at Sen'jin Village in southern Durotar, where the Darkspear trolls stable and breed their raptors.",al={"where is this quest","quest location","where is zjolnir"}},{q="Is the new raptor faster than the old one?",a="No. Zjolnir notes that the new raptor is just as fast as the old one, but it features a different look, complete with sharpened claws and reinforced harness gear.",al={"is it faster","mount speed increase","does it run faster"}},{q="Why do the Darkspear trolls ride raptors?",a="Raptors have lived alongside trolls for generations in the jungles of Azeroth. The Darkspear appreciate the beasts' vicious cunning, agility, and fierce loyalty once broken to the saddle, making them the preferred mount of the tribe.",al={"why raptors","troll mounts","trolls and raptors"}},{q="Can members of other Horde races make this exchange?",a="Any Horde rider who legitimately obtained a Mottled Red Raptor—typically through gaining exalted standing with the Darkspear or being a troll rider—can bring the beast to Zjolnir for replacement.",al={"can orcs do this","can tauren do this","cross race exchange"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Sen'jin Village is the heart of Darkspear raptor training, where riders prove their mastery over Kalimdor's deadliest predators.",["faction:Horde"]="Darkspear raptor handlers supply the Horde with fierce, agile cavalry mounts suited for the rocky barrens and scrubland of Durotar."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","mottled red raptor","mount","raptor","sen'jin village","swift raptor","zjolnir"},rel={"npc:zjolnir","zone:durotar"},m={start="Zjolnir",level="1",faction="Horde",id=7665},src={"Red Raptor Replacement"}}
E["quest:784"] = {t="quest",n="Vanquish the Betrayers",z="durotar",s="Vanquish the Betrayers is a Horde military strike ordered by Gar'Thok in Razor Hill to reclaim Tiragarde Keep from human invaders. Kul Tiran forces under Lieutenant Benedict have reoccupied the stronghold, directly violating the fragile peace between Durotar and Theramore. Eliminating their garrison is critical to securing the eastern coast of the orcish homeland.",h="Vanquish the Betrayers is a Horde military strike ordered by Gar'Thok in Razor Hill to reclaim Tiragarde Keep...",sec={{t="A Shattered Truce",b="When Thrall led the Horde across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, he formed an uneasy alliance with Lady Jaina Proudmoore to vanquish the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal. That peace was shattered when Jaina's estranged father, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, arrived with the formidable navy of Kul Tiras. Blaming all orcs for the atrocities of the Old Horde, the Admiral invaded Durotar and seized coastal footholds, including Tiragarde Keep. Though Daelin was eventually slain at Theramore, remnants of his fleet refuse to honor any pact or surrender their hatred.",sp=0},{t="Benedict's Resurgence",b="Following the fall of the Grand Admiral, Tiragarde Keep was briefly broken, but Kul Tiras reserves under Lieutenant Benedict have since retaken the fortress. From this fortified redoubt between Razor Hill and Sen'jin Village, the sailors and marines harass travelers and threaten the eastern sea approaches. Gar'Thok views their entrenched position as an immediate danger to the security of Durotar, calling upon Horde warriors to strike directly at Benedict's command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are Kul Tiran humans attacking Durotar?",a="They are remnants of the expeditionary fleet commanded by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. The Admiral refused to accept peaceful coexistence between humans and orcs, seeking to eradicate Durotar entirely. Even after his death, his loyalists continue to occupy coastal redoubts like Tiragarde Keep in defiance of the Horde.",al={"why are humans in durotar","kul tiras attacking","tiragarde keep humans lore"}},{q="Who is Lieutenant Benedict?",a="Lieutenant Benedict is the commanding officer of the Kul Tiran reserves currently holding Tiragarde Keep. Following the defeat of Grand Admiral Proudmoore, Benedict rallied the surviving marines and sailors to retake the coastal fortification and mount persistent operations against the orcs.",al={"who is benedict","lieutenant benedict lore","leader tiragarde keep"}},{q="Does Jaina Proudmoore support these humans?",a="No. Jaina made a pact of mutual survival with Warchief Thrall and actively opposed her father's aggressive crusade to preserve peace. The troops holding Tiragarde Keep are rogue remnants of Kul Tiras who reject Theramore's diplomacy and view Jaina's truce as an act of treason.",al={"does jaina support them","theramore kul tiras alliance","jaina proudmoore tiragarde"}},{q="Why are they called 'betrayers'?",a="Gar'Thok considers them betrayers because their invasion directly violated the diplomatic understanding forged between Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore after the Third War. Their continued military presence in sovereign Horde territory defies the post-war boundaries established on Kalimdor.",al={"why betrayers","who betrayed who","betrayers meaning"}},{q="Where is Tiragarde Keep located?",a="Tiragarde Keep is situated on the eastern coastline of Durotar, south of Razor Hill and just northeast of Sen'jin Village. Its high stone walls overlook the coastal waters, providing the invaders a strategic base close to Horde settlements.",al={"tiragarde keep location","where is tiragarde keep","where to find benedict"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Kul Tiran occupation of Tiragarde Keep is an ongoing act of war right on Durotar's threshold. Removing Benedict's forces demonstrates that the Horde can defend its newly settled home from foreign fleets.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs honor the truce struck with Jaina at Mount Hyjal, but Kul Tiras brings back bitter memories of the Second War. Fighting off Benedict's marines is a matter of survival and ancestral pride.",["race:Troll"]="Tiragarde Keep lies uncomfortably close to the Darkspear settlement of Sen'jin Village. Clearing out these hostile sailors directly protects the trolls' vulnerable new home."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","gar'thok","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","marines","razor hill","sailors","tiragarde keep","vanquish the betrayers"},rel={"subzone:tiragarde-keep","npc:gar-thok","quest:825","quest:830","subzone:razor-hill","topic:kul-tiras","npc:jaina-proudmoore","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gar'Thok",level="7",faction="Horde",id=784},src={"Vanquish the Betrayers"}}
E["quest:786"] = {t="quest",n="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression",z="durotar",s="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression is a vital Horde defense mission handed out by the scout Lar Prowltusk near Sen'jin Village. Players are tasked with infiltrating Kolkar Crag to destroy three sets of coordinated invasion plans before the centaur clan can strike the fledgling settlements of Durotar.",h="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression is a vital Horde defense mission handed out by the scout Lar Prowltusk near...",sec={{t="A Looming Invasion",b="While scouting western Durotar, the troll tracker Lar Prowltusk slipped into Kolkar Crag under cover of night. What he discovered was alarming: the Kolkar centaurs were not merely mounting disorganized coastal raids, but coordinating an ambitious, three-pronged invasion aimed squarely at the orc and Darkspear homelands. The centaur warlords divided their battle strategies among three distinct leaders, intending to strike the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, and the gates of Orgrimmar itself.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Canyons",b="To avert catastrophic fighting across the dry red canyons of Durotar, recruits are sent deep into Kolkar Crag to cut the head off the serpent. Infiltrating the dusty encampment and burning the three attack scrolls disrupts the centaurs' chain of command. While Lar Prowltusk remains confident that the Horde would inevitably crush any full invasion, destroying these documents spares Durotar's defenders costly bloodshed while their young nation is still finding its footing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Thwarting Kolkar Aggression?",a="The quest is given by Lar Prowltusk, a Darkspear troll scout stationed just outside Sen'jin Village along the southern bluffs of Durotar.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","lar prowltusk location"}},{q="What targets are the Kolkar centaur planning to attack?",a="The Kolkar battle plans outline a coordinated, three-tiered offensive targeting the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, and the Horde capital of Orgrimmar.",al={"centaur targets","what are attack plans","three targets"}},{q="Where is Kolkar Crag located?",a="Kolkar Crag is a sunbaked canyon complex tucked just west over the rocky ridges from Sen'jin Village in southern Durotar.",al={"kolkar crag location","where is the crag","centaur village durotar"}},{q="Where are the attack plans found inside the crag?",a="The three scrolls containing the invasion blueprints are kept in the hands of three separate Kolkar leaders guarding different campsites throughout the crag.",al={"attack plan locations","where are scrolls","centaur leaders"}},{q="Why do the Kolkar want to invade Durotar?",a="The Kolkar are an aggressive, expansionist centaur clan native to the dry lands of Kalimdor. They view the arriving orcs and Darkspear trolls as intruders infringing upon their territory and hunting grounds.",al={"why are centaur attacking","centaur motive","kolkar lore"}},{q="What happens after the plans are destroyed?",a="Destroying the documents prevents a coordinated siege, throwing the Kolkar's tactical offensive into disarray and protecting Durotar's fragile settlements from sudden devastation.",al={"quest aftermath","does centaur attack stop"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Stopping the Kolkar offensive prevents the fledgling Horde from having to fight an exhausting, multi-front territorial war right at the threshold of its new home.",["race:Troll"]="Having already lost their ancient island home, the Darkspear trolls cannot afford to let Sen'jin Village be overwhelmed by marauding centaurs.",["race:Orc"]="The Valley of Trials is where young orcs undergo their rites of adulthood, making centaur aggression there an existential insult to orcish warrior culture."},kw={"durotar","kolkar","kolkar crag","lar prowltusk","orgrimmar","sen'jin village","thwarting kolkar aggression","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:lar-prowltusk","subzone:kolkar-crag","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Lar Prowltusk",level="8",faction="Horde",id=786},src={"Thwarting Kolkar Aggression"}}
E["quest:787"] = {t="quest",n="The New Horde",z="durotar",s="The New Horde is an introductory task in the Valley of Trials given by the veteran warrior Eitrigg. It directs fresh recruits to report to Gornek within the Den to begin their training. Through this brief summons, Eitrigg shares his personal journey and Thrall's guiding vision for a redeemed Horde.",h="The New Horde is an introductory task in the Valley of Trials given by the veteran warrior Eitrigg.",sec={{t="A Veteran's Return",b="Eitrigg stands in the Valley of Trials under orders from Warchief Thrall to evaluate and mentor the newest hopefuls of the Horde. Having abandoned the Old Horde after the Second War, disillusioned by its corruption by the Burning Legion, Eitrigg lived in quiet exile until captured by humans. Rescued by Thrall, he chose to return after learning of the young Warchief's dream: an honorable Horde rooted in ancestral shamanism, entirely severed from demonic masters.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to the Den",b="Before any recruit can venture beyond the harsh canyons of the Valley of Trials, they must prove their mettle. Eitrigg sends newcomers into the shaded cavern known as the Den to speak with Gornek. Though Gornek rarely minces words about the crude state of incoming aspirants, his oversight ensures that only those who master discipline and survival are permitted into the wider reaches of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Eitrigg?",a="Eitrigg is an aging orc veteran who witnessed firsthand the corruption of the Old Horde under the influence of the Burning Legion. Disillusioned, he withdrew into self-imposed exile in Lordaeron. After being captured by humans and subsequently liberated by Thrall, he swore loyalty to Thrall's newly reformed Horde and now helps oversee recruit training in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who is eitrigg","eitrigg backstory","eitrigg lore"}},{q="Why does Eitrigg talk about the 'New Horde'?",a="The original Horde was manipulated and enslaved by demonic bloodlust under the sway of the Burning Legion. Thrall's New Horde was forged to cast aside demonic control, resurrect traditional shamanistic ways, and build an honorable, autonomous future for orcs and their allies in Kalimdor.",al={"what is the new horde","difference between old and new horde","new horde meaning"}},{q="Where is Gornek located?",a="Gornek is stationed just inside the entrance of the Den, the prominent cave hollowed out in the northern rock wall of the Valley of Trials.",al={"where is gornek","find gornek","gornek location"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Gornek?",a="Gornek accepts you as one of Eitrigg's trainees and gives you your initial field assignments, putting you to work defending the valley and testing your readiness to serve the Horde.",al={"next quest after the new horde","what does gornek do","gornek quest"}},{q="Why was Eitrigg exiled?",a="Eitrigg abandoned the Horde because he was disgusted by the demonic corruption and senseless slaughter orchestrated by warlocks serving the Burning Legion during the earlier wars.",al={"why did eitrigg leave","eitrigg exile reason","eitrigg demon corruption"}},{q="Why are recruits trained in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials provides a secluded, rugged environment in Durotar where young orcs and allied newcomers can face dangerous beasts and scorpids under the watchful eye of veteran trainers before setting out into the wider world.",al={"why valley of trials","purpose of the valley of trials","valley of trials training"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This task encapsulates the founding ethos of Thrall's regime: a complete break from demonic servitude in favor of honor, survival, and ancestral identity.",["race:Orc"]="For young orcs stepping into the Valley of Trials, Eitrigg represents the living memory of their people's tragic past and their redemption under Thrall.",["race:Troll"]="The Darkspear trolls train alongside the orcs in the Valley of Trials, having embraced Thrall's vision of mutual survival and honor."},kw={"burning legion","durotar","eitrigg","gornek","new horde","the den","thrall","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:eitrigg","npc:gornek","quest:1089","npc:thrall","topic:horde","zone:durotar","topic:burning-legion"},m={level="1",faction="Horde",id=787},src={"The New Horde (quest)"}}
E["quest:791"] = {t="quest",n="Carry Your Weight",z="durotar",s="Carry Your Weight is an introductory task offered by Furl Scornbrow atop the watchtower overlooking Razor Hill. Too old to fight on the front lines, the scarred veteran asks young Horde adventurers to salvage canvas from local human and centaur hostiles so he can fashion supplies to aid their journey.",h="Carry Your Weight is an introductory task offered by Furl Scornbrow atop the watchtower overlooking Razor...",sec={{t="A Veteran's Calling",b="Furl Scornbrow is a veteran of the Third War who marched alongside Warchief Thrall during the pioneering of Durotar and the desperate defense at Mount Hyjal. Now slowed by age and old injuries, he no longer wields his axe in battle. Instead, he maintains a steady vigil from the Razor Hill watchtower, sounding the alarm against incursions while supporting the next generation of defenders.",sp=0},{t="Scavenged Canvas",b="With signal horn alerts growing less frequent as the Horde's grip on the region tightens, Furl passes his hours crafting practical gear. Sturdy canvas is hard to come by in the arid canyons of Durotar, but it is carried in abundance by both the Kul Tiran interlopers along the eastern shore and the nomadic Kolkar centaur roaming the plains. Scavenging scraps from these hostile forces provides Furl the cloth needed to stitch utility bags for active scouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furl Scornbrow?",a="Furl Scornbrow is an aging orc veteran stationed in the watchtower above Razor Hill. He fought alongside Thrall during the founding of Durotar and stood in the combined ranks that brought down Archimonde at Mount Hyjal. No longer able to fight on the front lines, he serves as a lookout and uses his downtime to craft field equipment for young Horde warriors.",al={"who is furl","furl scornbrow lore","who gives carry your weight"}},{q="Where can canvas scraps be found in Durotar?",a="Canvas scraps are gathered from the Kul Tiran humans occupying Tiragarde Keep along Durotar's coast and from the Kolkar centaur encamped across the plains. Both factions carry heavy woven materials that can be salvaged from their camps and belongings.",al={"where to get canvas scraps","who drops canvas scraps","canvas scrap locations"}},{q="Where is the watchtower where Furl is located?",a="Furl's watchtower is perched on the high rocky bluffs directly northwest of Razor Hill. A winding path behind the settlement leads up to the summit where the wooden lookout structure stands.",al={"where is furl scornbrow","razor hill watchtower location","find razor hill watchtower"}},{q="What does Furl craft with the canvas scraps?",a="Furl stitches the gathered canvas scraps into a rugged utility bag. For young adventurers journeying across Durotar, having extra carrying capacity for provisions, rations, and salvaged arms is essential for surviving the harsh wilderness.",al={"what does furl make","what is the canvas used for","canvas scraps reward"}},{q="Why is an old warrior crafting bags instead of fighting?",a="Decades of relentless combat have taken their toll on Furl's body, leaving him unable to match the speed and strength demanded in the field. Rather than lamenting his retirement, he finds honor in keeping watch over Razor Hill and manufacturing gear that directly empowers younger fighters to defend the realm.",al={"why is furl crafting","why does furl stay in the tower","why isn't furl fighting"}},{q="What war did Furl fight in?",a="Furl fought under Warchief Thrall during the Third War, taking part in the settlement of Durotar and the climactic Battle of Mount Hyjal against the Burning Legion. He proudly recalls answering the battlecry during the temporary, necessary truce formed between the Horde, the night elves, and the Alliance to defeat Archimonde.",al={"furl battle history","what did furl do before","archimonde furl"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every young soldier in Durotar relies on seasoned veterans like Furl Scornbrow, who remind newcomers that honoring the Horde means doing whatever duty the homeland requires, whether guarding an outpost or sewing canvas.",["race:Orc"]="Furl embodies the older generation of orcs who broke free from demonic corruption, crossed the sea with Thrall, and now dedicate their final years to nurturing the future of their fledgling nation.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Furl demonstrates practical, rugged frontier tailoring, turning discarded heavy canvas from human invaders and centaur raiders into durable wilderness survival gear."},kw={"canvas scraps","carry your weight","durotar","furl scornbrow","kolkar","razor hill","razor hill watchtower","tiragarde"},rel={"npc:furl-scornbrow","subzone:razor-hill-watchtower","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:784","quest:786","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Furl Scornbrow",level="7",faction="Horde",id=791},src={"Carry Your Weight"}}
E["quest:806"] = {t="quest",n="Dark Storms",z="durotar",s="Dark Storms is a critical task assigned by Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill to strike down a rogue warlock corrupting the land. A goblin named Fizzle Darkstorm has entrenched himself in Thunder Ridge on behalf of the insidious Burning Blade cult. Eliminating him is vital to safeguarding Durotar from demonic resurgence before the cultists spread further.",h="Dark Storms is a critical task assigned by Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill to strike down a rogue warlock...",sec={{t="A Threat in the Ridge",b="While young Horde defenders patrol the borders of Durotar, internal corruption festers right under their watch. Orgnil Soulscar, conducting inquiries from Razor Hill, discovered that Thunder Ridge to the northwest has fallen under the sway of dark magic. The ravine is crawling with Burning Blade cultists who bring ruin and chaos to the local wildlife and land.",sp=0},{t="Fizzle Darkstorm",b="Directing the cultist activity within the ridge is Fizzle Darkstorm, an opportunistic goblin warlock allied with the Burning Blade. Rather than serving commerce or cartel interests, Fizzle wields fel power directly in service of the cult's subversive agenda. Slaying him and claiming his twisted claw proves to Orgnil that the cult's immediate leadership in the ravine has been broken.",sp=0},{t="Rooting Out the Cult",b="The Burning Blade represents everything Thrall's new Horde fights to leave behind: demonic servitude, reckless corruption, and bloodthirsty madness. Striking down Fizzle removes an active conspirator from Durotar's interior, but it also signals that the shadow over the orcish homeland runs far deeper than isolated encampments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Fizzle Darkstorm?",a="Fizzle Darkstorm is a goblin warlock operating on behalf of the Burning Blade cult. He and his cultist followers have taken refuge in Thunder Ridge, spreading demonic chaos across the ravine until Orgnil Soulscar calls for his execution.",al={"who is fizzle","fizzle darkstorm lore","fizzle goblin"}},{q="Where is Thunder Ridge located?",a="Thunder Ridge is a rugged canyon situated in northwestern Durotar, west of the river divide and north of Razor Hill. It is notoriously overrun by lightning-infused beasts and encampments of Burning Blade cultists.",al={"where is thunder ridge","thunder ridge location","how to find thunder ridge"}},{q="Why is the Burning Blade in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade seeks to undermine Thrall's Horde and re-establish demonic dominance over the orcs. They operate secretly out of hidden ravines, caves, and canyons across Durotar to sow corruption from within.",al={"burning blade in durotar","why are cultists in durotar","burning blade motives"}},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar want Fizzle's claw specifically?",a="Orgnil requires unmistakable proof that the warlock has been terminated. Bringing back Fizzle's claw confirms that the head of the cultist cabal in Thunder Ridge can no longer direct operations.",al={"why fizzle claw","fizzle's claw meaning","proof of death fizzle"}},{q="What happens after Fizzle is slain?",a="Defeating Fizzle clears the immediate threat in Thunder Ridge, leading Orgnil Soulscar to direct seasoned champions toward other veteran scouts and investigators, such as Margoz, to root out further Burning Blade conspiracies.",al={"what comes after dark storms","dark storms follow up","next quest after dark storms"},sp=1},{q="Why would a goblin work for the Burning Blade?",a="While many goblins seek gold through trade cartels, some are enticed by the raw power, influence, and dark arts offered by shadow magic. Fizzle embraced fel witchcraft and lent his ruthless cunning directly to the cultists.",al={"goblin in burning blade","why is fizzle with the cult","fizzle warlock"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The Burning Blade represents the dark past the orcs fight every day to overcome. Eliminating cultist infiltrators like Fizzle is essential to preserving Thrall's free nation.",["class:Warlock"]="Fizzle Darkstorm demonstrates the reckless danger of uncontrolled fel devotion, making him an embarrassment and a hazard that disciplined Horde practitioners cannot tolerate.",["faction:Horde"]="Ensuring the heart of Durotar remains secure from demonic subversion allows the nascent Horde to direct its defenses outward rather than collapsing from inside.",["class:Shaman"]="The dark rites practiced by Fizzle and his minions disrupt the natural spirits of Thunder Ridge, agitating its beasts and demanding elemental balance be restored."},kw={"burning blade","dark storms","durotar","fizzle darkstorm","fizzle's claw","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","thunder ridge"},rel={"npc:orgnil-soulscar","subzone:thunder-ridge","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:823","topic:goblin"},m={start="Orgnil Soulscar",level="12",faction="Horde",id=806},src={"Dark Storms (quest)"}}
E["quest:808"] = {t="quest",n="Minshina's Skull",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village is haunted by the desperate cries of his deceased brother, Minshina. Slain and subjected to dark magic by the rogue witch doctor Zalazane on the Echo Isles, Minshina's soul remains bound inside his own severed skull. Freeing the fallen troll requires infiltrating Zalazane's ritual grounds to reclaim the relic and release his spirit from eternal torment.",h="Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village is haunted by the desperate cries of his deceased brother, Minshina.",sec={{t="A Plea from the Shadows",b="Master Gadrin serves as one of the Darkspear tribe's spiritual anchors in Sen'jin Village, but his mind is tormented by dark visions. His brother Minshina fell victim to Zalazane's betrayal when the mad warlock seized control of the Echo Isles. Minshina perished during the conflict, but in troll tradition and voodoo mysticism, physical death does not always grant peace. Minshina's tormented voice speaks into Gadrin's dreams, pleading for salvation from a fate worse than death.",sp=0},{t="Zalazane's Circle of Power",b="Zalazane does not simply kill his former brethren; he ensnares their souls to fuel his dark sorcery. Minshina's essence was ritually bound to his own skull, which now rests amidst a blasphemous circle of power on the largest of the Echo Isles. Guarded by hexed trolls and bathed in candlelit ritual, the skull serves as a focal point for the traitor's twisted mojo. So long as it sits within the circle, Minshina remains an eternal captive to Zalazane's will.",sp=0},{t="Freedom in Death",b="To save Minshina, a brave champion must cross the waters east of Sen'jin Village to the southern reaches of the Echo Isles, break into the ritual ring, and extract the skull from the witch doctor's influence. Returning the remains to Master Gadrin severs the dark bindings, allowing Minshina's grateful spirit to briefly materialize, bow in reverence, and finally depart for the realm of the ancestors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Minshina?",a="Minshina was the brother of Master Gadrin, the prominent witch doctor and elder residing in Sen'jin Village. He was murdered during the uprising on the Echo Isles by Zalazane, who then desecrated his remains with dark sorcery.",al={"minshina identity","who is minshina","gadrin brother"}},{q="Why is Minshina's spirit trapped in his skull?",a="Zalazane uses dark voodoo and warlock magic to enslave the spirits of slain Darkspear trolls. By binding Minshina's soul directly to his physical skull and placing it within a ritual circle of power, Zalazane denied him passage to the afterlife and harnessed his spirit.",al={"why trap skull","zalazane soul trap","minshina soul"}},{q="Where is the circle of power located?",a="The ritual site is located atop a hill on the southernmost and largest of the Echo Isles, off the southeastern coast of Durotar. It is recognizable by ritual candles, dancing hexed trolls, and displays of skulls.",al={"where is skull","circle of power location","minshina skull spot"}},{q="What happens when the skull is brought back to Sen'jin Village?",a="Once Master Gadrin receives the skull, the necromantic bindings shatter. Minshina's ghostly form appears before his brother and the adventurer, bows in gratitude, and vanishes to rest peacefully with the ancestors.",al={"quest turn in","what happens to minshina","does minshina appear"},sp=1},{q="Who is Zalazane and why did he do this?",a="Zalazane was once a respected witch doctor alongside Gadrin and Vol'jin. Driven mad by lust for power, he turned on his tribe, used hexes to mind-control his brothers and sisters, and drove the remaining Darkspear refugees onto the mainland of Durotar.",al={"who is zalazane","why zalazane evil","zalazane lore"}},{q="Why can't Gadrin retrieve the skull himself?",a="Master Gadrin is crucial to holding Sen'jin Village together. Between guiding the young Darkspear leadership, advising chieftain Vol'jin, and actively countering Zalazane's expanding hexes across the coast, Gadrin cannot leave the settlement unprotected.",al={"why doesn't gadrin go","gadrin duties"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For a Darkspear troll, recovering Minshina's skull is a sacred duty to family and tribe, striking a blow against Zalazane's perversion of ancestral voodoo traditions.",["class:Priest"]="Priests understand the deep sanctity of the departed soul and recognize the horror of ritual necromancy that binds a fallen brother from finding eternal peace.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman revere the spirits of the ancestors; breaking Zalazane's circle to release a tortured soul restores balance between the spirit world and the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Assisting Master Gadrin honors the bond between the new Horde and the Darkspear tribe, proving that an ally's grief is shared by all."},kw={"circle of power","darkspear","echo isles","gadrin","minshina","sen'jin village","skull","voodoo","zalazane"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:826","topic:troll","zone:durotar","quest:817","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Master Gadrin",level="9",faction="Horde",id=808},src={"Minshina's Skull (quest)"}}
E["quest:812"] = {t="quest",n="Need for a Cure",z="durotar",s="Stranded along the rugged cliffs of northwestern Durotar, the Darkspear troll Rhinag lies poisoned by a venomtail scorpid. With precious little time before the toxin finishes him, he relies on a courier to sprint to Orgrimmar and retrieve a cure from Kor'ghan.",h="Stranded along the rugged cliffs of northwestern Durotar, the Darkspear troll Rhinag lies poisoned by a...",sec={{t="A Scorpid's Sting",b="The arid canyons of Durotar are crawling with venomtail scorpids, aggressive predators whose sting carries a swift, debilitating neurotoxin. Rhinag made the mistake of dropping his guard while battling the beasts near the borderlands. Knowing that the venom coursing through his veins will kill him in under an hour, he is unable to walk the distance to the city gates himself and must place his survival in the hands of whoever passes his remote camp.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Shadows",b="Rather than trusting an ordinary apothecary or shaman, Rhinag directs travelers deep beneath Orgrimmar into the shadowy subterranean caverns of the Cleft of Shadow. There dwells Kor'ghan, an enigmatic practitioner familiar with the harsh poisons of Durotar's wastes. Kor'ghan possesses the knowledge required to brew an effective counter-agent, though he rarely gives his aid freely to those who have not proven their mettle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhinag?",a="Rhinag is a Darkspear troll adventurer found clinging to life along the northwestern cliffs of Durotar. Stung by a venomtail scorpid, he fears both imminent death and the mockery he would face from his kin in Sen'jin Village if he were to return in such a humbled state.",al={"rhinag lore","who is rhinag","rhinag the troll"}},{q="Why is Kor'ghan in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="Kor'ghan makes his home in the Cleft of Shadow, the shadowy cavern beneath Orgrimmar where warlocks, rogues, and other practitioners of dark arts ply their trades away from the eyes of Thrall's honored warriors. His understanding of venomous brews and grueling trials fits the Cleft's subterranean environment.",al={"where is korgan","who is korghan","kor'ghan location"}},{q="Why doesn't Rhinag just seek a shaman or healer in Sen'jin Village?",a="Rhinag admits that his own pride holds him back. He fears that returning to Sen'jin Village in such a careless, venom-stricken condition would earn him nothing but mockery from fellow trolls, preferring instead to seek a discreet remedy from Kor'ghan.",al={"why not go to senjin","why rhinag avoids senjin"}},{q="What happens after Rhinag receives the antidote?",a="Rhinag drinks the antidote and recovers, though his troubles do not end there. Knowing Kor'ghan, the curer will demand that Rhinag prove himself through further grueling trials—slaying boars and harvesting scorpid tails—before he is fully back in the practitioner's good graces.",al={"does rhinag survive","rhinag aftermath"},sp=1},{q="Where can Rhinag be found?",a="He is located in the rugged bluffs of northwestern Durotar, nestled near the border passes leading westward toward the Barrens.",al={"rhinag location","where is rhinag"}},{q="Why is there such an urgent rush for this cure?",a="The venomtail scorpid's poison is exceptionally potent, giving an untreated victim less than an hour before the venom overwhelms their vital organs.",al={"why is it timed","rhinag poison timer"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Rhinag's dread of returning to Sen'jin Village underscores the harsh pride of the Darkspear tribe, where carelessness in basic wilderness survival invites harsh mockery from kin.",["faction:Horde"]="Durotar's rocky terrain is harsh and unforgiving, serving as an unrelenting trial by fire for newly arrived defenders of Thrall's young realm."},kw={"antidote","cleft of shadow","durotar","kor'ghan","need for a cure","orgrimmar","rhinag","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"npc:rhinag","npc:kor-ghan","quest:813","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Rhinag",level="9",faction="Horde",id=812},src={"Need for a Cure"}}
E["quest:813"] = {t="quest",n="Finding the Antidote",z="durotar",s="Finding the Antidote is an urgent task undertaken for Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar to brew a cure for the poisoned hunter Rhinag. Facing a strict deadline before the venom proves fatal, an adventurer must gather venomtail poison sacs from scorpids outside the city walls. It highlights the unforgiving nature of Durotar's wildlife and the necessity of wilderness preparation.",h="Finding the Antidote is an urgent task undertaken for Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar to brew a cure for the poisoned...",sec={{t="A Race Against the Venom",b="While hunting throughout Durotar, a Darkspear troll named Rhinag made the perilous mistake of engaging native venomtail scorpids without bringing along an antidote. Stung and succumbing rapidly to their potent toxins, he was forced to send for immediate aid. The task falls to Kor'ghan, an experienced hunter residing in Orgrimmar, to mix a restorative draught before the poison finishes its work.",sp=0},{t="Crafting the Cure",b="Creating an antidote requires harvesting the source of the affliction itself: the venom sacs of mature venomtails lurking outside the gates of Orgrimmar. Kor'ghan notes that chastising Rhinag for his lack of preparation must wait, as every moment counts. Once the sacs are quickly retrieved and brought back into the city, Kor'ghan synthesizes the draught so it can be rushed straight to the dying hunter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhinag?",a="Rhinag is a Darkspear troll hunter in Durotar who was badly stung by native venomtails while out tracking beasts. Lacking an antidote in the field, he was left incapacitated and reliant on couriers to retrieve a remedy from Orgrimmar before succumbing to the poison.",al={"rhinag lore","who is poisoned","who needs the antidote"}},{q="Who is Kor'ghan?",a="Kor'ghan is an experienced Darkspear troll hunter based in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. He understands the natural beasts of Durotar intimately and possesses the alchemical knowledge required to brew an effective counter-venom using raw venomtail poison sacs.",al={"kor'ghan","who is korphan","korgan orgrimmar"}},{q="Where do the required venom sacs come from?",a="The poison sacs are harvested directly from venomtail scorpids that prowl the rocky arid plains just outside the primary southern and eastern entrances of Orgrimmar.",al={"where are venomtails","poison sac location","venomtail scorpid sacs"}},{q="Why is there an active time limit on this task?",a="The urgency is driven by Rhinag's failing health in the field. Because venomtail toxins are exceptionally virulent and fast-acting, Kor'ghan must receive the ingredients and distill the cure before the hunter perishes from systemic poisoning.",al={"why is there a timer","need for a cure timer","timed quest"}},{q="What lesson does Kor'ghan emphasize during this hunt?",a="Kor'ghan warns that every hunter must carefully study the habits and lethal dangers of their quarry prior to engaging it. Entering the wilderness without proper preparation or countermeasures is an oversight that can easily cost a warrior their life.",al={"kor'ghan lesson","hunting lesson","kor'ghan advice"}},{q="How does this task fit with 'Need for a Cure'?",a="'Need for a Cure' is the foundational errand that sets the emergency in motion and starts the timer. 'Finding the Antidote' is the intermediary step where the player gathers the raw components for Kor'ghan to brew the finished concoction.",al={"need for a cure connection","prerequisite quest","how does it connect"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Kor'ghan serves as a stern reminder to all hunters: knowledge of a beast's venom and carrying appropriate remedies is just as critical as your bow and tracking skills.",["race:Orc"]="Survival in Durotar tests the endurance of the newly settled orcs, demonstrating that even a seasoned scout can fall to the land's native hazards if careless.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde in Durotar looks after its own, ensuring that isolated rangers and scouts on the perimeter can rely on the stronghold of Orgrimmar for aid."},kw={"antidote","durotar","kor'ghan","orgrimmar","poison","rhinag","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"quest:812","npc:kor-ghan","npc:rhinag","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft-of-shadow"},m={start="Kor'ghan",level="9",faction="Horde",id=813},src={"Finding the Antidote"}}
E["quest:816"] = {t="quest",n="Lost But Not Forgotten",z="durotar",s="Lost But Not Forgotten is a somber quest given by Misha Tor'kren at her homestead northwest of Razor Hill. Desperate for closure, she asks travelers to search the dangerous banks of the Southfury River for any trace of her headstrong son, Kron.",h="Lost But Not Forgotten is a somber quest given by Misha Tor'kren at her homestead northwest of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Mother's Dread",b="Northwest of Razor Hill, tucked away in the arid red wastes of Durotar, sits the humble Tor'kren farmstead. Here lives Misha Tor'kren, an orc mother paralyzed by sorrow and anxiety. Days earlier, her son Kron declared he was heading west toward the Southfury River on the border of the Barrens to hunt the river's ferocious crocolisks. Despite her warnings about the deadly beasts, Kron's stubborn pride drove him to storm off to prove his mettle. He has not been seen since.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="Misha asks passing adventurers to comb the shores of the Southfury River for any sign of Kron's fate, even suggesting they look inside the bellies of the crocolisks. Tragically, her darkest instincts prove true. Slaying the vicious Dreadmaw crocolisks along the water reveals Kron's swallowed amulet. Returning the keepsake to Misha extinguishes any lingering hope that her boy survived, but finally grants a grieving mother the closure she needs to begin mourning.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Misha Tor'kren?",a="Misha Tor'kren is an orcish farm mother living at a secluded homestead northwest of Razor Hill in Durotar. Plagued by grief and worry, she asks wanderers to seek out any trace of her missing son, Kron.",al={"misha torkren","who gives lost but not forgotten","kron mother"}},{q="Who was Kron?",a="Kron was Misha Tor'kren's headstrong son. Seeking to prove his strength, he ignored his mother's cautions and left to hunt dangerous crocolisks near the Southfury River, where he met his untimely death.",al={"who is kron","what happened to kron","misha son"},sp=1},{q="Where did Kron go missing?",a="Kron traveled west across Durotar toward the border of the Barrens to hunt along the banks of the Southfury River.",al={"where is kron","where to look for kron","kron location"}},{q="How do you prove Kron's fate to Misha?",a="You find Kron's swallowed amulet among the remains of Dreadmaw crocolisks prowling the waters of the Southfury River. Bringing this recovered heirloom back to Misha confirms his death.",al={"krons amulet","sign of krons fate","crocolisk stomach"},sp=1},{q="What reward does Misha give?",a="Misha gives you a gift she had originally prepared for Kron to celebrate his triumphant return from the hunt. Unable to bear looking at it after learning of his death, she passes it to the adventurer who brought her closure.",al={"lost but not forgotten reward","misha gift"},sp=1},{q="Why did Kron leave in the first place?",a="Kron was driven by stubborn pride and a desire to prove his hunting prowess. When his mother warned him that the crocolisks were far too vicious and dangerous, he grew furious and stormed out to hunt them anyway.",al={"why did kron hunt","kron pride"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Kron's fate is a tragic reminder that while pride and martial glory are core to orcish culture, reckless arrogance without respect for dangerous beasts leads to an unheroic death.",["class:Hunter"]="For hunters, Kron serves as a cautionary tale of a tracker who failed to assess the ferocity of his prey and ended up as their meal.",["faction:Horde"]="Life in early Durotar is harsh and unyielding, where everyday families struggle against the unforgiving landscape and the deadly predators that roam its borders."},kw={"amulet","crocolisk","dreadmaw","kron","misha","razor hill","southfury","tor'kren"},rel={"npc:misha-tor-kren","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Misha Tor'kren",level="11",faction="Horde",id=816},src={"Lost But Not Forgotten (Classic)"}}
E["quest:817"] = {t="quest",n="Practical Prey",z="durotar",s="Practical Prey is a hunting task given by the leatherworker Vel'rin Fang in Sen'jin Village. Facing a growing population and dwindling stockpiles, the Darkspear tribe must harvest durable tiger hides from the neighboring Echo Isles to craft essential shelters, clothing, and gear.",h="Practical Prey is a hunting task given by the leatherworker Vel'rin Fang in Sen'jin Village.",sec={{t="A Matter of Survival",b="Life along the arid coast of Durotar is harsh, and the Darkspear trolls exiled to Sen'jin Village must make full use of every resource. Tiger pelts are among the most versatile materials available, essential for stitching together tents, heavy blankets, and reinforced armor. As the settlement swells with refugees and returning scouts, stockpiles have worn thin, compelling craftspeople like Vel'rin Fang to commission new hunts.",sp=0},{t="Balance and the Hunt",b="The Darkspear maintain a deliberate relationship with the predators of their territory. Rather than overhunting the native Durotar tigers, the trolls generally allow the prowlers to thrive unmolested, culling them only when tribal stores require replenishment. Venturing across the water to the Echo Isles to stalk these predators serves both practical necessity and a traditional test of patience, discipline, and wilderness skill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vel'rin Fang?",a="Vel'rin Fang is a Darkspear troll artisan based in Sen'jin Village who works with pelts and leather. He directs hunters to gather essential hides to keep the tribe clothed, sheltered, and equipped.",al={"vel'rin fang","who gives practical prey","velrin fang"}},{q="Why does Sen'jin Village need tiger furs?",a="The growing population of Sen'jin Village has strained its existing reserves. Tiger pelts provide durable materials for warm blankets, sturdy tents, and leather armor to protect the villagers against the harsh elements.",al={"why tiger pelts","practical prey purpose","what are furs used for"}},{q="Where are the Durotar tigers found?",a="The tigers stalk the wilderness across the Echo Isles, the archipelago situated just off the southeastern coastline of Durotar.",al={"where are the tigers","tiger location","echo isles tigers"}},{q="Why don't the trolls hunt all the tigers nearby?",a="Vel'rin explains that the Darkspear deliberately balance their needs with the local ecology. They allow the predators to thrive so the population remains sustainable, stepping in to cull them only when the village's material demands outpace their supplies.",al={"why let tigers thrive","culling the flock"}},{q="Is hunting tigers significant to Darkspear culture?",a="Yes. Stalking a tiger is viewed as a rite of patience and cunning. Vel'rin fondly recounts waiting nearly an entire day motionless in the foliage of the Echo Isles before claiming his first major hunting victory.",al={"tiger hunt tradition","first tiger hunt"}},{q="Why must hunters travel to the Echo Isles if Zalazane holds them?",a="While the traitor witch doctor Zalazane and his hexed minions occupy much of the archipelago, the wild beasts of the islands remain abundant. Scavenging and hunting along the outer shores remains a necessary risk for the Darkspear.",al={"tigers on echo isles","why go to echo isles"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the exiled Darkspear, hunting across the Echo Isles is a bitter reminder of their lost home, where providing for the clan requires treading ground stolen by Zalazane.",["class:Hunter"]="Vel'rin's tale of enduring a full day of silent tracking before springing the trap speaks directly to the core virtues of patience and precision taught to all young hunters.",["faction:Horde"]="Supporting the fledgling Darkspear enclave with essential trade goods helps anchor the Horde's southern flank along the Great Sea."},kw={"darkspear","durotar tiger","echo isles","hunting","leatherworking","practical prey","sen'jin village","tiger fur","vel'rin fang"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","quest:808","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Vel'rin Fang",level="8",faction="Horde",id=817},src={"Practical Prey"}}
E["quest:818"] = {t="quest",n="A Solvent Spirit",z="durotar",s="Master Vornal of Sen'jin Village tests fledgling adventurers by demanding reagents to compensate for his failing eyesight. He sends prospective pupils to harvest makrura eyes and crawler mucus along the coast of Durotar. While he scoffs at the idea of taking an apprentice, the task serves as a deliberate trial of patience and resolve.",h="Master Vornal of Sen'jin Village tests fledgling adventurers by demanding reagents to compensate for his...",sec={{t="A Master's Fading Sight",b="Master Vornal sits in Sen'jin Village, burdened by age and diminishing vision. Where primal magic once flowed naturally to his fingertips, he now leans heavily on alchemy to sharpen his perceptions and weave his arts. Despite his mounting physical decline, the stubborn troll refuses to take on an apprentice, claiming neither the Darkspear nor the orcs of Durotar have produced anyone worthy of his tutelage.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Unproven",b="Rather than straightforward instruction, Vornal demands raw materials from the harsh coastline: intact makrura eyes and vials of crawler mucus. Sourcing undamaged eyes from the armored, snapping makrura requires delicate strikes, while gathering sufficient mucus tests an adventurer's willingness to endure tedious, menial work. To Vornal, hunting these littoral beasts is less about the reagents and more about weeding out those who lack focus.",sp=0},{t="A Measure of Will",b="For Master Vornal, time and patience are the ultimate measures of strength. He expects brash youths to give in to frustration or abandon the chore entirely. Returning to Sen'jin Village with pristine ingredients demonstrates not only survival skills along the dangerous reefs of the Echo Isles channel, but the discipline necessary to master the subtle arts of alchemy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Vornal?",a="Master Vornal is an elderly troll alchemist and spellcaster dwelling in Sen'jin Village. His physical sight is failing him with age, forcing him to turn to alchemical solvents and brews to perform magic that once came easily.",al={"master vornal","who is vornal","vornal lore"}},{q="Why does Vornal need makrura eyes and crawler mucus?",a="Vornal relies on alchemical concoctions to aid his magic and compensate for his waning eyesight. The mucus and intact makrura eyes serve as reagents for his mixtures, while also functioning as an initiation test for prospective apprentices.",al={"why crawler mucus","why makrura eyes","what does vornal make"}},{q="Why is Vornal so reluctant to teach an apprentice?",a="Vornal possesses high standards and little tolerance for arrogance. He believes no troll or orc has demonstrated the genuine dedication and patience required to learn from him, viewing most aspiring pupils as overly proud and easily discouraged.",al={"vornal apprentice","why no apprentice","is vornal looking for a student"}},{q="Where are these creatures found around Sen'jin Village?",a="Crawlers and makrura roam the shallows along Darkspear Strand and inhabit the waterways separating the mainland from the Echo Isles just offshore.",al={"where are makrura","where are crawlers","darkspear strand beasts"}},{q="Why do the makrura eyes need to be intact?",a="Alchemical brews that sharpen perception require undamaged sensory organs. Brutal strikes during combat risk crushing the makrura's delicate eyes, demanding precision and restraint from the hunter.",al={"intact eye","makrura intact eyes","why intact eyes"}},{q="What lesson is Vornal trying to teach?",a="Vornal believes that patience is the true test of character. By assigning a repetitive and dirty harvesting chore along the surf, he aims to see whether a novice will succumb to weakness and haste or maintain the calm focus of an alchemist.",al={"vornal lesson","meaning of the quest","patience test"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear rebuilding at Sen'jin Village, proving yourself to elder practitioners like Master Vornal is vital to carrying forward the tribe's mystical and alchemical traditions.",["race:Orc"]="Vornal openly doubts whether orcs possess the quiet discipline needed for alchemy, making the task a chance to prove Horde solidarity extends to scholarly patience.",["faction:Horde"]="Coastal Durotar remains perilous for the fledgling Horde; clearing aggressive makrura and surf crawlers secures the fishing shores around Sen'jin Village."},kw={"alchemy","crawler mucus","darkspear strand","durotar","intact makrura eye","makrura","master vornal","sen'jin village"},rel={"npc:master-vornal","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:darkspear-strand","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:99141"},m={start="Master Vornal",level="7",faction="Horde",id=818},src={"A Solvent Spirit"}}
E["quest:823"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Orgnil",z="durotar",s="Report to Orgnil is an early Horde quest dispatched by Master Gadrin from Sen'jin Village. It directs fledgling adventurers northward to Razor Hill to warn Orgnil Soulscar about the insidious reach of the Burning Blade cult. This dispatch helps coordinate Durotar's scattered defense against demonic corruption brewing right in the orcs' homeland.",h="Report to Orgnil is an early Horde quest dispatched by Master Gadrin from Sen'jin Village.",sec={{t="A Coordinated Defense",b="While Sen'jin Village grapples with its own local woes—most notably Zalazane's treachery on the Echo Isles—Master Gadrin recognizes that reports of the Burning Blade cult represent a far wider danger. Whispers of demonic corruption were uncovered in the Valley of Trials, and the Darkspear witch doctor knows these threats cannot be handled in isolation. He dispatches traveling heroes north along the dusty road to Razor Hill, where the local orc authorities maintain a broader watch over Durotar.",sp=0},{t="Orgnil Soulscar",b="Stationed in the military encampment of Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar is an orc charged with rooting out domestic evils and safeguarding the central heartlands. When adventurers deliver Gadrin's warning, Orgnil wastes no time integrating the reports from both the Valley of Trials and Sen'jin Village. Recognizing that the shadow of the Burning Blade looms dangerously close, he quickly mobilizes forces to dismantle the cultists before their dark rituals can unseat the young nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Report to Orgnil?",a="Master Gadrin, the Darkspear witch doctor and spiritual leader residing in Sen'jin Village, gives you this task after you assist the trolls with their initial local struggles.",al={"who gives report to orgnil","where to get report to orgnil","quest giver report to orgnil"}},{q="Where is Orgnil Soulscar located?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is located in Razor Hill, the fortified settlement situated north of Sen'jin Village in central Durotar.",al={"where is orgnil soulscar","orgnil soulscar location","find orgnil soulscar"}},{q="Why does Master Gadrin send you to Razor Hill?",a="Master Gadrin realizes that demonic cult activity discovered in the Valley of Trials and around Durotar poses a threat to everyone, not just the trolls. He directs you to Orgnil Soulscar, the orc responsible for policing the region against the Burning Blade.",al={"why report to orgnil","why go to razor hill","purpose of report to orgnil"}},{q="What is the Burning Blade mentioned in the quest?",a="The Burning Blade is a treacherous cult of demon worshippers operating in the shadows of Durotar and beyond. Their covert presence in nearby canyons and caves threatens the safety and stability of the nascent Horde.",al={"who are the burning blade","burning blade cult","what is burning blade"}},{q="What quest follows Report to Orgnil?",a="Upon turning in the report to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill, he immediately assigns you the quest Dark Storms to investigate and combat the gathering cultist threat.",al={"next quest after report to orgnil","report to orgnil followup","what comes after report to orgnil"}},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before receiving this quest?",a="It naturally follows your arrival in Sen'jin Village via the quest Report to Sen'jin Village, linking early Valley of Trials discoveries with the wider Durotar campaign.",al={"prereq report to orgnil","how to unlock report to orgnil","previous quest report to orgnil"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This task marks the vital communication and cooperation between the newly allied Darkspear trolls and the orcs of Durotar as they face shared threats.",["race:Troll"]="Though the Darkspear are absorbed in their battle against Zalazane, Master Gadrin demonstrates the trolls' commitment to the Horde by alerting orc leaders to regional dangers.",["race:Orc"]="Orgnil Soulscar represents the frontline defense of your new homeland, ensuring demonic taint does not take root within Durotar's borders."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","master gadrin","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","report to orgnil","sen'jin village"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","npc:orgnil-soulscar","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","subzone:valley-of-trials"},m={start="Master Gadrin",["end"]="Orgnil Soulscar",level="7",faction="Horde",id=823},src={"Report to Orgnil"}}
E["quest:825"] = {t="quest",n="From The Wreckage....",z="durotar",s="Gar'Thok of Razor Hill directs Horde scouts to scavenge the sunken remains of Grand Admiral Proudmoore's fleet off the Scuttle Coast. By recovering advanced Gnomish Tools from the watery wreckage, the Horde hopes to dissect Alliance engineering and turn that technological advantage to its own benefit.",h="Gar'Thok of Razor Hill directs Horde scouts to scavenge the sunken remains of Grand Admiral Proudmoore's...",sec={{t="Echoes of the Fleet",b="When Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore brought the naval might of Kul Tiras to Kalimdor, his vessels choked the shoreline near Tiragarde Keep. Following his defeat, shattered hulls settled along the Scuttle Coast. While the surviving Kul Tiran soldiers fortify the keep itself, the remnants of their armada lie broken on the shoals, slowly rotting beneath the tide.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Contraptions",b="Orcish warfare traditionally relies on raw strength, iron, and blood, but the Horde recognizes the dangerous edge provided by Alliance ingenuity. Gnomish technicians accompanied the expeditionary fleets, outfitting the Alliance vessels with complex machinery and precision gear. Gar'Thok seeks to recover these submerged tools so the Horde can unravel the mechanics behind them.",sp=0},{t="Destined for Orgrimmar",b="The salvaged tools are not meant to remain gathering dust in Razor Hill. Gar'Thok arranges for them to be transported by caravan directly to Orgrimmar. By reverse-engineering gnomish instruments, Horde craftspeople and tacticians aim to better counter Alliance devices in coming conflicts while bolstering their own emerging industries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde salvaging tools from these wrecks?",a="The Horde wants to understand the advanced technology utilized by the Alliance. Gnomes build intricate machinery for human forces, and by studying their tools, Horde tacticians can figure out how to counter Alliance devices while adopting useful mechanics for their own craftspeople.",al={"why get gnomish tools","why salvage wreck","gar'thok reason for tools"}},{q="Whose ships are wrecked off the Scuttle Coast?",a="The sunken vessels belonged to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet. After landing on the shores of Durotar to wage war against Thrall's newly founded nation, several ships were destroyed along the coastline just east of Tiragarde Keep.",al={"whose ships are these","who wrecked ships durotar","proudmoore fleet wreckage"}},{q="Where do the recovered tools go after Razor Hill?",a="Gar'Thok sends the recovered Gnomish Tools on the next caravan bound for Orgrimmar. There, engineers and craftsmen can study the contraptions thoroughly to help strengthen the capital's defenses and industry.",al={"what happens to tools","where do gnomish tools go","who gets the salvage"}},{q="Why are gnomish tools found on human warships?",a="The gnomes are close allies of the humans within the Grand Alliance, frequently providing naval expeditions with mechanical expertise, siege gear, and precision maintenance tools to keep war fleets operational.",al={"why gnomes with humans","gnomes on proudmoore ships","alliance gnomish tech"}},{q="What is the Scuttle Coast?",a="The Scuttle Coast is the eastern shoreline of Durotar running past Tiragarde Keep. It is named for the half-submerged and sunken vessels littering the shallow waters following the battles against Proudmoore's expedition.",al={"where is scuttle coast","scuttle coast location","durotar sunken ships area"}},{q="How does this task relate to the threat at Tiragarde Keep?",a="After clearing out Kul Tiran marines during the assault on Tiragarde Keep, Gar'Thok uses the opportunity to loot the remaining Alliance resources. Stripping the nearby shipwrecks ensures the Horde profits from the enemy's defeat before scavengers or tides take everything.",al={"tiragarde keep connection","vanquish the betrayers link","why do this after tiragarde"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For tinkers, the recovery of Gnomish Tools highlights the early technological friction between Alliance mechanical precision and the burgeoning craft industries of the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="Gar'Thok views every scrap of Alliance metal as a dual prize: knowledge to defeat future invasions and material to help build the nascent nation of Durotar.",["race:Gnome"]="Though small in stature, gnomes leave their mark everywhere the Alliance sails; their sophisticated gear is respected enough by the Horde to warrant dedicated recovery missions."},kw={"durotar","gar'thok","gnomish tools","proudmoore","razor hill","salvage","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep","wreckage"},rel={"npc:gar-thok","quest:784","subzone:scuttle-coast","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:gnome"},m={start="Gar'Thok",level="8",faction="Horde",id=825},src={"From The Wreckage...."}}
E["quest:826"] = {t="quest",n="Zalazane",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village tasks Horde champions with traveling to the Echo Isles to end the treachery of the witch doctor Zalazane. Driven mad by dark magic, Zalazane enslaved his fellow tribesmen and seized the Darkspear trolls' rightful home, forcing them into exile on Durotar's coast.",h="Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village tasks Horde champions with traveling to the Echo Isles to end the treachery...",sec={{t="Betrayal on the Isles",b="When the Darkspear tribe fled their sunken island home and followed Thrall across the Great Sea, they established a settlement on the Echo Isles just off Durotar's southeast coast. Zalazane, a respected and potent witch doctor of the tribe, fell prey to a lust for power. Harnessing mind-enslaving hexes, he subjugated many of his kin and launched a violent uprising. The remaining free Darkspear, led by Vol'jin, were driven from their ancestral camps across the water, forced to build a temporary refuge at Sen'jin Village.",sp=0},{t="A Tribe's Torment",b="Zalazane was not content merely driving the tribe away. From his hilltop redoubt on the central Echo Isle, he regularly sends raiding parties across the channel to snatch more Darkspear and drag them into his thrall. Those afflicted become mindless voodoo and hexed thralls, utterly lost to the tribe. Master Gadrin views this not merely as an occupation of land, but as an existential threat: until Zalazane's severed head is brought before the elders, no Darkspear can ever truly be safe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zalazane?",a="Zalazane was once a prominent witch doctor among the Darkspear trolls. Corrupted by a hunger for dark power, he turned on his brethren, using mind-controlling voodoo to enslave fellow tribespeople and conquer the Echo Isles for himself.",al={"zalazane lore","who is the boss on echo isles","witch doctor zalazane"}},{q="Why did the Darkspear flee the Echo Isles?",a="Zalazane staged a surprise coup d'etat on the islands, turning brothers and sisters into mindless thralls through foul sorcery. Vol'jin and the surviving free Darkspear lacked the numbers to stand against their enchanted kin and retreated to mainland Durotar, founding Sen'jin Village as a temporary refuge.",al={"why are trolls in sen'jin village","echo isles backstory","how did trolls lose echo isles"}},{q="What happens to the trolls under Zalazane's control?",a="The trolls under his sway have their minds completely fractured by powerful hexes. They act purely as Zalazane's mindless servants, patrolling the islands and staging mainland raids to capture more victims. Master Gadrin considers them entirely lost to the tribe, leaving execution as the only mercy.",al={"hexed trolls","voodoo trolls","can zalazane's thralls be cured"}},{q="Where is Zalazane located?",a="Zalazane makes his lair on the largest island of the Echo Isles chain, just east off the southern coast of Durotar. He patrols between the high summit of the central hill down into the cluster of troll huts directly beneath it.",al={"zalazane location","find zalazane","where is zalazane"}},{q="Who gives the quest to kill Zalazane?",a="Master Gadrin, the tribal elder situated in Sen'jin Village on Durotar's southern shore, offers the quest after you complete introductory tasks dealing with local threats and arrive from the Valley of Trials.",al={"who starts zalazane","where to get zalazane quest"}},{q="Why does Vol'jin not lead the assault himself?",a="While Vol'jin rules the tribe and coordinates the Darkspear's defense alongside Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar, Sen'jin Village remains under the local guidance of elders like Master Gadrin. Gadrin coordinates day-to-day survival and enlists capable adventurers to strike back at the treacherous witch doctor.",al={"where is vol'jin","why isn't vol'jin fighting zalazane"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For a Darkspear troll, slaying Zalazane is a deeply personal act of vengeance and duty, punishing the betrayer who stole your people's rightful home and enslaved your brothers.",["faction:Horde"]="The conflict represents one of the young Horde's first major tests of unity, proving that allies from across Durotar will rally to defend the displaced Darkspear tribe.",["class:Shaman"]="Zalazane perverts the spiritual crafts and primal powers practiced by troll shamans and witch doctors, turning binding magics against his own brethren."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","hexed troll","master gadrin","sen'jin village","vol'jin","voodoo troll","zalazane"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:808","topic:darkspear-tribe","npc:vol-jin","zone:durotar","quest:817"},m={start="Master Gadrin",level="10",faction="Horde",id=826},src={"Zalazane (quest)"}}
E["quest:827"] = {t="quest",n="Skull Rock",z="durotar",s="Assigned by the hermit Margoz, this task directs Horde adventurers into the cavern of Skull Rock just east of Orgrimmar. The cave has been overrun by the Burning Blade cult, who use painful demonic devices to bind themselves to dark magic. Securing these cursed artifacts allows Margoz to study the cult's presence right on the capital's doorstep.",h="Assigned by the hermit Margoz, this task directs Horde adventurers into the cavern of Skull Rock just east of...",sec={{t="A Den of Shadows",b="Skull Rock is a forbidding sea cave nestled along the craggy eastern coastline of Durotar. While seemingly isolated, it sits distressingly close to the mighty gates of Orgrimmar. Rather than housing wild beasts or mere outlaws, the caverns harbor a cell of the Burning Blade—the shadowy demonic cult that has long plagued orcish society. Within these dim tunnels, cultists conduct unholy rituals under the nose of the Warchief's scouts.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Attunement",b="The cultists operating within Skull Rock wear Searing Collars, torcs designed to scorch and brand their own flesh. According to Margoz, this self-inflicted torment is far from mindless cruelty; the searing agony and fel sorcery embedded in the metal serve to attune the wearers to demonic power. By recovering these artifacts, Margoz intends to unravel the exact spells and bindings empowering the Burning Blade's ranks.",sp=0},{t="The Looming Threat",b="Uncovering the secret behind the collars confirms that the cult's presence in Durotar is deliberate and organized. The Burning Blade does not simply operate as scattered brigands; their sorceries run deep and pose an active, insidious threat to the newly established Horde territories. Analyzing the collars sets off a chain of inquiries that leads directly into the shadowy circles of Orgrimmar itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Skull Rock located?",a="Skull Rock is a coastal cavern located in northeastern Durotar, tucked along the shoreline east of Orgrimmar and north of Sen'jin Village. It is identified by the craggy cliffside framing the entrance.",al={"skull rock location","where is skull rock","skull rock cave durotar"}},{q="Who is the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade is a dangerous cult of orcs and fel-worshipers dedicated to demonic entities and dark magic. Though the modern Horde broke away from demonic servitude, splinter groups like the Burning Blade continue to practice forbidden rituals to corrupt the Horde from the shadows.",al={"what is burning blade","who are burning blade cultists","burning blade lore"}},{q="What do the cultists use the Searing Collars for?",a="The cultists wear the fiery metal bands around their necks to burn their own flesh. Margoz suspects that this ritualistic pain and demonic enchantment allows them to channel and attune themselves to dark fel energies.",al={"searing collars purpose","why wear searing collars","what are searing collars"}},{q="Who is Margoz?",a="Margoz is an orcish hermit dwelling in a small camp atop the bluffs of Durotar, near Skull Rock. He keeps a watchful eye on cultist movements along the coast and works to dismantle the Burning Blade's dark operations.",al={"who is margoz","margoz durotar","margoz questgiver"}},{q="Why does the Horde allow the cult so close to Orgrimmar?",a="They do not knowingly tolerate it. The cult operates in deep secrecy, hiding within sea caves and desolate ravines where regular patrols rarely reach. Adventurers are sent to investigate precisely because the cultists manage to conceal their footholds until their dark rituals begin.",al={"why is skull rock near orgrimmar","orgrimmar burning blade nearby"}},{q="What happens after Margoz examines the collars?",a="Margoz casts an investigative spell over the gathered collars to divine their origin and magical signature. The magical backlash and revealed secrets urge him to send you into Orgrimmar to seek out others knowledgeable in fel sorcery.",al={"next quest after skull rock","where do collars lead","margoz spell"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The Burning Blade represents the dark past the orcs fight every day to leave behind; purging them from the rocks of Durotar is a matter of survival and honor.",["class:Warlock"]="The Searing Collars demonstrate crude but potent fel bindings, offering dark practitioners a glimpse into how the cult channels demonic sacrifice into raw power.",["faction:Horde"]="A demonic cult festering just outside the walls of Orgrimmar threatens the very heart and security of the young Horde."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","demonic","durotar","fel","margoz","orgrimmar","searing collar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:828","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Margoz",level="12",faction="Horde",id=827},src={"Skull Rock (Classic)"}}
E["quest:828"] = {t="quest",n="Margoz",z="durotar",s="Margoz is a Horde quest tasking adventurers with seeking out an isolated orc shaman who watches over the northern reaches of Durotar. Following the confrontation with fel corruption in the canyon, Orgnil Soulscar directs champions to consult Margoz before assaulting a nearby cultist stronghold. The wise hermit provides crucial counsel regarding the growing shadow cast by the Burning Blade.",h="Margoz is a Horde quest tasking adventurers with seeking out an isolated orc shaman who watches over the...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Vigil",b="After discovering the depths of fel taint at Thunder Ridge, Orgnil Soulscar recognizes that brute strength alone will not suffice to cleanse Durotar. He directs his champions toward Margoz, an experienced orc shaman who keeps a lonely camp in the crags northeast of Razor Hill. Positioned between the jagged heights of Drygulch Ravine and the eastern sea, Margoz keeps watch over dark omens that the bustling warriors of Orgrimmar often overlook.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Skull Rock",b="Margoz possesses crucial intelligence regarding the Burning Blade's true power base in northern Durotar: a concealed cavern system known as Skull Rock, carved directly into the mountain cliffs outside Orgrimmar's southern gates. By conferring with Margoz, travelers learn that the cultists operate far closer to Thrall's capital than the Warchief's guards realize. The shaman ensures that anyone sent to purge the coven does not walk blindly into demonic ambush.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Margoz?",a="Margoz is a wise orc shaman loyal to the Horde who lives in a secluded camp in northeastern Durotar. He studies the movements of dark magic and monitors the demonic corruption spreading through the region.",al={"margoz lore","who is margoz","margoz npc"}},{q="Where do I find Margoz?",a="Margoz is camped out in the rugged hills of northeastern Durotar, situated between Drygulch Ravine and the eastern coastline, just southeast of Orgrimmar.",al={"margoz location","find margoz","where is margoz"}},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar send me to Margoz?",a="Orgnil recognizes that Margoz has spent extensive time studying the local Burning Blade cultists. Before sending you to assault their stronghold, Orgnil wants you to receive Margoz's spiritual wisdom and practical counsel.",al={"why speak with margoz","orgnil soulscar margoz"}},{q="What is Skull Rock?",a="Skull Rock is a hidden mountain cave just south of Orgrimmar's eastern walls. It serves as a fortified coven for the Burning Blade, where demon-worshiping cultists conduct rituals right under the Horde's nose.",al={"skull rock lore","what is skull rock"}},{q="What happens after finding Margoz?",a="Once you report to Margoz, he acknowledges your growing strength and immediately tasks you with entering Skull Rock to slay the cultists and recover their corrupted insignia.",al={"next quest after margoz","margoz follow up"},sp=1},{q="Is Margoz part of the Burning Blade?",a="No. Margoz is a devoted Horde shaman dedicated to purging demonic influence and keeping young champions grounded on an honorable, uncorrupted path.",al={"is margoz evil","is margoz a cultist"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Margoz represents the old, patient wisdom of shamanism, taking watch on the wilderness margins to sense spiritual corruption before it boils over into war.",["faction:Horde"]="Margoz's warning highlights the vulnerability of Orgrimmar, proving that demon cults lurk within striking distance of the Horde's heart.",["race:Orc"]="Meeting Margoz reminds orcish warriors of the lingering temptation of fel power, urging the new generation to walk a pure and honorable path."},kw={"burning blade","drygulch ravine","durotar","margoz","orgnil soulscar","orgrimmar","shaman","skull rock"},rel={"npc:orgnil-soulscar","quest:827","zone:durotar","subzone:drygulch-ravine","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Orgnil Soulscar",["end"]="Margoz",level="12",faction="Horde",id=828},src={"Margoz (Classic)"}}
E["quest:830"] = {t="quest",n="The Admiral's Orders",z="durotar",s="Recovered from a locked strongbox atop Tiragarde Keep, these weathered papers bear the personal seal of the late Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. The recovered orders reveal that the Kul Tiran human garrison along Durotar's coast is far more entrenched and organized than simple shipwreck survivors. Delivering them to Gar'Thok in Razor Hill exposes lingering military plans threatening the fledgling Orc nation.",h="Recovered from a locked strongbox atop Tiragarde Keep, these weathered papers bear the personal seal of the...",sec={{t="A Sealed Legacy",b="Hidden inside a heavy chest on the upper floors of Tiragarde Keep, an aged envelope survives under the watch of Lieutenant Benedict. Sealed with the crest of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, the parchment outlines direct naval commands issued during Kul Tiras's bloody invasion of Durotar. Even after the Grand Admiral fell at Theramore, his officers maintained their fortifications, clinging tightly to their mission to eradicate the Horde settlement.",sp=0},{t="Alarm in Razor Hill",b="Bringing the recovered documents to Gar'Thok, commander of Razor Hill, confirms the worst fears of the local defense force. The human forces entrenched along the eastern shoreline are not aimless castaways, but an established beachhead awaiting reinforcement. Gar'Thok immediately recognizes that dismantling the Tiragarde command structure is an urgent matter of survival for Durotar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the Admiral's Orders found?",a="The orders are found inside an Aged Envelope stored within a locked chest on the third floor of Tiragarde Keep in Durotar. To open the chest, you must first defeat Lieutenant Benedict on the second floor to claim his key.",al={"orders location","where is aged envelope","find admirals orders"}},{q="Who was Admiral Proudmoore?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore was the ruler of Kul Tiras and supreme commander of the Alliance naval fleet during the Second War. Refusing to believe orcs could ever live peacefully, he sailed to Kalimdor to wage a war of extermination against Durotar before meeting his demise at Theramore.",al={"who is the admiral","daelin proudmoore lore","who issued orders"}},{q="Why are Kul Tiran soldiers still in Tiragarde Keep?",a="When Daelin Proudmoore invaded Durotar, he established fortified coastal footholds like Tiragarde Keep. Following his defeat, surviving officers and marines under Lieutenant Benedict held their posts, determined to continue his campaign against the Horde.",al={"why are humans in durotar","tiragarde keep soldiers","kul tiras in durotar"}},{q="Why is Gar'Thok so concerned about these orders?",a="As military commander of Razor Hill, Gar'Thok is tasked with safeguarding central Durotar. Discovering organized naval orders proves that Tiragarde Keep poses an active, calculated military threat to the orcish homeland rather than disorganized, stranded survivors.",al={"gar'thok reaction","why does garthok care"}},{q="Who holds the key to the Admiral's chest?",a="Lieutenant Benedict, the commanding Kul Tiran officer situated on the second level of Tiragarde Keep, carries the key required to unlock the strongbox containing the Aged Envelope.",al={"benedict key","who drops key"}},{q="What happens after giving the orders to Gar'Thok?",a="Upon inspecting the orders, Gar'Thok recognizes the immediate strategic danger and commands further action to neutralize the remaining human leadership and dismantle their operations in Durotar.",al={"admirals orders follow up","next quest"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Uncovering Proudmoore's orders proves that the Alliance presence on Durotar's shores was an orchestrated campaign of extermination, reinforcing why the Horde must defend its newfound home with vigilance.",["race:Orc"]="For the orcs fighting to build a future in Durotar, these documents are a stark reminder of Daelin Proudmoore's relentless hatred and the remnants who still seek their destruction."},kw={"admirals orders","aged envelope","daelin proudmoore","gar'thok","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","razor hill","tiragarde keep"},rel={"npc:gar-thok","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar"},m={start="Aged Envelope",["end"]="Gar'Thok",level="7",faction="Horde",id=830},src={"The Admiral's Orders"}}
E["quest:832"] = {t="quest",n="Burning Shadows",z="durotar",s="Recovered from the Burning Blade cultist Gazz'uz in the depths of Skull Rock, this mysterious glowing pendant whispers urgent warnings into the bearer's mind. The voice specifically threatens Gazz'uz with the wrath of Neeru Fireblade, an orc warlock residing in Orgrimmar.",h="Recovered from the Burning Blade cultist Gazz'uz in the depths of Skull Rock, this mysterious glowing pendant...",sec={{t="A Voice in the Stone",b="Upon slaying Gazz'uz deep within Skull Rock, an ominous pendant known as the Eye of Burning Shadow is retrieved from his remains. Rather than being an inert magical trinket, the stone vibrates with psychic communication. A demanding voice speaks directly into the mind of anyone holding it, demanding reports from Gazz'uz and warning him that his clandestine operations east of Orgrimmar have been compromised.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Threat",b="What catches any loyal Horde scout off guard is the voice's desperate ultimatum: respond, or Neeru Fireblade will be notified to hunt Gazz'uz down with swift brutality. Neeru Fireblade dwells openly in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, ostensibly practicing dark arts under Thrall's strict oversight. Delivering the talisman to Neeru prompts feigned surprise and curiosity, with the warlock marveling that his name was invoked as a boogeyman against the cult.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Eye of Burning Shadow?",a="The Eye of Burning Shadow is an enchanted pendant dropped by the Burning Blade leader Gazz'uz inside Skull Rock. It acts as a two-way telepathic relay between cult operatives and their unseen masters.",al={"eye of burning shadow","what is this pendant","gazz'uz eye"}},{q="Who is speaking through the pendant?",a="An unidentified superior within the Shadow Council or Burning Blade hierarchy is attempting to contact Gazz'uz, unaware that the cultist has already been slain in Skull Rock.",al={"who spoke to me","voice in the pendant","who talks through eye"}},{q="Why does the voice threaten Gazz'uz with Neeru Fireblade?",a="The voice claims Neeru Fireblade will descend upon Gazz'uz with brutal force if he fails to report. On the surface, this frames Neeru as a feared loyal enforcer of Thrall, though the familiarity between the cult and Neeru suggests deeper undercurrents.",al={"why mention neeru","neeru fireblade threat","neeru connection"}},{q="Where do I take the Eye of Burning Shadow?",a="Bring the pendant to Neeru Fireblade, who can be found hovering over cauldrons and tomes deep within the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.",al={"where to turn in burning shadows","where is neeru fireblade"}},{q="How does Neeru Fireblade react when given the eye?",a="Neeru claims ignorance, acting baffled that cultists would invoke his name. He takes the pendant ostensibly to study its magic and uncover why the Burning Blade bears a name so similar to his own clan identity.",al={"neeru reaction","what does neeru say"},sp=1},{q="Where is Gazz'uz located?",a="Gazz'uz lurks at the deepest point of Skull Rock, a cavern hidden along the crags on Durotar's eastern coastline just east of Orgrimmar.",al={"where is gazz'uz","gazz'uz location","skull rock boss"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="For a warlock training in the Cleft of Shadow, witnessing another practitioner's name invoked by the Burning Blade serves as a stark reminder of how thin the line is between state-sanctioned fel study and open treason.",["faction:Horde"]="Uncovering whispers between cultists right outside the capital's gates reveals that the demonic corruption of the Old Horde still festers uncomfortably close to Durotar's heart.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs who fought alongside Thrall to purge the Legion's taint view the Burning Blade's presence in Durotar as an intolerable desecration of their new homeland."},kw={"burning blade","burning shadows","cleft of shadow","durotar","eye of burning shadow","gazz'uz","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:827","quest:829","zone:durotar"},m={start="Eye of Burning Shadow",["end"]="Neeru Fireblade",level="12",faction="Horde",id=832},src={"Burning Shadows"}}
E["quest:834"] = {t="quest",n="Winds in the Desert",z="durotar",s="Rezlak, an engineer contracted from Gazlowe's operations, needs help recovering crucial construction materials stolen by harpies in Durotar. A caravan bound for Orgrimmar was ambushed in Razorwind Canyon, scattering sacks of supplies among the cliffs.",h="Rezlak, an engineer contracted from Gazlowe's operations, needs help recovering crucial construction...",sec={{t="A Goblin on a Deadline",b="Rezlak was sent directly by Chief Engineer Gazlowe of Ratchet to assist the Horde with their ambitious construction projects across Durotar. Building fortifications in harsh, barren terrain is demanding enough without logistical disasters, but Rezlak's shipments keep disappearing before they reach the building sites. Without essential cargo, all progress grinds to a halt, leaving the irritable goblin supervisor stranded with nothing to build with.",sp=0},{t="Ambush in the Canyon",b="The latest vital supply run promised to Rezlak was intercepted by the Dustwind harpies inhabiting Razorwind Canyon. These winged scavengers roost along the high ravine cuts flanking the road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar, swooping down on unsuspecting wagons. Instead of eating or destroying the freight, the harpies hoard the crates and sacks around their nesting sites, leaving the cargo intact for anyone brave enough to fight into their territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is a goblin worker employed by Gazlowe, the boss of Ratchet. Gazlowe sent him to Durotar to assist the orcs with their ongoing construction efforts outside the gates of Orgrimmar.",al={"rezlak","who is rezlak","who gave this quest"}},{q="Why are goblins helping build in Durotar?",a="Gazlowe and the Steamwheedle Cartel have an ongoing commercial and engineering partnership with Warchief Thrall. Goblin engineers and machines helped lay out the foundations of Orgrimmar, and Gazlowe continues to supply contracted labor and materials to the Horde.",al={"why are goblins helping orcs","gazlowe durotar","goblin horde cooperation"}},{q="Where did the supplies come from?",a="The supplies were transported via caravan through Durotar to support regional construction efforts, likely shipped overland through the Southfury river routes or brought north from merchant vessels docked at Ratchet.",al={"where are the supplies from","caravan origin"}},{q="What are the harpies doing in Durotar?",a="The Dustwind harpies are aggressive, predatory scavengers that infest the cliffs and ravines of central Durotar. They harass travelers, raid trade lines through Razorwind Canyon, and scavenge anything bright or useful for their nests.",al={"why harpies in durotar","dustwind harpies lore","razorwind harpies"}},{q="Where is Razorwind Canyon located?",a="Razorwind Canyon branches directly off the main southern gorge that connects Orgrimmar to Razor Hill. Ravines cut into both the eastern and western cliff walls, forming high roosts where the Dustwind harpies stash their stolen cargo.",al={"razorwind canyon location","where to find supplies","sacks of supplies location"}},{q="Why didn't the orc guards protect the caravan?",a="The young Horde's military resources are stretched thin across Durotar, dealing with threats from Centaur raiders, Bristleback quilboar, and Kul Tiras marines along the coast. Guard detachments are often too small to fend off sudden aerial strikes from cliff-dwelling harpies.",al={"why failed caravan","durotar security","orc caravans"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every shipment lost to canyon beasts threatens the rapid expansion and fortification of the Horde's stronghold in Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs rely on goblin expertise and foreign supplies to turn the harsh, dry soil of Durotar into a fortified homeland.",["profession:Engineering"]="Rezlak represents the pragmatic ingenuity of Steamwheedle engineers, who care far more about keeping blueprints and deliveries on schedule than local wildlife troubles."},kw={"caravan","durotar","dustwind harpies","gazlowe","orgrimmar","ratchet","razorwind canyon","rezlak","supplies"},rel={"npc:rezlak","quest:835","subzone:razorwind-canyon","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Rezlak",faction="Horde",id=834},src={"Winds in the Desert"}}
E["quest:835"] = {t="quest",n="Securing the Lines",z="durotar",s="Securing the Lines is a task given by Rezlak near Razorwind Canyon to protect vital goblin supply routes running through Durotar. Harpies roosting in Drygulch Ravine continuously intercept and plunder supply caravans, prompting the frustrated goblin to hire muscle to clear them out.",h="Securing the Lines is a task given by Rezlak near Razorwind Canyon to protect vital goblin supply routes...",sec={{t="A Route Plagued by Harpies",b="The dry valleys of Durotar are harsh enough without aggressive harpies swooping down on unsuspecting travelers. Operating on behalf of his boss Gazlowe, the goblin Rezlak watches over regional supply operations. Unfortunately, the Dustwind harpies inhabiting Drygulch Ravine have turned Razorwind Canyon into a hazard, routinely raiding caravans and seizing incoming shipments before they can reach their destinations.",sp=0},{t="Business and Bloodshed",b="Rezlak lives by the goblin maxim that you can get anything done if the price is right. Rather than personally entering the canyon, he hires adventurers to break the back of the roost by eliminating Dustwind Savages and Dustwind Storm Witches. Clearing these harpies keeps the trade corridors open, secures incoming shipments of engineering gadgets, and points helpful travelers toward greater opportunities in Ratchet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak working for?",a="Rezlak works for Gazlowe, the chief engineer and boss of the neutral goblin port town of Ratchet. Gazlowe oversees extensive commerce and infrastructure projects throughout Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"rezlak boss","who does rezlak work for","rezlak employer"}},{q="Why are the harpies attacking caravans?",a="The Dustwind harpies have established a substantial roost in Drygulch Ravine, which cuts directly alongside the primary transit routes of Razorwind Canyon. They fiercely attack any intruders and plunder the wagons and goods passing nearby.",al={"why do harpies attack","dustwind harpies motive","why drygulch ravine"}},{q="Where is Drygulch Ravine located?",a="Drygulch Ravine is nestled deep within the eastern reaches of Razorwind Canyon in northern Durotar, carved out into the arid crimson hills.",al={"drygulch ravine location","where is drygulch ravine","how to find drygulch"}},{q="What happens after helping Rezlak?",a="With the Dustwind harpies culled and his supply route secured, Rezlak points adventurers toward Ratchet across the border in the Barrens, encouraging them to seek out Gazlowe for further profitable contracts.",al={"after securing the lines","rezlak follow up","what next after rezlak"}},{q="Why doesn't the Horde handle the harpies instead of goblins?",a="While the Horde maintains outposts in Durotar, their resources are stretched thin managing centaur, quilboar, and internal settlement needs. Goblin merchants like Rezlak often find it quicker and cheaper to hire independent adventurers directly to protect their private enterprise.",al={"why goblins hiring","why isn't orgrimmar handling this","horde and harpies"}},{q="What kinds of harpies reside in Drygulch Ravine?",a="The roost primarily consists of feral Dustwind Savages who attack in close combat and Dustwind Storm Witches who command wind and lightning against trespassing caravans.",al={"harpy types","dustwind harpy types","drygulch enemies"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Safeguarding Rezlak's shipments keeps cutting-edge goblin components moving from Ratchet into the hands of local tinkerers.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the harpy menace in eastern Razorwind Canyon preserves the flow of goods and reinforcements between Durotar's frontier outposts and the coastal trade hubs."},kw={"drygulch ravine","dustwind savage","dustwind storm witch","gazlowe","ratchet","razorwind canyon","rezlak","securing the lines"},rel={"npc:rezlak","subzone:drygulch-ravine","subzone:razorwind-canyon","subzone:ratchet","zone:durotar"},m={start="Rezlak",level="11",id=835},src={"Securing the Lines (Classic)"}}
E["quest:8358"] = {t="quest",n="Incoming Gumdrop",z="durotar",s="Incoming Gumdrop is a seasonal Hallow's End quest in Durotar where Kali Remik trades a sweet treat for a bit of playful humiliation. In order to obtain a Darkspear Gumdrop for an ailing orphan, adventurers must play along and mimic the sounds and motion of a steam train.",h="Incoming Gumdrop is a seasonal Hallow's End quest in Durotar where Kali Remik trades a sweet treat for a bit...",sec={{t="A Troll's Price for Candy",b="During the festive season of Hallow's End, heroes across Durotar collect traditional holiday sweets on behalf of a sick child in need of cheer. While Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village is happy to contribute a chewy Darkspear Gumdrop to the cause, she refuses to part with her confection without demanding the customary trick first.",sp=0},{t="Playing the Fool",b="Rather than demanding combat or dangerous trials, Kali asks visiting champions to drop their dignity and perform a train impression on command. Embracing the lighthearted revelry of Hallow's End, seasoned warriors and grim warlocks alike must make chugging engine noises and whistle blows to secure the sweet prize.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kali Remik?",a="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll resident located in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar. During Hallow's End, she holds the Darkspear Gumdrops needed for the holiday festivities.",al={"kali remik","who gives quest","quest giver"}},{q="Why do I need to make a train noise?",a="Hallow's End is built around tricks and treats. Even though the candy is collected for an ailing child, Kali insists on enjoying the holiday tradition by asking you to perform an absurd train impression before handing over the sweet.",al={"why train","train emote","what does she want"}},{q="What is the Darkspear Gumdrop used for?",a="The Darkspear Gumdrop is one of several regional confections gathered across Horde lands to complete a festive assortment of treats intended to lift the spirits of a sick orphan.",al={"what does gumdrop do","darkspear gumdrop use","hallows end treats for spoops"}},{q="Where does this quest fit into the holiday?",a="This quest is only available during the annual Hallow's End celebration, serving as one of the regional errand quests that send Horde players visiting various settlements.",al={"is this seasonal","hallows end quest","holiday event"}},{q="Can Alliance players complete this quest?",a="No, this quest is exclusive to the Horde. Kali Remik is situated in the Darkspear settlement of Sen'jin Village in Durotar and will not offer treats to Alliance adventurers.",al={"alliance version","can alliance do this"}},{q="Where is Kali Remik located?",a="She can be found in Sen'jin Village, situated along the southern coast of Durotar, south of Razor Hill.",al={"kali remik location","where is kali","durotar location"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Visiting Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village gives Darkspear trolls a chance to share holiday revelry on their home shores before heading out to other Horde settlements.",["faction:Horde"]="Gathering seasonal sweets across Durotar, Mulgore, and Tirisfal Glades brings together the disparate cultures of the Horde in a shared, lighthearted tradition."},kw={"darkspear gumdrop","durotar","hallow's end","incoming gumdrop","kali remik","sen'jin village","spoops","train emote"},rel={"npc:kali-remik","zone:durotar"},m={start="Kali Remik",faction="Horde",id=8358},src={"Incoming Gumdrop (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8670"] = {t="quest",n="Runetotem the Elder",z="durotar",s="Runetotem the Elder is an encounter with an ancestral spirit during the Lunar Festival in Durotar. Found standing within Razor Hill under a pillar of heavenly light, she offers blessings and festival tokens to travelers who come to pay their respects to the past.",h="Runetotem the Elder is an encounter with an ancestral spirit during the Lunar Festival in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Spirit in Razor Hill",b="During the Lunar Festival, the spirits of ancient elders materialize across Azeroth to commune with the living. Elder Runetotem manifests inside Razor Hill, positioned just past the southern entrance. Bathed in a clear beam of starlight from above, she watches over the orcish settlement and welcomes adventurers who step aside from their travels to acknowledge the wisdom of those who came before.",sp=0},{t="Guidance Across the Lands",b="Approaching Elder Runetotem does more than honor an individual ancestor. In exchange for your homage, she rewards you with a festival token of fortune and shares word of where other spirits may be found, pointing wanderers toward Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain across the continent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Elder Runetotem located?",a="Elder Runetotem is located inside Razor Hill in Durotar, positioned just to the right immediately after entering through the southern entrance.",al={"elder runetotem location","where is elder runetotem","find elder runetotem"}},{q="Why is there a beam of light shining on her?",a="Like all the ancestral spirits who manifest during the Lunar Festival, Elder Runetotem is highlighted by a celestial shaft of light shining down from the sky, marking her as an honored elder.",al={"light beam elder","why is runetotem glowing","elder beam of light"}},{q="What do you receive for honoring Elder Runetotem?",a="Honoring Elder Runetotem rewards a festival token commemorating your respect for the ancestors, and she offers directions toward other wandering spirits like Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain.",al={"runetotem reward","what does runetotem give","elder runetotem turn in"}},{q="Can Alliance players visit Elder Runetotem?",a="The Lunar Festival elders welcome homage from all mortals regardless of allegiance, though Razor Hill is a heavily guarded Horde outpost, making it perilous for Alliance travelers to approach her.",al={"alliance elder runetotem","can alliance talk to runetotem"}},{q="Which elders does Runetotem mention?",a="Elder Runetotem shares lore on the whereabouts of fellow ancestors, specifically giving guidance on finding Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain.",al={"runetotem directions","who does runetotem tell you to find"}},{q="Is Elder Runetotem a living tauren or a ghost?",a="Elder Runetotem is an ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival season to bestow blessings upon those whose spirits burn with life.",al={"is runetotem dead","is runetotem a ghost"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Meeting a spirit bearing the revered Runetotem family name outside the plains of Mulgore serves as a potent reminder of your people's deep spiritual heritage across Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Standing right inside the walls of Razor Hill, Elder Runetotem is one of the safest and most convenient ancestors for young Horde travelers to honor early in their journeys.",["faction:Alliance"]="Paying homage to Elder Runetotem requires slipping deep behind enemy lines into the heart of Durotar without drawing the wrath of Razor Hill's orcish guards."},kw={"durotar","elder darkhorn","elder high mountain","elder runetotem","lunar festival","razor hill","runetotem"},rel={"npc:elder-runetotem","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Runetotem",id=8670},src={"Runetotem the Elder"}}
E["quest:96652"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="durotar",s="While exploring the rugged wastes of Durotar, travelers stumble across a plain, discarded journal chronicling the quiet travels of an unfamiliar figure. Its pages speak warmly of outdoor life and camping out under the stars, awaiting delivery to Brakk near Razor Hill.",h="While exploring the rugged wastes of Durotar, travelers stumble across a plain, discarded journal chronicling...",sec={{t="A Wanderer's Notes",b="Durotar is a harsh land where survival usually takes precedence over leisurely travel, making the discovery of a wandering chronicler's book an unusual sight. Found lying unattended in the red dirt, the modest journal contains the musings and exploits of someone completely unknown to the common heroes of the Horde. Rather than detailing bloody battles or grand campaigns, its pages dwell on the humble joys of sleeping under the open sky and making camp in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Brakk",b="Whoever penned the entries left enough of an impression—or connection—to point toward Brakk, an orc stationed near the settlement of Razor Hill. Carrying the personal effects of lost travelers to local scouts and encampment hands is often the only way scattered wanderers are ever reunited with their belongings, or at least remembered by those watching the dusty roads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the lost journal?",a="The book is remarkably ordinary, filled with day-to-day entries detailing the quiet exploits of an obscure adventurer. In particular, it repeatedly highlights the simple joys and fun of setting up camp in the wilderness.",al={"what does the journal say","lost journal contents","journal text"}},{q="Who wrote the journal?",a="The identity of the author remains unnamed in the recovered pages; it describes the life and travels of someone you have never heard of before encountering the book in the wilds.",al={"who is the adventurer","author of lost journal","who wrote this book"}},{q="Who is Brakk?",a="Brakk is an orc located near Razor Hill in central Durotar who takes delivery of the lost journal.",al={"brakk razor hill","who is brakk","where is brakk"}},{q="Where is the journal found?",a="The plain journal is discovered lying abandoned amidst the terrain of Durotar, waiting for a passing Horde traveler to recover it.",al={"where do i find the journal","lost journal location","adventurer quest start"}},{q="Why does Brakk care about this journal?",a="Positioned just outside Razor Hill along Durotar's active trails, Brakk serves as a key contact point for items, reports, and wandering business passing through central Horde territory.",al={"why bring it to brakk","brakk purpose","brakk journal"}},{q="Is the adventurer who wrote it in danger?",a="The recovered pages give no indication of foul play, merely containing fond recollections of camping out. However, leaving behind one's travel journal in the red dust of Durotar suggests the writer either dropped it by mistake or moved on unexpectedly.",al={"is the author alive","did the adventurer die","lost adventurer status"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The arid trails of Durotar are walked by many new recruits; retrieving lost property and reporting back to scouts near Razor Hill helps maintain order along the central frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters who spend their lives surviving off the land can easily relate to the journal's fond, repeated entries on the joys of wilderness camping."},kw={"adventurer","brakk","camping","durotar","journal","lost journal","razor hill"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Object #654925",["end"]="Brakk",level="6",faction="Horde",id=96652},src={"The Adventurer (Durotar)"},fv=true}
E["quest:98576"] = {t="quest",n="Glyphic Parchment",z="durotar",s="Glyphic Parchment is an introductory summons directed to aspiring mages in the Valley of Trials. Delivered via Gornek, the written missive guides fledglings toward Mai'ah, a troll mage trainer stationed near the Den, to begin their arcane discipline.",h="Glyphic Parchment is an introductory summons directed to aspiring mages in the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Summons to Study",b="While new recruits prove their physical mettle against the local pests of Durotar, those possessing an affinity for the arcane cannot rely purely on brute force. Gornek passes along a written notice scribed with runes, instructing novice spellcasters to seek out Mai'ah, who oversees the early magical instruction of the Horde's newest recruits.",sp=0},{t="The Way of the Arcane",b="Stationed just outside the entrance to the Den, Mai'ah tempers the ambitions of young spellweavers. Rather than recklessly hurling raw sorcery, she emphasizes patience, timing, and calculated intellect. Under her guidance, novices learn to view the cosmos as delicate strands to weave rather than an unruly tempest to unleash.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Glyphic Parchment?",a="The parchment is sent by Mai'ah, the mage trainer positioned near the Den in the Valley of Trials. Gornek holds the letter and hands it over once a fledgling mage begins their trials.",al={"who wrote glyphic parchment","who sent this","parchment author"}},{q="Where can Mai'ah be found?",a="Mai'ah is located in the Valley of Trials in Durotar, stationed right outside the entrance to the Den alongside other class mentors.",al={"where is maiah","mai'ah location","find mai'ah"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It serves to introduce novice mages to their class trainer. Speaking with Mai'ah initiates your formal instruction in arcane arts, opening access to new spells and foundational training.",al={"what does glyphic parchment do","why do this quest","quest goal"}},{q="What is Mai'ah's philosophy on magic?",a="Mai'ah teaches that arcane magic requires intellect, restraint, and calculated patience. Rather than acting impulsively, an effective mage watches carefully and strikes at the precise moment with the appropriate response.",al={"what does maiah teach","mai'ah lore"}},{q="Why is a troll training mages in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials welcomes both young orcs and Darkspear trolls entering the Horde's ranks. Darkspear spellcasters like Mai'ah lend their wisdom and mastery of cosmic forces to tutor emerging practitioners.",al={"why troll mage","trolls and arcane","troll trainer in orc area"}},{q="Who delivers the parchment to the player?",a="Gornek, the primary trial overseer situated at the central camp of the Valley of Trials, delivers the parchment when you return to him during your early tasks.",al={"who gives glyphic parchment","gornek quest"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="This missive marks your formal recognition as a student of the arcane, directing you to Mai'ah to begin learning and expanding your spellbook.",["faction:Horde"]="Mentorship in the Valley of Trials ensures that even volatile arts like the arcane are cultivated with discipline to strengthen the Horde's future.",["race:Troll"]="Mai'ah represents the Darkspear's growing arcane traditions, offering her cosmic insights to guide both fellow trolls and allied recruits."},kw={"arcane","durotar","glyphic parchment","gornek","mage","mai'ah","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:mai-ah","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:1089"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Mai'ah",level="1",faction="Horde",id=98576},src={"Glyphic Parchment (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["subzone:bladefist-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Bladefist Bay",z="durotar",s="Bladefist Bay is the rugged stretch of coast lining eastern Durotar just outside the gates of Orgrimmar. Named in honor of Kargath Bladefist, the bay serves as a natural harbor facing the Great Sea, shadowed by craggy bluffs and the nearby southern shores of Azshara.",h="Bladefist Bay is the rugged stretch of coast lining eastern Durotar just outside the gates of Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Harbor on the Great Sea",b="Stretching along the northeastern edge of Durotar, Bladefist Bay opens directly into the vast waters of the Great Sea. Flanked by rocky cliffs and treacherous surf, it functions as a primary maritime threshold for the Horde capital of Orgrimmar. The tides frequently deposit driftwood, ocean refuse, and flotsam onto the coastline, earning it a reputation among locals as a natural collection point for ocean debris. Directly north, the ancient red cliffs and ruins of Azshara loom across the water, making the bay a vital maritime boundary for Durotar.",sp=0},{t="Shadow of the Shattered Hand",b="The bay honors Kargath Bladefist, the famed chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan who severed his own hand to replace it with a blade during the old Horde's trials on Draenor. The proximity of the bay to places like Skull Rock—where cultists and hidden rogue networks operate in the shadows—echoes the fierce and ruthless legacy of the clan whose chieftain gave the waters their name.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bladefist Bay named after?",a="The bay is named after Kargath Bladefist, the legendary chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan known for replacing his severed hand with a lethal scythe blade.",al={"who is bladefist","bladefist namesake","kargath bladefist bay"}},{q="Where is Bladefist Bay located?",a="It lies along the northeastern coast of Durotar, directly east of Orgrimmar's main gates and south across the water from Azshara.",al={"bladefist bay location","where is bladefist bay","how to get to bladefist bay"}},{q="What threats lurk around Bladefist Bay?",a="The shoreline is situated right beside Skull Rock, a cavern infamous for harboring warlocks, demons, and members of the sinister Burning Blade cult.",al={"bladefist bay danger","dangers at bladefist bay","enemies in bladefist bay"}},{q="Why is the bay sometimes called a midden heap?",a="Ocean currents from the Great Sea routinely sweep sea detritus, wreckage, and rubble straight onto its shores, giving it a reputation as a dumping ground for the sea's refuse.",al={"midden heap","bladefist flotsam","ocean trash bay"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The bay bears the proud and brutal name of Kargath Bladefist, serving as a reminder of the trials of the Shattered Hand clan on Draenor.",["class:Rogue"]="The Shattered Hand operates within Orgrimmar's shadows as the Horde's guild of thieves and assassins, giving this coast quiet resonance for covert operatives."},kw={"bay","bladefist","durotar","great sea","kargath","orgrimmar","shattered hand","skull rock"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","quest:827","zone:azshara","quest:1858"},src={"Bladefist Bay"}}
E["subzone:burning-blade-coven"] = {t="subzone",n="Burning Blade Coven",z="durotar",s="Tucked into the northern cliffs of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven is an infested cave network threatening the Horde's newest recruits. Corrupted cultists and summoned demons lurk within, turning an old mineral cavern into a staging ground for dark magic right on Durotar's doorstep.",h="Tucked into the northern cliffs of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven is an infested cave network...",sec={{t="A Shadow Over the Proving Grounds",b="The dusty red mountains rimming the Valley of Trials were once simply a testing wilderness for young orcs and Darkspear trolls taking their first steps in service to the Horde. In recent days, however, dark rituals have taken hold of the northern caves. Imps and lesser fiends spill from the cavern mouth, stirring chaos and threatening recruits. Led by the shadowy warlock Yarrog Baneshadow, the Burning Blade cult has entrenched itself deep inside, turning what was once a routine training ground into an active battleground against demonic corruption.",sp=0},{t="Corruption in the Rocks",b="Before the demons took root, the caves attracted the attention of local overseers hoping to harvest raw materials for the settlement. Foreman Thazz'ril ventured deep inside on a mineral survey, only to be driven out in haste, leaving valuable equipment behind as the cultists made their presence known. Now, driving back Baneshadow's coven serves as the ultimate proving trial for aspiring warriors, rogues, and spellcasters before they are deemed ready to venture out into greater Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Burning Blade Coven located?",a="The cave is embedded in the high red rock ridges directly along the northern edge of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",al={"coven location","where is burning blade coven","valley cave location"}},{q="Who leads the cultists here?",a="The coven is led by a warlock named Yarrog Baneshadow, who directs the local rituals and commands the summoned demons.",al={"coven leader","who leads burning blade coven","yarrog"}},{q="What kinds of enemies lurk inside?",a="The cave is infested with rogue imps, minor demonic servitors, and mortal acolytes aligned with the shadowy Burning Blade cult.",al={"what mobs are in the cave","coven monsters","demons in valley of trials"}},{q="Why do new recruits go into the cave?",a="Braving the dark depths of the cave, recovering lost tools like Foreman Thazz'ril's pick, and slaying Yarrog Baneshadow serves as the final initiation rite for new orc and troll adventurers before leaving the valley.",al={"why go to coven","coven purpose","coven final test"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The demonic imps and dark rituals here are an early, cautionary glimpse into what happens when fel power is wielded recklessly in open defiance of the Horde.",["race:Orc"]="The presence of the Burning Blade cult so close to the Valley of Trials is an intolerable insult to Thrall's new Horde and a stark reminder of the demon worship the orcs fought to leave behind."},kw={"burning blade coven","demon","durotar","imps","thazz'ril","valley of trials","yarrog baneshadow"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Burning Blade Coven"}}
E["subzone:darkspear-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkspear Hold",z="durotar",s="Darkspear Hold is the central settlement and redoubt of the Darkspear tribe on Darkspear Isle off the southern coast of Durotar. Today it lies in the grip of the mad witch doctor Zalazane, while Vol'jin and the free Darkspear wait across the water on the mainland.",h="Darkspear Hold is the central settlement and redoubt of the Darkspear tribe on Darkspear Isle off the...",sec={{t="Heart of the Darkspear",b="Perched on the Echo Isles just south of Durotar's mainland, Darkspear Hold represents the hard-won sanctuary of the Darkspear trolls. Having fled their ancestral homeland in the Darkspear Islands under the guidance of the late Sen'jin, the tribe arrived in Kalimdor alongside Thrall's Horde. That refuge was lost when the witch doctor Zalazane enslaved many of the tribe with dark voodoo, forcing Chieftain Vol'jin and the free Darkspear to withdraw to Sen'jin Village on the mainland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darkspear Hold?",a="Darkspear Hold is the primary fortified encampment of the Darkspear tribe, located on Darkspear Isle within the Echo Isles archipelago off the southern coast of Durotar.",al={"darkspear hold lore","what is this place","troll fortress durotar"}},{q="Who rules Darkspear Hold?",a="For now, the mad witch doctor Zalazane holds the Echo Isles with his hexed thralls. The tribe's rightful leader, Chieftain Vol'jin, son of Sen'jin, has led the free Darkspear to Sen'jin Village on the mainland.",al={"who leads darkspear hold","darkspear hold leader","voljin location"}},{q="Why did the Darkspear settle here?",a="After the sea witch drove them from their island home in the Great Sea, the Darkspear traveled west to Kalimdor with Thrall. They claimed the Echo Isles off Durotar as their new home, bound in close alliance to the orcish Horde.",al={"why are trolls in durotar","how did darkspear get here","troll history durotar"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, the Hold is the lost center of tribal sovereignty, which Vol'jin hopes to wrest back from Zalazane for his exiled people.",["faction:Horde"]="The hold anchors the southern approach to Durotar, securing the coastline and cementing the vital bond forged between the trolls and Warchief Thrall."},kw={"darkspear hold","darkspear isle","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin","trolls","vol'jin"},rel={"subzone:darkspear-isle","npc:vol-jin","zone:durotar","topic:horde","npc:thrall","quest:826"},src={"Darkspear Hold"}}
E["subzone:darkspear-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkspear Isle",z="durotar",s="Darkspear Isle is the largest landmass among the Echo Isles off the southeastern coast of Durotar. Originally settled by the Darkspear trolls following their exodus from the South Seas, it currently languishes under the dark hexes of the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane.",h="Darkspear Isle is the largest landmass among the Echo Isles off the southeastern coast of Durotar.",sec={{t="A Lost Sanctuary",b="When Sen'jin fell in the Darkspear Islands and Thrall offered the survivors refuge in Kalimdor, the Darkspear tribe sought a home of their own along the coast of Durotar. They settled the Echo Isles, establishing their primary villages across the archipelago with the largest island as their heart. That refuge was shattered when one of their own prominent witch doctors, Zalazane, went mad with power. Using twisted voodoo, Zalazane enslaved the minds of his fellow tribesfolk, forcing Chieftain Vol'jin and the free Darkspear to flee to the mainland at Sen'jin Village. Today, the island crawls with Zalazane's thralls, savage beasts, and dark rituals.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Isles",b="From the mainland shores, Vol'jin and his remaining advisors direct strikes against the island to disrupt Zalazane's influence and put their enchanted brethren to rest. The Darkspear refuse to abandon their rightful home to a madman. Horde scouts and young warriors regularly cross the water to recover fallen relics, eliminate Zalazane's practitioners, and prepare for the day the tribe can finally purge the traitor and retake their islands for good.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why don't the Darkspear live on the island right now?",a="The witch doctor Zalazane betrayed Chieftain Vol'jin, using powerful dark magic to drive many of the tribesfolk mad and bend them to his will. Vol'jin led the remaining free trolls across the water to Sen'jin Village on the mainland of Durotar to regroup.",al={"why echo isles abandoned","why did trolls leave","darkspear isle empty"}},{q="Who is Zalazane?",a="Zalazane was once a respected witch doctor among the Darkspear tribe. He betrayed his people by tapping into dark voodoo to strip his brethren of their free will, taking command of the Echo Isles and declaring himself master of the islands.",al={"who is zalazane","traitor troll zalazane"}},{q="Is Darkspear Isle part of the Echo Isles?",a="Yes. Darkspear Isle is the largest and central landmass within the tropical archipelago known as the Echo Isles, located just off the southeastern shore of Durotar.",al={"darkspear isle echo isles difference","is darkspear isle in echo isles"}},{q="What can you find on the island currently?",a="The island is currently overrun by Zalazane's hexed troll thralls, aggressive raptors, coastal hexstriders, and hostile tiger and beast populations, along with Zalazane's inner circle of dark practitioners.",al={"what is on darkspear isle","mobs on darkspear isle"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The Echo Isles represent the sanctuary promised to your people by Thrall after the fall of Sen'jin. Seeing your kin enslaved by Zalazane's dark voodoo on your own soil makes reclaiming this island a personal matter of tribal honor.",["faction:Horde"]="The Darkspear are vital allies in Durotar, and Zalazane's rebellion threatens the security of Durotar's southern coastline. Helping Vol'jin strike at the island stabilizes the young Horde's homeland."},kw={"darkspear isle","darkspear tribe","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","vol'jin","voodoo","zalazane"},rel={"subzone:echo-isles","topic:darkspear-tribe","npc:vol-jin","quest:826","quest:808","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:troll"},src={"Darkspear Isle"}}
E["subzone:darkspear-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkspear Strand",z="durotar",s="Darkspear Strand is the stretch of coastline in southern Durotar where the Darkspear trolls washed ashore following their exile from the Echo Isles. Located directly beside Sen'jin Village, this beach marks the bitter beginning of the tribe's mainland refuge under Vol'jin's leadership.",h="Darkspear Strand is the stretch of coastline in southern Durotar where the Darkspear trolls washed ashore...",sec={{t="A Shore of Exile",b="When the witch doctor Zalazane went mad and seized control of the Echo Isles, the surviving Darkspear trolls were forced to abandon their offshore home. Desperate refugees crossed the narrow waters and landed along this sun-bleached coast. Rather than scatter into the hostile red wastes of Durotar, the survivors banded together just yards inland from the shoreline to construct Sen'jin Village. Today, the strand serves as a quiet reminder of their displacement, looking out across the surf toward the islands they still hope to reclaim.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened at Darkspear Strand?",a="This coastline is where the Darkspear trolls made landfall after fleeing the Echo Isles. When Zalazane turned his dark magic against his own people, the survivors evacuated across the water and came ashore here, immediately gathering nearby to establish Sen'jin Village.",al={"why is it called darkspear strand","darkspear strand lore","what is this beach"}},{q="Why did the Darkspear leave the Echo Isles?",a="The witch doctor Zalazane betrayed his kin and used dark voodoo to enslave the minds of his fellow tribesfolk. Chief Vol'jin led the remaining uncorrupted Darkspear off the islands to escape total subjugation, landing on this strand.",al={"why did trolls leave echo isles","zalazane exile","echo isles evacuation"}},{q="What settlement is located next to Darkspear Strand?",a="Sen'jin Village sits just yards inland from the beach. It was established by the refugees immediately after landing on the strand and serves as the primary Darkspear outpost and spiritual center in Durotar.",al={"village near darkspear strand","town next to beach","sen'jin village location"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, stepping onto this shore carries the sting of Zalazane's betrayal and the bittersweet memory of escaping with their lives to found Sen'jin Village.",["faction:Horde"]="The strand marks the southern coast where the Darkspear cemented their place on the Kalimdor mainland beside their Orc allies after losing their island settlement."},kw={"darkspear","darkspear strand","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Darkspear Strand"}}
E["subzone:deadeye-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Deadeye Shore",z="durotar",s="Deadeye Shore is a windswept stretch of coastline along Durotar's eastern edge, directly east of Drygulch Ravine. Named in memory of the legendary Bleeding Hollow chieftain Kilrogg Deadeye, the barren sands are roamed primarily by wild raptors, scorpids, and feral boars.",h="Deadeye Shore is a windswept stretch of coastline along Durotar's eastern edge, directly east of Drygulch...",sec={{t="A Shoreline of the Bleeding Hollow",b="Stretching beneath the red bluffs of central Durotar, Deadeye Shore takes its name from Kilrogg Deadeye, the one-eyed chieftain of the Bleeding Hollow clan who fought in the First and Second Wars. From high above, the sand and rocky outcrops faintly mirror the shape of a skull with a missing eye socket. While lacking major settlements or military outposts, the shoreline is far from peaceful: aggressive wildlife dominates the sands, and shadowy cultists from the Burning Blade have been known to prowl down toward the water from their nearby hideouts in the ravines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Deadeye Shore?",a="The shoreline is named after Kilrogg Deadeye, the famed chieftain of the Bleeding Hollow clan. The natural coastal terrain also resembles a skull missing an eye, echoing the chieftain's own blinded socket.",al={"who is deadeye","why deadeye shore","origin of name"}},{q="Who lives along Deadeye Shore?",a="No permanent settlements stand on Deadeye Shore. The stretch of coast is inhabited primarily by native wildlife like raptors, scorpids, and boars, though fishermen and travelers occasionally pass through—sometimes running afoul of hidden Burning Blade cultists.",al={"who is here","settlements deadeye shore","npcs deadeye"}},{q="What threats are found around Deadeye Shore?",a="Beyond aggressive local beasts, the greatest danger comes from the neighboring Drygulch Ravine. Cultists belonging to the Burning Blade occasionally wander down from the rocky canyons toward the coast, ambushing unwary travelers and fishermen.",al={"dangers deadeye shore","enemies here","burning blade deadeye"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For orcs establishing their new nation in Durotar, the shore honors Kilrogg Deadeye, reminding them of the old chieftains who shaped the Horde's history during the wars on Azeroth."},kw={"bleeding hollow","deadeye shore","drygulch ravine","durotar","kilrogg deadeye"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:drygulch-ravine"},src={"Deadeye Shore"}}
E["subzone:drygulch-ravine"] = {t="subzone",n="Drygulch Ravine",z="durotar",s="Drygulch Ravine is a rugged, hidden gorge tucked into the rocky bluffs of eastern Durotar. Accessible only through an obscure cave passage from Razorwind Canyon or a perilous drop from above, this craggy trench is overrun by nesting Dustwind harpies who menace nearby supply caravans.",h="Drygulch Ravine is a rugged, hidden gorge tucked into the rocky bluffs of eastern Durotar.",sec={{t="A Bandit Haven in the Red Rocks",b="Carved deep into the crags east of Orgrimmar, Drygulch Ravine is almost entirely cut off from casual travel. Its only ground-level access is a cramped natural tunnel connected to Razorwind Canyon. Fed by a modest river, this sheltered depression once saw peaceful orc habitation, but wild beasts and roosting Dustwind harpies have turned it into a lawless pocket of Durotar. The winged scavengers use the steep cliff faces to nest their broods and stockpile stolen goods taken from Horde supply trains passing along the regional trails.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="Life in Drygulch Ravine has long been precarious. Not long after the Third War, escaped thunder lizards from Thunder Ridge threatened the area, prompting warnings to Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar. Today, the harpies pose the immediate danger. Their matriarchs fiercely defend clutches of eggs tucked along the high ledges, and Horde scouts frequently dispatch young warriors to cull the flock, recover plundered trade crates, and break the harpies' grip on the ravine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get into Drygulch Ravine?",a="Unless you survive a leap from the high cliffs above, the only ground route is through a small cave entrance tucked within neighboring Razorwind Canyon.",al={"drygulch entrance","how to enter drygulch","where is the cave to drygulch"}},{q="What creatures live in Drygulch Ravine?",a="The ravine is dominated by Dustwind harpies who build their nests, lay eggs, and stash looted caravan supplies along the craggy rock shelves.",al={"drygulch mobs","what is in drygulch ravine","who lives in drygulch"}},{q="Why does the Horde care about this ravine?",a="The Dustwind harpies raid Durotar's vital trade trails, hoarding stolen cargo in the gorge. Horde authorities in Razor Hill regularly send recruits to recover provisions and cull the flock.",al={"why kill harpies drygulch","drygulch ravine quests","horde interest in drygulch"}},{q="Did thunder lizards once attack the ravine?",a="Yes. A few years after the Third War, agitated thunder lizards broke out of nearby Thunder Ridge and threatened Drygulch Ravine, forcing local orcs to seek military aid from Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar.",al={"thunder lizards drygulch","drygulch history lizards"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the ravine's roosts and recovering stolen supplies helps secure Durotar's internal trade routes against constant banditry.",["race:Orc"]="Drygulch Ravine stands as a test of frontier endurance, where young orcs prove their mettle against the ferocious harpies perched on the homeland's rocky bluffs."},kw={"drygulch ravine","durotar","dustwind harpies","harpy nests","orgrimmar","razorwind canyon","stolen supplies","thunder ridge"},rel={"subzone:razorwind-canyon","subzone:thunder-ridge","quest:834","quest:835","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","npc:thrall","topic:third-war"},src={"Drygulch Ravine"}}
E["subzone:dustwind-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustwind Cave",z="durotar",s="Dustwind Cave is a secluded hollow perched atop the cliffs of Razorwind Canyon, just northeast of Razor Hill. It serves as an active training ground and covert sanctuary for initiates of the nefarious Burning Blade cult operating within Durotar.",h="Dustwind Cave is a secluded hollow perched atop the cliffs of Razorwind Canyon, just northeast of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Shadow in the Cliffs",b="Overlooking Razorwind Canyon, Dustwind Cave is one of the closest and most perilous threats to Razor Hill. While many assume demonic cultists gather only in deep subterranean depths, here the Burning Blade trains fresh recruits right under the noses of the Horde authorities. Shadowy cultists tutor initiates in forbidden dark magics and demonology, preparing them to undermine the young orcish realm from within Durotar's own borders.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Bloodlines",b="Those who trespass into the cave risk exposure to the cultists' dangerous corruptions. Practitioners inside channel volatile dark arts such as felblood afflictions, demonstrating how deeply the Burning Blade clings to the demonic legacy Thrall fought so hard to banish. Eliminating the cabal here is vital for maintaining the precarious peace of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Dustwind Cave located?",a="Dustwind Cave is situated high along the clifftops of Razorwind Canyon, directly northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar.",al={"dustwind cave location","where is dustwind cave","how to find dustwind cave"}},{q="Who occupies Dustwind Cave?",a="The cave is occupied by cultists and initiates of the Burning Blade, a shadowy demonic cult dedicated to spreading fel corruption and destabilizing the Horde.",al={"who is in dustwind cave","dustwind cave enemies","mobs in dustwind cave"}},{q="Why is the Burning Blade operating here?",a="The Burning Blade uses Dustwind Cave as a secluded training outpost where seasoned cultists instruct new recruits in demonic arts away from the immediate gaze of the Orgrimmar and Razor Hill guards.",al={"why are cultists in dustwind cave","burning blade purpose durotar"}},{q="Why does the Horde want this cave cleared?",a="Having demon-worshiping cultists lurking just steps away from Razor Hill poses an unacceptable security risk to traveling recruits and the overall defense of Durotar.",al={"why clear dustwind cave","horde threat dustwind cave"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks of the Horde will recognize the dark rituals taking place within Dustwind Cave, though the Burning Blade wields their fel gifts toward rebellion rather than the service of Thrall's new order.",["faction:Horde"]="Dustwind Cave represents an embarrassing and dangerous internal breach, harboring demon cultists within shouting distance of Razor Hill."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","durotar","dustwind cave","felblood","razor hill","razorwind canyon"},rel={"subzone:razorwind-canyon","subzone:razor-hill","quest:827","zone:durotar"},src={"Dustwind Cave"}}
E["subzone:echo-isles"] = {t="subzone",n="Echo Isles",z="durotar",s="The Echo Isles are a cluster of tropical islands lying just off the southeastern coast of Durotar. Originally settled by the Darkspear trolls after fleeing their ancestral islands, the archipelago is currently lost to the rogue witch doctor Zalazane, who drove his people into exile with dark magic and enslaved minions.",h="The Echo Isles are a cluster of tropical islands lying just off the southeastern coast of Durotar.",sec={{t="A Fractured Sanctuary",b="Following their flight across the Great Sea alongside Thrall, the Darkspear tribe claimed the Echo Isles as their new home. Their peace was repeatedly shattered: first by the naval forces of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore during Kul Tiras' invasion of Durotar, and later from within. Shortly after the trolls drove back Proudmoore's fleet, one of their own witch doctors, Zalazane, seized dark arts to enslave the minds of his kin. Chieftain Vol'jin and the free Darkspears were forced to abandon the islands once more, seeking temporary refuge across the narrow strait at Sen'jin Village.",sp=0},{t="Zalazane's Grip",b="Today, the tropical cluster is overrun by aggressive predators, tainted wildlife, and the thralls of Zalazane. Using malevolent hexes, voodoo fetishes, and ju-ju heaps placed throughout the islands, the traitorous witch doctor bends beasts and captive trolls to his will. From their encampment at Darkspear Strand, Vol'jin's scouts and warriors mount frequent sorties into the islands, determined to recover the remains of their fallen and strike down the mad mystic who stole their home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why don't the Darkspear trolls live here right now?",a="The witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the tribe, using dark magic to strip his brethren of their free will and twist them into obedient servitors. Chieftain Vol'jin ordered an evacuation to the mainland coast of Durotar, founding Sen'jin Village as a staging ground while the tribe fights to reclaim their home.",al={"why abandoned","why did trolls leave","troll home"}},{q="Who is Zalazane?",a="Zalazane is a traitorous Darkspear witch doctor who turned on his tribe. Using powerful voodoo and dark magic, he placed hexes over the islands, corrupted the local wildlife, and enslaved fellow trolls into mindless thralls.",al={"who is zalazane","boss on echo isles","witch doctor zalazane"}},{q="What threats are on the islands?",a="The archipelago is infested with wild raptors, tigers, and corrupted beasts, as well as Zalazane's voodoo heaps and his mind-controlled troll minions, including hexed and voodoo trolls.",al={"echo isles mobs","what is on the islands","echo isles dangers"}},{q="How did the Darkspear tribe end up on these islands originally?",a="After Thrall and the Horde rescued the Darkspear tribe from a sinking island and hostile naga in the Great Sea, the trolls journeyed to Kalimdor and were granted the Echo Isles to settle alongside their orc allies.",al={"how did trolls get here","darkspear origin","echo isles history"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The Echo Isles represent both the promised home of the Darkspear in Kalimdor and the bitter sting of Zalazane's betrayal. Reclaiming them is a matter of tribal survival and personal honor.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the Echo Isles is essential for stabilizing the southern coast of Durotar, protecting Sen'jin Village, and consolidating the young Horde's borders against naval threats and rogue mystics."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","trolls","vol'jin","voodoo","zalazane"},rel={"topic:darkspear-tribe","quest:826","npc:vol-jin","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","subzone:darkspear-strand","quest:808","topic:kul-tiras"},src={"Echo Isles"}}
E["subzone:hidden-path"] = {t="subzone",n="Hidden Path",z="durotar",s="The Hidden Path is a secluded mountain trail winding through the crags above the Valley of Trials in Durotar. It serves as a rite of passage for aspiring shaman seeking the sacred Spirit Rock, while offering an overlooked vantage overlooking the rugged borders of the Barrens.",h="The Hidden Path is a secluded mountain trail winding through the crags above the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Sacred Ascent",b="Carved into the red peaks bordering the Valley of Trials, the Hidden Path is intentionally difficult to spot from the canyon floor. Young shaman are directed here by their mentors to prove their awareness and discipline before communing with the spirits at Spirit Rock. Along the trail's highest reaches, travelers are treated to expansive panoramic views stretching westward toward the rolling savannas of the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Strategic Vulnerability",b="Beyond its spiritual importance, the path cuts a precarious breach through the natural fortifications enclosing the valley. A low pass along the route provides a direct back door toward Ratchet and the road to Orgrimmar. Because it circumvents the standard canyon checkpoints, vigilant defenders fear that bold Alliance infiltrators could exploit this quiet trail to slip directly into the Horde's primary proving grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Hidden Path lead?",a="The path ascends from the Valley of Trials up into the crags to Spirit Rock, a sacred site where shaman commune with the elements. It also winds along mountain passes that connect toward the Barrens and the coastline.",al={"hidden path destination","where does hidden path go","hidden path leads to"}},{q="Why is the path significant to shaman?",a="Initiate shaman in the Valley of Trials are tasked with locating this secluded trail as part of their early elemental trials. Climbing the path allows them to reach the Spirit Rock and drink the Sapta required to commune with the spirits.",al={"shaman path valley of trials","spirit rock path","shaman quest path"}},{q="Could enemies use the Hidden Path to attack the Valley of Trials?",a="Yes. The low gaps along the path bypass the standard guarded entrances to the valley. A cunning Alliance strike force coming from Ratchet or the coast could theoretically use the trail to bypass Horde scouts and enter the training grounds undetected.",al={"hidden path alliance invasion","is valley of trials vulnerable","valley of trials back door"}},{q="What can you see from the top of the path?",a="At its highest point, the trail offers a clear, elevated view looking west toward the vast plains of the Barrens, as well as sweeping views across the red canyons of Durotar.",al={"hidden path view","lookout point hidden path"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The Hidden Path is your first true physical and spiritual climb, testing your perception before you commune with the earth spirits at Spirit Rock.",["faction:Horde"]="Though sacred to shaman, this unfortified passage represents a security blind spot above the Valley of Trials that warrants a watchful eye."},kw={"barrens","durotar","hidden path","shaman","spirit rock","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:spirit-rock","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","topic:alliance","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Hidden Path"}}
E["subzone:jaggedswine-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Jaggedswine Farm",z="durotar",s="Jaggedswine Farm is a modest livestock steading situated in northern Durotar, just south of the main entrance to Orgrimmar. Comprising a timber storage shed, a sprawling pen, and a muddy watering hole, it serves as a critical food source raising hardy swine for the nearby Horde capital.",h="Jaggedswine Farm is a modest livestock steading situated in northern Durotar, just south of the main entrance...",sec={{t="Provisions for the Capital",b="Carved out of Durotar's unforgiving, sunbaked earth, Jaggedswine Farm represents the harsh reality of sustaining an urban stronghold like Orgrimmar. The red soil of the region yields sparse agriculture, making robust livestock essential to feeding thousands of orcish warriors and laborers. The farm centers on a timber storehouse, a wide wooden pen, and a natural watering pond where swine are herded, bred, and butchered to keep the Horde's granaries stocked.",sp=0},{t="A Quiet Frontier",b="Though quiet and often appearing half-tended under the dry heat, the farm is a regular stomping ground for local swineherds and patrolling Orgrimmar Grunts. Wild and mature swine roam both inside and outside the enclosures, occasionally testing the patience of nearby guards. Sitting right on the threshold of the capital's valley approach, the plot remains an unassuming yet indispensable outpost in the daily logistics of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Jaggedswine Farm?",a="The farm raises and maintains swine to provide meat and lard for the Horde, particularly to feed the population and garrison of nearby Orgrimmar.",al={"what is jaggedswine farm","why is there a pig farm in durotar","jaggedswine farm purpose"}},{q="Where exactly is Jaggedswine Farm located?",a="It lies in northern Durotar, sitting just outside the southern approach and grand gates that lead into the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar.",al={"where is jaggedswine farm","how to get to jaggedswine farm","pig farm durotar location"}},{q="Why does the farm look somewhat deserted?",a="Orcish livestock farming in Durotar is utilitarian and unglamorous. Between free-roaming boars and sparse timber structures, the steading lacks grand homesteads, but it remains actively used by Horde supply lines.",al={"is jaggedswine farm abandoned","who lives at jaggedswine farm","why no farmers"}},{q="Are the pigs here dangerous to travelers?",a="While the domesticated swine inside the pens are docile, wild and mature boars roaming the outskirts can be aggressive if startled by young travelers or careless foragers.",al={"are swine hostile","do pigs attack here","swine dangerous"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For Horde cooks learning their trade in Durotar, the abundant swine around Jaggedswine Farm make it a primary local source for tender ribs, pork cuts, and cooking grease.",["faction:Horde"]="Establishing stable meat supplies in the arid wastes of Durotar is a matter of survival, making outposts like Jaggedswine vital to sustaining Orgrimmar's military strength."},kw={"boars","durotar","horde provisions","jaggedswine farm","orgrimmar","pig pen","pigs","swine"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:gates-of-orgrimmar","topic:horde"},src={"Jaggedswine Farm"}}
E["subzone:kolkar-crag"] = {t="subzone",n="Kolkar Crag",z="durotar",s="Kolkar Crag is a sunbaked, jagged gorge in southern Durotar claimed by the hostile Kolkar centaur. Led by Warlord Kolkanis, this enclave serves as a staging ground for coordinated raids against nearby Horde settlements.",h="Kolkar Crag is a sunbaked, jagged gorge in southern Durotar claimed by the hostile Kolkar centaur.",sec={{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="Tucked away in the rugged canyons of southern Durotar, Kolkar Crag is a base of operations for the aggressive Kolkar clan. Despite the arid and unforgiving terrain, these centaur have fortified the natural choke points of the gorge. From this ravine, their scouts and marauders keep close watch over the surrounding flats, probing for vulnerabilities across orc and Darkspear holdings. For young warriors training in the Valley of Trials or patrolling the southern coast, Kolkar Crag represents the nearest organized front of centaur hostility.",sp=0},{t="Schemes of Invasion",b="Under the command of Warlord Kolkanis, the centaur entrenched at the crag hold ambitions far beyond simple skirmishes. Recovered attack plans reveal plots targeting the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and daring strikes aimed directly toward the gates of Orgrimmar. Halting these plans requires decisive preemptive strikes deep into the ravine to assassinate Kolkanis and break their muster before their war parties can sweep through the valleys.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives in Kolkar Crag?",a="Kolkar Crag is held by the Kolkar centaur clan, led on-site by Warlord Kolkanis. They use the defensible canyon as a camp and raiding post against Horde outposts throughout Durotar.",al={"who is at kolkar crag","kolkar crag inhabitants","who owns kolkar crag"}},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about this ravine?",a="The centaur within the gorge have drafted plans to launch coordinated assaults on Durotar's vital settlements, including the training grounds in the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and Orgrimmar itself.",al={"why care about kolkar crag","is kolkar crag dangerous","kolkar threat"}},{q="Who leads the centaur here?",a="The encampment is commanded by Warlord Kolkanis, a ferocious centaur warlord who directs their scouting maneuvers and formulates battle plans against the orcs and trolls.",al={"kolkar crag boss","who leads kolkar crag","warlord kolkanis"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The presence of centaur so close to the Valley of Trials threatens the initiation of young orcs, making the pacification of Kolkar Crag an urgent matter of territorial defense.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing southern Durotar against centaur incursions protects the supply lines running between Sen'jin Village and the road to Orgrimmar."},kw={"centaur","durotar","kolkanis","kolkar","kolkar crag","sen'jin village","valley of trials","warlord kolkanis"},rel={"quest:786","topic:centaur","zone:durotar","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Kolkar Crag"}}
E["subzone:orgrimmar"] = {t="subzone",n="Orgrimmar",z="durotar",s="Orgrimmar is the formidable warrior capital of the New Horde, carved into the winding red canyons of northern Durotar. Founded by Warchief Thrall and named in memory of Orgrim Doomhammer, it serves as the beating heart of orcish renewal and intertribal survival on Kalimdor.",h="Orgrimmar is the formidable warrior capital of the New Horde, carved into the winding red canyons of northern...",sec={{t="A Stronghold in the Stone",b="Following the Third War and the victory at Mount Hyjal, Warchief Thrall brought his surviving people south to establish a permanent homeland in Durotar. Nestled into a natural barrier of sheer mountain crags, Orgrimmar was engineered to withstand siege, boasting spiked timber palisades, stone watchtowers, and deep mountain-carved caverns. Built in cooperation with the Darkspear trolls, tauren stonemasons, and goblin engineers, the fortress turned a desolate wilderness into an unassailable bastion of strength.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the New Horde",b="Free of the demonic bloodlust that once bound them, the orcs built Orgrimmar as a beacon of honor, community, and survival. Today in 25 ADP, the city houses not only orcs and Darkspear trolls, but also welcomes emissaries from the tauren of Mulgore and emissaries from the newly allied Forsaken. Within its fortified canyons, shamans instruct the next generation in ancestral balance, while veterans clash in gladiatorial rings to hone the army that shields the fragile peace of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orgrimmar named after?",a="Warchief Thrall named the city in honor of his mentor and predecessor, the legendary orc Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. Doomhammer fell in the Eastern Kingdoms during the liberation of the orc internment camps, bestowing his iconic warplate and battle hammer onto Thrall.",al={"orgrimmar name origin","why called orgrimmar","who was orgrimmar named for"}},{q="Who helped build the city?",a="The capital was raised rapidly through the joint effort of orcs, the Darkspear trolls, the tauren, hired goblin sappers and engineers, and the wandering champion Rexxar. Its natural stone walls were excavated and fortified to provide swift, defensible shelter in the harsh terrain of Durotar.",al={"who built orgrimmar","how was orgrimmar made","orgrimmar builders"}},{q="Which races call Orgrimmar home?",a="Orgrimmar is primarily inhabited by the orcs and Sen'jin's Darkspear trolls, who share its districts. Tauren travelers frequently reside in the city as steadfast allies, and envoys of the recently accepted Forsaken have begun establishing a quiet foothold alongside them.",al={"who lives in orgrimmar","orgrimmar residents","races in orgrimmar"}},{q="Where does Warchief Thrall reside?",a="Thrall presides over the New Horde from Grommash Hold, a central stronghold located in the Valley of Wisdom within Orgrimmar, named to honor his fallen friend, Grom Hellscream.",al={"where is thrall","thrall location orgrimmar","warchief seat"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As the supreme seat of Horde leadership, Orgrimmar is the central staging ground for military campaigns, clan alliances, and diplomatic relations across Kalimdor and beyond.",["race:Orc"]="For the orcs, Orgrimmar is the realization of their redemption, where they cast off the legacy of the demonic curse to build an honorable, independent future."},kw={"darkspear","doomhammer","durotar","grommash hold","new horde","orgrimmar","tauren","thrall"},rel={"zone:durotar","npc:thrall","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:grommash-hold","subzone:drag","topic:new-horde","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:tauren"},src={"Orgrimmar"}}
E["subzone:razor-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Razor Hill",z="durotar",s="Razor Hill is the principal Horde settlement in central Durotar, nestled at the strategic crossroads between the Valley of Trials, the Barrens, and Orgrimmar. Centered around a prominent fortified barracks, it serves as the staging ground and training center for young orc and troll warriors testing their mettle in the harsh wilderness.",h="Razor Hill is the principal Horde settlement in central Durotar, nestled at the strategic crossroads between...",sec={{t="Heart of Durotar",b="Built at a vital geographical junction, Razor Hill connects northern Durotar with the coastal settlements to the south and the sprawling plains of the Barrens across the Southfury River. Dominated by its stone-and-timber barracks and classic orcish burrows, the settlement was established early in the founding of Durotar. Shortly after the Third War, human forces from Kul Tiras lured the Horde into an ambush here under the guise of an emissary summit, an assault thwarted when Rexxar went in Thrall's stead. Today, the outpost stands fully fortified against further coastal incursions.",sp=0},{t="Watch on the Frontier",b="Under the command of veteran officers like Gar'Thok, Razor Hill coordinates local defense against several looming threats. Human marine remnants still hold Tiragarde Keep along the eastern shoreline, while aggressive quilboar and harpy tribes harass local supply lines. Far more insidious is the presence of the Burning Blade cult, whose shadowy rituals and corrupted agents in the nearby crags are closely tracked and stamped out by investigators like Orgnil Soulscar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Razor Hill's purpose in Durotar?",a="Razor Hill serves as the main administrative and defensive outpost in central Durotar. It connects the southern shores and the Valley of Trials to Orgrimmar in the north and the Barrens to the west, while providing supplies and training for young adventurers.",al={"why is razor hill here","razor hill purpose","what is razor hill"}},{q="What happened here during the Kul Tiras invasion?",a="Following the Third War, forces loyal to Kul Tiras offered a peaceful summit with Warchief Thrall at Razor Hill. Suspecting treachery, the champion Rexxar went in Thrall's place, uncovered an ambush, and defeated the human assassins.",al={"kul tiras ambush","rexxar razor hill","what happened at razor hill summit"}},{q="Who commands the settlement?",a="The settlement's garrison is commanded by the orc veteran Gar'Thok from within the town's barracks, overseeing patrols against human remnants and local wild beasts.",al={"razor hill leader","who runs razor hill","gar'thok"}},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing near Razor Hill?",a="The shadowy demonic cult has infiltrated hidden crags and canyons around central Durotar. Horde scouts, directed by Orgnil Soulscar, work out of Razor Hill to uncover their covens and eliminate their influence.",al={"burning blade durotar","orgnil soulscar","cultists near razor hill"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As the first true town encountered after leaving the training grounds, Razor Hill serves as the launchpad for young Horde soldiers proving their loyalty to Thrall's new nation.",["race:Orc"]="Razor Hill stands as a testament to the new life orcs have carved out in Durotar, trading demonic servitude for sturdy burrows and hard-won survival."},kw={"barracks","burning blade","durotar","gar'thok","kul tiras","orgnil soulscar","razor hill"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:tiragarde-keep","npc:gar-thok","npc:orgnil-soulscar","zone:barrens"},src={"Razor Hill"}}
E["subzone:razor-hill-watchtower"] = {t="subzone",n="Razor Hill Watchtower",z="durotar",s="Perched on the red stone bluffs overlooking Razor Hill, this sturdy outpost serves as an early warning post for the heart of Durotar. Sentries stationed here keep a vigilant eye across the dusty plains and toward the coast, safeguarding the settlement below from encroaching threats.",h="Perched on the red stone bluffs overlooking Razor Hill, this sturdy outpost serves as an early warning post...",sec={{t="Eyes Over Durotar",b="Constructed from thick timber and iron framing, the Razor Hill Watchtower guards the settlement of Razor Hill and the surrounding canyons. Durotar faces relentless threats from Kul Tiras marines along the eastern shore, quillboar raiders prowling the scrublands, and Burning Blade cultists lurking in nearby crags. From this elevated vantage point atop the ridgeline, Horde sentries can spot approaching warbands, smoke signals, and incursions long before they reach the settlement gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Razor Hill Watchtower?",a="The watchtower serves as the primary lookout post for Razor Hill and central Durotar. Its high elevation allows scouts to monitor the trails, watch for hostile beasts, and detect any troop movements from nearby Alliance encampments or centaur raiding parties.",al={"why is the watchtower here","watchtower purpose","razor hill tower"}},{q="Who guards the watchtower?",a="Horde sentries and scouts are stationed here on rotation from Razor Hill. They keep watch over the surrounding red ravines and stand ready to sound the alarm if the town below is threatened.",al={"who is at the tower","watchtower guards"}},{q="What threats can be seen from up here?",a="Scouts primarily keep watch for aggressive quillboar from the Razormane tribes, human infiltrators from Tiragarde Keep along the eastern coast, and wild beasts roaming the dry valleys.",al={"threats to razor hill","what are they looking for"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For young warriors and scouts emerging from the Valley of Trials, the watchtower is a reassuring landmark signaling the safety and strength of the fledgling Horde.",["class:Hunter"]="The high vantage point offers an unobstructed view of the surrounding crags, ideal for spotters tracking quarry and tracking beast movements across Durotar."},kw={"durotar","lookout","razor hill","razor hill watchtower","sentry","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Razor Hill Watchtower"}}
E["subzone:razormane-grounds"] = {t="subzone",n="Razormane Grounds",z="durotar",s="The Razormane Grounds form the forward encampment of the Razormane quilboar pushing eastward from the Barrens into central Durotar. Choked with sharp briars and the stripped carcasses of wild game, this bristling outpost serves as the frontline in the quilboars' unending clash with the orcs of Orgrimmar.",h="The Razormane Grounds form the forward encampment of the Razormane quilboar pushing eastward from the Barrens...",sec={{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="Sprawling beneath the red cliffs of central Durotar, the Razormane Grounds mark the furthest eastern reach of quilboar expansion out of the Barrens. Entangled within thick brambles and surrounded by bleached bones, the encampment poses a constant danger to travelers along the Southfury River. The camp is led by figures such as Captain Flat Tusk of the Battleguard and Geolord Mottle, who orchestrate raids against neighboring orc settlements and passing supply lines. Despite regular patrols dispatched from Razor Hill and nearby outposts, the Razormane replenish their ranks tirelessly, sprouting from the briars faster than the Horde can clear them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Razormane Grounds?",a="It is a fortified quilboar encampment in central Durotar, acting as a forward base for the Razormane tribe as they expand eastward from the Barrens.",al={"razormane grounds","quilboar camp durotar","where are razormane"}},{q="Why are the quilboar attacking Durotar?",a="The Razormane quilboar view all neighboring territories as rightfully theirs, seeking to expand their thorny thickets and hunting lands at the expense of the new Horde settlements.",al={"why quilboar attack","why are razormane here","quilboar invasion"}},{q="Who leads the quilboar at the Razormane Grounds?",a="The encampment is commanded by Captain Flat Tusk, leader of the Razormane Battleguard, alongside the earth-shaping geomancer Geolord Mottle.",al={"razormane bosses","who leads the razormane grounds","captain flat tusk"}},{q="Why are there so many bones around the camp?",a="The Razormane are aggressive scavengers and hunters who strip the local wildlife down to the bone to feed their raiders, leaving the carcasses behind to mark their territory.",al={"bones in camp","razormane animal carcasses","why dead animals"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For the orcs of Durotar, the Razormane Grounds are a persistent threat right in the heart of their new homeland, requiring young warriors to prove their mettle by culling the quilboar.",["faction:Horde"]="Keeping the Razormane Grounds suppressed is vital to securing travel and supply lines between the Barrens and the Horde capital of Orgrimmar."},kw={"captain flat tusk","durotar","geolord mottle","quilboar","raggaran","razormane","razormane grounds"},rel={"zone:durotar","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},src={"Razormane Grounds"}}
E["subzone:razorwind-canyon"] = {t="subzone",n="Razorwind Canyon",z="durotar",s="Razorwind Canyon is a winding, rocky gulch split across the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. Infested by the aggressive Dustwind harpies, the canyon poses a persistent danger to travelers moving north toward the Horde's capital.",h="Razorwind Canyon is a winding, rocky gulch split across the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Threat on the High Road",b="Razorwind Canyon flanks the central artery linking Razor Hill to Orgrimmar, carving paths into both the eastern bluffs and the western scrublands toward Tor'kren Farm. The canyon is the nesting ground of the Dustwind harpies, territorial creatures that strike without hesitation at travelers who stray too close to their roosts. Their presence so near the capital's trade routes makes clearing out these gullies an ongoing necessity for the defenders of Durotar.",sp=0},{t="Passages and Ravines",b="Beyond serving as harpy nests, the twists of Razorwind Canyon function as hidden routes through Durotar's red rock hills. The eastern branch tunnels deeply into the crags, providing a passage through a cavern into Drygulch Ravine. Because the harpies roost on the high perches and descend in flocks, unwary adventurers traversing these passes can easily find themselves surrounded and cut down.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Razorwind Canyon located?",a="Razorwind Canyon is located in central Durotar, flanking both sides of the main road running between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. Entrances lead into it north of Razor Hill, near Tor'kren Farm, and through a cave connecting to Drygulch Ravine.",al={"razorwind canyon location","where is razorwind canyon","how to find razorwind canyon"}},{q="What creatures inhabit Razorwind Canyon?",a="The canyon is heavily inhabited by the Dustwind harpies. These aggressive, avian creatures nest in large clutches throughout the gullies and rocky outcroppings, preying on unwary travelers.",al={"razorwind mobs","what lives in razorwind canyon","harpy canyon durotar"}},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about this canyon?",a="Razorwind Canyon borders the primary trade and travel route between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. The nesting harpies frequently harass couriers, supply caravans, and travelers passing along the central road.",al={"why care about razorwind","orgrimmar threat razorwind"}},{q="Does Razorwind Canyon connect to other areas?",a="Yes. In addition to opening onto the main road, the canyon provides trails west toward Tor'kren Farm, as well as an eastern cavern leading into Drygulch Ravine.",al={"canyon connections","where does razorwind lead"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the Dustwind harpies from Razorwind Canyon is vital to keeping the main thoroughfare between Razor Hill and the capital of Orgrimmar safe for couriers and fresh recruits.",["race:Orc"]="The harpies nesting right along Durotar's central roadway are an insult to the security of the orcish homeland, requiring young warriors to cull their numbers."},kw={"drygulch ravine","durotar","dustwind harpies","razor hill","razorwind canyon","tor'kren farm"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:razor-hill","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:drygulch-ravine","subzone:tor-kren-farm","quest:835","quest:834"},src={"Razorwind Canyon"}}
E["subzone:rocktusk-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Rocktusk Farm",z="durotar",s="Rocktusk Farm is a small swine ranch situated in northern Durotar just down the road outside the gates of Orgrimmar. Tucked near the fortified approaches of the capital, the stead supplies vital meat and provisions to the city's inhabitants.",h="Rocktusk Farm is a small swine ranch situated in northern Durotar just down the road outside the gates of...",sec={{t="Provisions for the Capital",b="Carved out of the arid soil of Durotar, Rocktusk Farm is dedicated to raising hardy swine suited to the rough desert climate. Due to Durotar's notoriously dry and stony ground, raising crops is difficult, making domestic swine farms an essential lifeline for feeding Orgrimmar's burgeoning population. Nestled close to the capital's fortified perimeter, the homestead enjoys a degree of safety rarely found in the harsh wilds of the red canyonlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rocktusk Farm used for?",a="Rocktusk Farm is a domestic pig farm. It raises swine to supply fresh meat and provisions to the neighboring capital of Orgrimmar, where arable land is scarce.",al={"what is this place","rocktusk farm purpose","why are there pigs here"}},{q="Where is Rocktusk Farm located?",a="The farm sits in northern Durotar, located just southwest down the road from the main gates of Orgrimmar and nestled along the rocky bluffs.",al={"where is rocktusk farm","rocktusk farm location"}},{q="Is the farm safe from wild beasts?",a="Its close proximity to Orgrimmar and nearby Horde military patrols keeps it safer than most outlying homesteads in Durotar, though wild beasts and roaming pests still prowl the outskirts.",al={"is rocktusk farm safe","dangers at rocktusk farm"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Settled just outside the capital, the swine reared here are critical sustenance for the warriors and laborers stationed in Orgrimmar.",["profession:Cooking"]="The pigs raised on the farm are prized by Horde cooks searching for fresh pork, ribs, and savory cuts to roast."},kw={"durotar","horde provisions","orgrimmar","pig farm","rocktusk farm","swine"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","subzone:gates-of-orgrimmar"},src={"Rocktusk Farm"}}
E["subzone:scuttle-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="Scuttle Coast",z="durotar",s="The Scuttle Coast is the wave-battered eastern shoreline of Durotar, situated between Razor Hill and Tiragarde Keep. The rocky beach is strewn with sunken wreckage from Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet, making it an active scavenging ground for the Horde and a lingering reminder of recent naval warfare.",h="The Scuttle Coast is the wave-battered eastern shoreline of Durotar, situated between Razor Hill and...",sec={{t="Wreckage of the Fleet",b="Running along Durotar's eastern edge out to the Great Sea, the Scuttle Coast earned its grim character during the invasion led by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. When the Kul Tiras fleet assaulted the fledgling nation of Durotar, fierce battles with the Horde drove many human warships against the jagged shoals, smashing them into splintered hulks. Today, the shoreline is choked with barnacle-encrusted timber, broken rigging, and salvaged cargo barrels. For the nearby encampments of Razor Hill, the coast represents both a lingering security hazard and a valuable source of recovered provisions and abandoned Alliance mechanisms.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers and Tides",b="The name Scuttle Coast refers not only to the sunken warships deliberately scuttled or grounded during the fighting, but also to the swarms of crabs and makrura that pick through the rotting detritus. While shoreline wildlife and dangerous tides keep casual travelers away, Horde scavengers periodically comb through the wreckage to retrieve valuable equipment, including gnomish technical components abandoned in the cargo holds of the sunken ships.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did all these shipwrecks come from?",a="The shattered ships belonged to the naval fleet of Kul Tiras under Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. They were smashed against Durotar's rocky shallows during the admiral's failed military campaign against the newly founded Horde.",al={"why are there ships here","who owns the wrecked ships","sunken ships durotar"}},{q="Why is it called the Scuttle Coast?",a="The name carries a double meaning. It refers directly to the warships scuttled along the coastline during naval combat, as well as the numerous makrura and crabs that scuttle across the rocky sands.",al={"why is it called scuttle coast","scuttle coast name origin"}},{q="What is the Horde looking for along the coast?",a="Horde scouts and scavengers search the broken holds for salvageable tools, supplies, and discarded gnomish technology left behind by the Alliance forces.",al={"what are orcs salvaging","horde salvage scuttle coast"}},{q="Is the Scuttle Coast safe to travel?",a="No. Aside from treacherous waves and jagged rocks, hostile coastal beasts like makrura prowl the surf, and armed Kul Tiras survivors remain entrenched just to the south at Tiragarde Keep.",al={"scuttle coast dangers","is scuttle coast dangerous"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The broken hulls littering this beach stand as stark monuments to Durotar's defense against Daelin Proudmoore's invading navy.",["profession:Engineering"]="The sunken Alliance holds along the shore contain abandoned gnomish gadgets, scrap metal, and intricate machinery ripe for reverse-engineering."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","kul tiras","makrura","razor hill","scuttle coast","shipwrecks","tiragarde keep"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","topic:kul-tiras","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},src={"Scuttle Coast"}}
E["subzone:sen-jin-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Sen'jin Village",z="durotar",s="Sen'jin Village is a coastal settlement on the southern shores of Durotar, serving as a sanctuary for the Darkspear trolls. Established by Chieftain Vol'jin after his people were driven from their ancestral home on the Echo Isles, the hamlet honors his fallen father, the witch doctor Sen'jin. Today, it stands as a fragile haven focused on survival, herbalism, and reclaiming what was stolen.",h="Sen'jin Village is a coastal settlement on the southern shores of Durotar, serving as a sanctuary for the...",sec={{t="A Refugee Shore",b="When the dark witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the Darkspear and seized control of the Echo Isles, Chieftain Vol'jin was forced to lead the survivors across the strait to the mainland of Durotar. There, nestled beneath coastal cliffs and looking out over the water, they raised crude huts and established Sen'jin Village. The settlement carries the name of Vol'jin's father, the venerable elder who sacrificed himself during the Third War to save their people from coastal murlocs. Despite their close alliance with Thrall's Horde, the trolls here live under the shadow of exile, staring daily across the shallows at the home they lost.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Isles",b="Daily life in Sen'jin Village revolves around preparation and defense. Between local Centaur raids, aggressive sea beasts, and Zalazane's hexes reaching across the sea, the villagers rely heavily on herbal remedies and brewing potent alchemical spirits. While Vol'jin coordinates broader tribal defense from the Horde capital, local shamans, hunters, and scouts gather here to recruit fresh wanderers stepping out of the Valley of Trials. Their aim is clear: to gather resources, protect Durotar's southern flank, and plot the eventual downfall of the traitor Zalazane.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did the Darkspear build Sen'jin Village here?",a="The Darkspear fled across the strait to the Durotar coastline after the witch doctor Zalazane went mad and took control of their home on the Echo Isles. Sen'jin Village was established by Vol'jin as a temporary refuge and staging ground just across the water from their stolen land.",al={"why is senjin village here","why are trolls in durotar","why did trolls leave echo isles"}},{q="Who was Sen'jin?",a="Sen'jin was a respected witch doctor and chieftain of the Darkspear tribe, as well as the father of Vol'jin. During the Third War, he foresaw Thrall's arrival and sacrificed his life while saving his tribe and the young Horde from fanatical sea murlocs in the South Seas.",al={"who was senjin","who is senjin named after","senjin lore"}},{q="Why are there so many herbalists and alchemists here?",a="The local witch doctors and medicine men rely heavily on Durotar's coastal flora and scorpok venoms to concoct charms, antidotes, and rituals. These botanical brews sustain the wounded and offer wards against the dark hexes drifting over from the Echo Isles.",al={"senjin village trainers","professions in senjin village","why alchemy here"}},{q="Can you reach the Echo Isles from Sen'jin Village?",a="The Echo Isles sit directly across the eastern water from the village. Adventurers often swim or wade across the shallow channel to strike back at Zalazane's voodoo cultists, recover stolen artifacts, or gather resources for the village defenders.",al={"how to get to echo isles","isles off senjin coast","swimming to echo isles"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls emerging from the Valley of Trials, this refuge is the beating heart of their displaced people, holding memories of their lost chieftain and the enduring sting of Zalazane's betrayal.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The village is a vital starting center for natural medicine, surrounded by coastal Peacebloom, Silverleaf, and Earthroot used by local witch doctors to treat venom and curses."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","senjin","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"topic:darkspear-tribe","subzone:echo-isles","npc:vol-jin","quest:826","zone:durotar","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","topic:third-war"},src={"Sen'jin Village"}}
E["subzone:sen-jin-village-outskirts"] = {t="subzone",n="Sen'jin Village Outskirts",z="durotar",s="The Sen'jin Village Outskirts encompass the arid, sun-scorched fringes surrounding the primary Darkspear troll settlement in Durotar. Ringed by red rock ridges and the nearby eastern coast, these plains separate the fragile coastal refuge from the harsher wilderness inland.",h="The Sen'jin Village Outskirts encompass the arid, sun-scorched fringes surrounding the primary Darkspear...",sec={{t="On the Village Boundary",b="Spreading out around Sen'jin Village, the outskirts form a rugged buffer zone between the Darkspear settlement and the untamed wilds of southern Durotar. The terrain is dominated by dry red dirt, sparse scrubland, and sheer crags overlooking the Great Sea. For young troll warriors and shamans, these perimeter lands represent their first taste of the wilderness, serving as the frontline against roving wildlife, Kul Tiras scouts from the coast, and lingering hostile threats eager to strike at the fledgling troll sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sen'jin Village Outskirts?",a="It is the open wilderness immediately surrounding Sen'jin Village in southern Durotar, serving as a boundary between the troll settlement and the surrounding arid plains.",al={"senjin outskirts","what is this area","outskirts of senjin"}},{q="Why is this area important to the Darkspear?",a="Having recently fled their flooded island home in the South Seas and lost the Echo Isles to Zalazane, the Darkspear rely on this perimeter to guard their primary coastal foothold on Kalimdor.",al={"why do trolls care","darkspear presence"}},{q="What threats wander these outskirts?",a="The open perimeter sees roaming scorpid, feral boars, and human interlopers scouting up from the southern shoreline, threatening the safety of the nearby village.",al={"dangers here","enemies in the outskirts"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Every young Darkspear remembers cutting their teeth in the dusty reaches around Sen'jin, proving they can protect the tribe's last haven on the Durotar coast.",["faction:Horde"]="Holding the southern approaches to Sen'jin Village keeps the Darkspear secure and prevents hostile incursions from moving further north toward Orgrimmar."},kw={"coast","darkspear","durotar","outskirts","sen'jin","trolls","village"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","npc:vol-jin"},src={"Sen'jin Village Outskirts"}}
E["subzone:shrine-of-the-dormant-flame"] = {t="subzone",n="Shrine of the Dormant Flame",z="durotar",s="Perched atop the highest peak northwest of the Valley of Trials, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is a secluded sanctuary revered by Horde shaman. Guided by its solitary keeper, Telf Joolam, initiates make the treacherous climb to commune with the element of fire and prove their spiritual mastery.",h="Perched atop the highest peak northwest of the Valley of Trials, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is a...",sec={{t="A Summit of Trial and Flame",b="Reaching the Shrine of the Dormant Flame requires braving a narrow, winding trail that begins along the Southfury River at the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed. High above the red cliffs of Durotar, the mountain summit offers a commanding view of the surrounding lands, though a single misstep along the precipice means certain death. In this quiet refuge wanders Telf Joolam, a solitary hermit tasked with overseeing sacred rites. For aspiring orc and troll shaman undertaking the ritual Call of Fire, the shrine's brazier serves as the crucible where they must ignite slumbering coals using the ember of a vanquished elemental, proving their power to commune with and respect the destructive spirits of flame.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="The path begins along the Southfury River on the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed, just northwest of the Valley of Trials. A narrow mountain trail spirals around the peak, leading directly up to the summit.",al={"how to get to shrine of the dormant flame","path to dormant flame","climb dormant flame mountain"}},{q="Why is this shrine important to shaman?",a="The shrine is a sacred site where aspiring Horde shaman learn to understand and command the element of fire. As part of their Call of Fire journey, initiates must travel to this summit to prepare a ritual draft and kindle the dormant brazier.",al={"shrine of dormant flame purpose","why do shaman go here","call of fire shrine"}},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is a solitary troll hermit who serves as the keeper of the shrine. He guides young shaman through their trials, concocting a draught of fire to awaken their spiritual sight and testing their resolve.",al={"who is telf joolam","dormant flame npc","shrine keeper"}},{q="What happens when you kindle the brazier?",a="Shaman who have gathered the required ritual components and defeated a hostile fire elemental place its burning ember into the brazier. This acts as an offering to prove they have the strength and discipline to tame the volatile spirit of flame.",al={"brazier of dormant flame","igniting the flame","shrine brazier quest"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Every young orc and troll shaman must make the arduous trek up this crag to kindle their spiritual connection with fire and earn their Fire Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="Tucked away in the mountains above Durotar, this isolated shrine preserves ancient elemental rites vital to the spiritual heart of the new Horde."},kw={"call of fire","dormant flame","durotar","fire totem","shrine","southfury watershed","telf joolam","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:merchant-coast","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Shrine of the Dormant Flame"}}
E["subzone:skull-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Skull Rock",z="durotar",s="Skull Rock is a cavern tucked into the eastern coastal cliffs of Durotar, just east of Orgrimmar. It serves as a fortified coven for the demonic Burning Blade cult right under the capital's nose.",h="Skull Rock is a cavern tucked into the eastern coastal cliffs of Durotar, just east of Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Den of Cultists",b="Hidden beneath the crags of northeastern Durotar, Skull Rock is one of the most perilous strongholds of the Burning Blade cult in the region. Dark cultists, fel-worshipping orcs, and summoners gather deep within the winding tunnels to practice demonic arts and weave conspiracies against the nascent Horde. The cell is led by the dangerous warlock Gazz'uz, whose operations pose an imminent threat to the nearby gates of Orgrimmar and travelers traversing the eastern shoreline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Skull Rock?",a="Skull Rock is a cave system situated in northeastern Durotar along the coast. It is occupied by cultists of the Burning Blade who use its natural cover to plot against Thrall's Horde.",al={"skull rock cave","where is skull rock","what is in skull rock"}},{q="Who controls Skull Rock?",a="The cavern is infested by the Burning Blade cult, led by the orc warlock Gazz'uz from the deepest chamber of the cave.",al={"who leads skull rock","who runs skull rock","skull rock boss"}},{q="Why does the Horde care about this cave?",a="Its proximity to Orgrimmar makes it a severe security hazard. The Burning Blade actively seeks to undermine Thrall's new realm and plunge the orcs back into demonic servitude.",al={"why clear skull rock","why is skull rock dangerous"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The dark arts practiced within Skull Rock showcase the unchecked spread of demonic influence that Thrall's Horde seeks to root out and control.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the cultists from Skull Rock is vital to securing the coastal approaches to Durotar and protecting Orgrimmar from subversion from within."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","durotar","gazz'uz","orgrimmar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:827","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Skull Rock"}}
E["subzone:spirit-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Spirit Rock",z="durotar",s="Spirit Rock is a sacred crag perched in the rugged bluffs above the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Reached by a winding trail known as the Hidden Path, it serves as a secluded holy site where initiates commune directly with the elemental forces of the land.",h="Spirit Rock is a sacred crag perched in the rugged bluffs above the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary of the Elements",b="Overlooking the red canyon where young Horde warriors and scouts begin their training, Spirit Rock stands as an altar of communion. Isolated from the clatter of the Valley of Trials, it is approached only via the Hidden Path winding up the rocky ridgeline. Aspiring shaman make pilgrimages to this desolate outcrop to drink the traditional sapta, piercing the veil of the physical world to hear the rumblings and whisperings of the earth itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Spirit Rock used for?",a="Spirit Rock is a sacred site used primarily by Horde shaman initiates. By consuming a specialized draught known as an Earth Sapta at the rock, novices gain the spiritual vision required to commune directly with the spirits of the earth.",al={"spirit rock purpose","what happens at spirit rock","spirit rock use"}},{q="How do you reach Spirit Rock?",a="Spirit Rock sits high in the cliffs above the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar. It is accessible by ascending the Hidden Path, a narrow, unmarked trail that winds out of the canyon floor into the rugged hills.",al={"how to get to spirit rock","path to spirit rock","spirit rock location"}},{q="What is a sapta?",a="A sapta is a ceremonial elemental brew prepared by shaman trainers. Drinking it alters the seeker's perception, allowing them to perceive elemental manifestations that remain invisible to ordinary senses.",al={"earth sapta","what is sapta","sapta drink"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Spirit Rock is a vital rite of passage for young orc and troll shaman, who venture up the Hidden Path to drink the Earth Sapta and forge their first bond with the spirits of stone and soil."},kw={"call of earth","durotar","earth spirits","hidden path","sapta","shaman","spirit rock","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:hidden-path","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1520","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Spirit Rock"}}
E["subzone:the-den"] = {t="subzone",n="The Den",z="durotar",s="The Den is the sheltered cave at the heart of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar. Serving as the primary base of operations for young orc and troll adventurers, it provides martial and magical training before they set out into the wider world.",h="The Den is the sheltered cave at the heart of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar.",sec={{t="Cradle of the Horde",b="Tucked into the red canyon walls of the Valley of Trials, the Den serves as an austere proving ground. Within its carved, shadowy interior, novice fighters, spellcasters, and hunters report to veterans like Gornek and Zureetha Fargaze. It is here that fledglings receive their foundational combat instruction, supplies, and initial rites of passage, hardening them for the harsh realities of Durotar and the greater struggles facing the new Horde.",sp=0},{t="A Watchful Outpost",b="Beyond housing class trainers and provisions, the Den functions as an active field redoubt. Between dispatching new recruits to cull the local beasts and aggressive quillboars, the overseers maintain a strict, vigilant watch over the valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Den?",a="The Den serves as the central command post and training sanctuary within the Valley of Trials. Here, novice orcs and Darkspear trolls gather to learn basic class techniques, purchase provisions, and receive assignments that prove their loyalty and combat readiness to the Horde.",al={"what is the den","why is the den here","purpose of the den"}},{q="Who runs things inside the Den?",a="The encampment is supervised by veteran overseers such as Gornek and Foreman Thazz'ril, along with spiritual and magical mentors like Zureetha Fargaze and Canaga Earthcaller, all working together to instruct the newest generation of warriors and mystics.",al={"who leads the den","who is in charge","den overseer"}},{q="Can you learn primary professions here?",a="No. The Den only hosts basic class trainers and general equipment merchants. New adventurers must travel north to Razor Hill or on to Orgrimmar to study primary trade skills such as Blacksmithing, Leatherworking, or Mining.",al={"profession trainers den","can i learn blacksmithing here","train mining in den"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Every young orc begins their journey at the Den, shedding the complacency of internment camps and blood haze to earn their place through discipline and labor.",["race:Troll"]="Following the devastation of the Darkspear Isles, young Darkspear trolls train in the Den alongside their orc allies, proving their mettle under the Horde's banner."},kw={"durotar","gornek","starting cave","the den","trainers","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:gornek","npc:zureetha-fargaze","subzone:razor-hill","npc:magga","npc:mai-ah","topic:troll"},src={"The Den"}}
E["subzone:thunder-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Thunder Ridge",z="durotar",s="Thunder Ridge is a rugged canyon in western Durotar, situated just southwest of Orgrimmar along the banks of the Southfury River. Once a lush grove of ancient trees inhabited by herds of thunder lizards, the canyon has suffered severe deforestation from human lumber operations and dark sorcery. Today, the agitated beasts and lingering cultists pose an ongoing threat to nearby settlements.",h="Thunder Ridge is a rugged canyon in western Durotar, situated just southwest of Orgrimmar along the banks of...",sec={{t="A Scarred Sanctuary",b="Not long ago, Thunder Ridge was a rare green haven in arid Durotar, sustained by ancient trees and watched over by the spirit Owa'nohe. Its tranquil balance shattered shortly after the Third War when human interlopers from Kul Tiras began felling its timber, driving the native thunder lizards into a frenzy. Later, fel sorcery wielded by the Burning Blade finished the destruction, stripping the canopy and leaving behind a barren, exposed gorge where angry lightning-spewing beasts now roam unrestrained.",sp=0},{t="Cultists and Tests of Strength",b="The denizens of Orgrimmar keep a wary eye on the ridge. The Burning Blade maintains a pocket of cultists here under the warlock Fizzle Darkclaw, who uses demonic magic to sow further chaos across Durotar. Horde veterans like Orgnil Soulscar task scouts with hunting down the cabal, while warrior trainers such as Uzzek send aspiring fighters into the crags to test their resilience against the enraged thunder lizards.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the trees in Thunder Ridge?",a="Thunder Ridge was once a dense woodland, but it suffered two waves of destruction. First, lumber operations run by Kul Tiran forces aggressively felled its ancient timber shortly after Durotar was founded. Later, the Burning Blade used dark, demonic magic to raze the surviving groves, wiping out the forest entirely.",al={"why is thunder ridge barren","thunder ridge forest","deforestation thunder ridge"}},{q="Why are the thunder lizards so aggressive here?",a="The thunder lizards lived peacefully among the ridge's ancient trees until outside intrusion ruined their habitat. The noise and destruction of human logging, combined with lingering fel corruption from the Burning Blade cultists, drove the herds into an agitated madness that makes them attack anyone who ventures into the canyon.",al={"angry lizards thunder ridge","thunder lizards durotar"}},{q="Who is Fizzle Darkclaw?",a="Fizzle Darkclaw is a leader within the Burning Blade cult who established an encampment within Thunder Ridge. From this staging ground, he and his followers direct dark rituals to destabilize the region, prompting Horde leaders like Orgnil Soulscar to place a bounty on his head.",al={"fizzle darkclaw lore","who is darkclaw","burning blade thunder ridge"}},{q="Did Rexxar fight in Thunder Ridge?",a="Yes. Shortly after Durotar was founded, the Champion of the Horde Rexxar traveled here to gather shimmerweed for the farseer Drek'Thar. While in the canyon, Rexxar discovered the human lumber camp driving the lizards wild, forcing him to cull the frenzied beasts and salvage their eggs for Drek'Thar to study.",al={"rexxar thunder ridge","drek'thar thunder ridge"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Warrior mentors like Uzzek send their trainees into Thunder Ridge to test their defensive prowess against the sheer physical force and lightning shocks of the wild thunder lizards.",["faction:Horde"]="Nestled just outside Orgrimmar's western bluffs, the ridge must be kept clear of Burning Blade agents like Fizzle Darkclaw to prevent demonic subversion at the capital's doorstep."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","fizzle darkclaw","orgnil soulscar","rexxar","southfury river","thunder lizards","thunder ridge","uzzek"},rel={"zone:durotar","quest:806","quest:1498","npc:orgnil-soulscar","npc:uzzek","subzone:southfury-river","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:drygulch-ravine"},src={"Thunder Ridge"}}
E["subzone:tiragarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Tiragarde Keep",z="durotar",s="Tiragarde Keep is a fortified human stronghold situated along Durotar's Scuttle Coast, south of Razor Hill. Originally built during Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's invasion, the ruined citadel remains garrisoned by hostile Kul Tiran marines under Lieutenant Benedict. It serves as a defiant, permanent thorn in the Horde's side right on their home territory.",h="Tiragarde Keep is a fortified human stronghold situated along Durotar's Scuttle Coast, south of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="Proudmoore's Bastion",b="Erected during Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's campaign to eradicate Thrall's newly founded realm, Tiragarde Keep provided the Kul Tiran fleet an entrenched beachhead on the red shores of Durotar. Although the Horde eventually broke the siege and killed Proudmoore at Theramore Isle, the keep was never fully abandoned. Resupply forces under Lieutenant Benedict reclaimed the shattered stone walls, following the late Admiral's standing orders to wage an unyielding war against the orcs, entirely refusing the peace forged by Lady Jaina Proudmoore.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Flank",b="Today, the keep's gleaming white battlements stand in harsh contrast against Durotar's crimson cliffs. Well-trained Kul Tiras sailors and marines patrol the ramparts and launch raids targeting supply lines near Razor Hill. For the Horde, Tiragarde Keep is an ongoing security crisis and a live proving ground. Orc and troll commanders constantly task young warriors with assaulting the fortress and cutting down Benedict's soldiers, seeking to contain the garrison before the humans can mount a deeper inland offensive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there humans in Durotar?",a="These humans are Kul Tiras sailors and marines who arrived with Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore during his invasion following the Third War. They reject peace with the Horde and maintain this garrison to harass the orcs.",al={"why are alliance here","who are the humans in tiragarde","human soldiers durotar"}},{q="Are these humans part of Jaina's forces in Theramore?",a="No. While Jaina Proudmoore rules Theramore Isle and maintains an uneasy truce with Thrall, these soldiers follow the orders of her late father, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. They consider any peace with orcs unacceptable treason.",al={"is tiragarde theramore","are they jaina proudmoore's men","theramore soldiers here"}},{q="Who commands Tiragarde Keep?",a="The stronghold is commanded by Lieutenant Benedict, a Kul Tiran officer acting on posthumous invasion orders left by Admiral Proudmoore to secure the coast and attack the Horde.",al={"tiragarde boss","who leads tiragarde keep","lieutenant benedict"}},{q="Why hasn't the Horde simply wiped them out?",a="The keep is fortified and manned by disciplined, well-armed Kul Tiran troops. While the defenders from Razor Hill frequently skirmish with the garrison and use it as a proving ground for new recruits, launching a full-scale siege would draw heavy casualties and divert vital resources away from securing the rest of Durotar.",al={"why not destroy tiragarde","why is the keep still here"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Tiragarde Keep is a blatant Alliance invasion base right on Durotar's doorstep; raiding its ramparts and eliminating Lieutenant Benedict is a rite of passage for young soldiers serving Razor Hill.",["race:Human"]="The garrison represents the unbending, vengeful legacy of Kul Tiras and Admiral Proudmoore, fighting a stubborn guerrilla war in defiance of Jaina Proudmoore's diplomacy."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","razor hill","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:scuttle-coast","subzone:razor-hill","quest:784","topic:kul-tiras","subzone:theramore-isle","npc:jaina-proudmoore","npc:thrall"},src={"Tiragarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:tor-kren-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Tor'kren Farm",z="durotar",s="Tor'kren Farm is a quiet, struggling swine farm nestled in northwestern Durotar, tucked between Thunder Ridge and the Southfury Watershed. It is maintained solely by Misha Tor'kren, an aging orc widow whose life has been weighed down by grief and the harsh frontier.",h="Tor'kren Farm is a quiet, struggling swine farm nestled in northwestern Durotar, tucked between Thunder Ridge...",sec={{t="A Lonely Homestead",b="Carving out a living from the dry, unforgiving red dirt of Durotar is never simple, but Tor'kren Farm has had a harder time than most. Situated southeast of Thunder Ridge, the homestead focuses on raising pigs in a rugged climate where feed and water are scarce. Unlike the bustling trade posts or heavily defended barracks of the Horde, the farm stands isolated and quiet, producing meager yields in the shadow of nearby bluffs.",sp=0},{t="A Mother's Loss",b="The farm's greatest burden is not poor soil, but tragedy. Misha Tor'kren once worked these pens alongside her beloved son, Kron. That life ended when Kron journeyed down to the Southfury River to hunt the ferocious crocolisks lurking along the banks and never returned. Left to carry on alone, Misha tends the swine by herself, holding fast to her homestead and clinging to the memory of her fallen child.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tor'kren Farm located?",a="Tor'kren Farm lies in northwestern Durotar, situated southeast of the canyon known as Thunder Ridge and just north of the Southfury Watershed.",al={"tor'kren farm location","where is torkren farm","find tor'kren farm"}},{q="Who lives at Tor'kren Farm?",a="The farm is tended solely by Misha Tor'kren, an elderly orc widow who raises pigs on the homestead by herself.",al={"who runs tor'kren farm","tor'kren farm npcs","who is misha tor'kren"}},{q="What happened to Misha's son?",a="Misha's son, Kron, was killed while hunting crocolisks along the nearby Southfury River several years ago, leaving his mother to manage the farm on her own.",al={"misha son","kron tor'kren death","who is kron"}},{q="What does Tor'kren Farm produce?",a="It operates as a swine farm, though harsh terrain and isolation keep its profits far leaner than other livestock operations in Durotar.",al={"torkren farm business","what kind of farm is torkren","tor'kren pigs"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The quiet tragedy at Tor'kren Farm reveals the everyday sacrifices made by ordinary Horde settlers striving to tame Durotar's wild frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="The fate of Kron serves as a grim warning to young hunters about the deadly predators lurking along the Southfury River."},kw={"durotar","kron","misha tor'kren","pig farm","southfury river","southfury watershed","thunder ridge","tor'kren farm"},rel={"npc:misha-tor-kren","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:durotar"},src={"Tor'kren Farm"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-trials"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Trials",z="durotar",s="Tucked away behind the rugged red cliffs of southern Durotar, the Valley of Trials serves as the testing ground for new recruits of the Horde. Young orcs and their Darkspear troll allies come here to prove their strength and earn their place among the warriors of Kalimdor. Those who survive the valley's harsh wildlife and hidden threats depart ready to defend their fledgling nation.",h="Tucked away behind the rugged red cliffs of southern Durotar, the Valley of Trials serves as the testing...",sec={{t="A Crucible of Sand and Stone",b="The Valley of Trials is designed to weed out the weak before they ever set foot in the broader reaches of Durotar. Overseen by chieftains and trainers stationed in the carved cliffside shelter known as The Den, young fighters are thrust into the sun-scorched gulch to hunt scorpids, culled aggressive boars, and enforce discipline among lazy peons harvesting scarce timber. The trial is uncompromising: those who prove their mettle earn the right to venture forth as true soldiers of the Horde, while those who fail are left to bleach beneath the desert sun.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow in the North",b="What was once an isolated training ground has recently taken on a far more sinister edge. In the natural caves along the northern cliffs, cultists of the Burning Blade have taken root, summoning minor demonic familiars into the valley. While trainers treat these interlopers as live-combat practice for fresh recruits, the presence of fel magic so close to Orgrimmar's threshold fuels dark rumors that the Shadow Council is actively attempting to sink its claws back into the orcish people.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Valley of Trials?",a="It is the traditional proving ground for recruits of the Horde, primarily young orcs and Darkspear trolls. Within its sheltered canyons, new adventurers complete rigorous tasks to demonstrate their martial skill, survival instinct, and loyalty before being permitted to leave for the rest of Durotar.",al={"why are orcs here","what is this place","valley of trials purpose"}},{q="What is The Den?",a="The Den is a central cavern carved into the valley's western cliffs. It houses class trainers, vendors, and overseers like Gornek who direct new recruits, equip them, and monitor their progress during their initial trials.",al={"the den","cave in valley of trials","who is in the den"}},{q="Why are there demons in a beginner's training ground?",a="Cultists belonging to the Burning Blade have established a secret coven in the northern caves. Although trainers use their weak familiars to test recruits, the cult's presence suggests shadowy forces like the Shadow Council are seeking a foothold right on Durotar's doorsteps.",al={"why demons in valley of trials","burning blade in durotar","demons north cave"}},{q="Who is Sarkoth?",a="Sarkoth is an unusually large, venomous scorpid residing in the rocky heights of the valley. Due to his aggression and lethality, instructors task promising recruits with hunting him down to test their courage and obtain samples of his potent venom.",al={"sarkoth lore","giant scorpid","sarkoth quest"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The valley represents a rite of passage for every young orc seeking honor, echoing the warrior traditions of Draenor in a newly forged homeland.",["race:Troll"]="Having lost their home on the Echo Isles to Zalazane, the Darkspear trolls train alongside their orc allies in this canyon to earn their place in the Horde."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","gornek","orcs","peons","sarkoth","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","zone:durotar","quest:1089","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:echo-isles","topic:horde","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:shadow-council"},src={"Valley of Trials"}}
E["topic:grommash-hellscream"] = {t="topic",n="Grommash Hellscream",z="durotar",s="Grommash Hellscream was the legendary chieftain of the Warsong clan, a close brother-in-arms to Warchief Thrall, and the first orc to drink the blood of Mannoroth. Though his thirst for battle once bound his people to the Burning Legion, he redeemed the orcish race by slaying the demon lord in Ashenvale at the cost of his own life.",h="Grommash Hellscream was the legendary chieftain of the Warsong clan, a close brother-in-arms to Warchief...",sec={{t="The First Drink and the Iron Will",b="Before the Dark Portal ever bridged worlds, Grom Hellscream led the Warsong clan with unyielding ferocity, distinguished by his pitch-black tattooed jaw and the deadly sweep of his two-handed axe, Gorehowl. When Gul'dan and the Shadow Council offered the chalice of demonic strength on Draenor, Grom was the first chieftain to drink the blood of the pit lord Mannoroth. That fateful draught doomed the orcish race to demonic subservience and a burning bloodlust. Yet unlike many chieftains who perished or succumbed entirely, Grom possessed an iron will that kept his fierce spirit intact, surviving the horrors of the old Horde while harboring an unspoken ache for what his people had surrendered.",sp=0},{t="A Brotherhood in the Wilds",b="Kept behind on Draenor during the Second War, Grom later crossed through the Dark Portal only to be stranded when the rift was shattered. For nearly fifteen years, Grom and his surviving Warsong warriors evaded the Alliance of Lordaeron, enduring the lethargy and despair that fell upon the orcs after the demon blood faded. Hope rekindled when a young fugitive named Thrall sought him out in the wilderness. Recognizing Thrall's strength and noble heart, Grom mentored him in the proud heritage of their people. Alongside Orgrim Doomhammer, the two rallied their disparate clans, broke open the human internment camps, and ignited the birth of the New Horde.",sp=0},{t="Fall and Final Redemption",b="Upon arriving in Kalimdor during the Third War, Grom's unquenched aggression resurfaced in the ancient forests of Ashenvale. Beset by the night elves and the demigod Cenarius, Grom succumbed once more, drinking from a corrupted fountain infused with Mannoroth's blood to save his clan. Enslaved anew by the demon lord, Grom turned against his own people until Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore captured and cleansed his corrupted spirit with ancient shamanic and arcane rites. Fully restored to his senses and burdened by immense guilt, Grom pursued Mannoroth into Demon Fall Canyon. In a desperate final strike, he drove Gorehowl into the demon lord's chest, severing the demonic curse forever as hellfire claimed his life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Grommash Hellscream?",a="Grommash 'Grom' Hellscream was the chieftain of the Warsong clan and Thrall's trusted lieutenant. He was famous for his razor-sharp axe, Gorehowl, and infamous as the first orc to accept the demonic pact by drinking Mannoroth's blood. He later redeemed his legacy by slaying Mannoroth in Kalimdor, freeing the entire orcish race from the Blood Curse.",al={"who is grom","who was hellscream","grom hellscream backstory"}},{q="How did Grom die?",a="Grom died in Demon Fall Canyon within Ashenvale alongside Thrall. Confronting the pit lord Mannoroth, Grom launched himself into the air and cleaved the demon's chest with Gorehowl. The fatal strike shattered the demon's heart, but the ensuing burst of demonic hellfire fatally wounded Grom, who died declaring that he had finally freed himself and his people.",al={"grom death","how did grom hellscream die","who killed grom"}},{q="What is Grom's connection to Thrall?",a="When Thrall escaped the internment camp of Durnholde, Grom was the first clan chieftain he encountered. Grom took the young orc under his wing, teaching him orcish traditions, language, and culture. Thrall came to view Grom as an older brother and spiritual guide, while Grom saw Thrall as the visionary who could lead their shattered race back to honor.",al={"thrall and grom","how did thrall know grom","were thrall and grom friends"}},{q="Why was Grom's jaw tattooed black?",a="Upon his ascension to chieftain of the Warsong clan on Draenor, Grom ritually tattooed his lower jaw a solid shade of pitch-black. It served as a distinct emblem of his authority and iron will throughout his life, making his ferocious war cries instantly recognizable on the battlefield.",al={"grom black jaw","why is groms jaw black","grom tattooed lower jaw"}},{q="Why did Grom drink demon blood a second time?",a="While harvesting lumber in Ashenvale, Grom's clan was decimated by the night elves and the demigod Cenarius, whose divine nature made him nearly invincible to mortal weapons. Desperate to ensure his clan's survival, Grom discovered a pool of water corrupted by Mannoroth's blood. Despite knowing the dreadful cost, he drank from it to gain the demonic fury needed to defeat Cenarius.",al={"why did grom drink again","grom chaos orcs","grom drank blood twice"}},{q="Where is Grommash buried?",a="Grom rests in Demon Fall Canyon in southeastern Ashenvale, the exact ground where he struck down Mannoroth. A stone monument stands over his burial site, inscribed with an epitaph authored by Thrall celebrating his courage and ultimate sacrifice for the Horde.",al={"grom grave","grom monument","where is groms tomb"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orcs revere Grommash as their ultimate savior. His sacrifice in Ashenvale broke the demonic Blood Curse that held the race in thrall for generations, allowing the New Horde to walk with pride and free will.",["faction:Horde"]="To the Horde, Grom represents the tragic arc of their founding: a fierce warrior whose reckless temper led them into darkness, but whose unyielding courage bought their survival and freedom in Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves view Grom's memory with lingering bitterness, remembering him as the demon-crazed invader who defiled Ashenvale's sacred groves and murdered the demigod Cenarius.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors study Grom's battlefield prowess and mastery of Gorehowl as the pinnacle of martial aggression, seeing in him the terrible cost of unchecked rage and the sheer power of an indomitable fighting spirit."},kw={"ashenvale","blood curse","cenarius","gorehowl","grom","grommash","hellscream","mannoroth","thrall","warsong"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:warsong-clan","topic:new-horde","zone:ashenvale","topic:third-war","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:burning-legion","npc:jaina-proudmoore"},src={"Grommash Hellscream"}}
E["zone:durotar"] = {t="zone",n="Durotar",z="durotar",s="Durotar is the arid, red-rock homeland founded by Warchief Thrall following the Third War, named in honor of his father, Durotan. Bounded by the Southfury River and the Great Sea, it serves as the heartland of the New Horde and the proving ground for young orcs and Darkspear trolls. Within its harsh canyons lie fortified settlements like Razor Hill, the sprawling warrior city of Orgrimmar, and entrenched hostile holdouts ranging from quilboar tribes to stranded Alliance troops.",h="Durotar is the arid, red-rock homeland founded by Warchief Thrall following the Third War, named in honor of...",sec={{t="A Harsh New Home",b="When Thrall led his people across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, he deliberately sought an untamed frontier where the orcs could carve out an honest existence through labor and grit rather than conquest. Durotar's cracked red soil, baked gullies, and towering red-rock spires remind the orcs deeply of Draenor before its destruction. While the climate is unforgiving, offering little arable land and sparse water, the Horde embraced the landscape's natural defense and austere majesty. Bordered to the west across the Southfury River by the open Barrens and to the north by the ruined wilderness of Azshara, Durotar stands as living proof that the orcs have forged their own destiny.",sp=0},{t="Enemies on the Frontier",b="Though Durotar is firmly under Horde dominion, securing it remains an active war. Razormane quilboar, pushed out during the nation's founding, relentlessly raid settlements and farms from the western crags. Farther south, remnants of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet still hold the crumbling garrison of Tiragarde Keep under Lieutenant Benedict, refusing to surrender. Worse still, demonic remnants of the Burning Blade coven lurk within hidden ravines and deep sea caves, subtly seeking to re-corrupt young orcs with promises of fel power.",sp=0},{t="The Trials of the Darkspear",b="Along the southern coast lies Sen'jin Village, the staging ground for the exiled Darkspear trolls. Led by Master Gadrin, the Darkspear were forced from their home on the nearby Echo Isles when the witch doctor Zalazane lost his mind and used dark voodoo to enslave his kin. Unable to reclaim their islands alone, the Darkspear rely on newly trained orc and troll warriors stepping forth from the Valley of Trials to break Zalazane's hold and secure the coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did Thrall settle the Horde in such a barren desert?",a="Thrall chose this unforgiving territory intentionally. The red earth and rugged mesas reminded the orcs of their ancestral world of Draenor, while its harsh conditions served as penance and a forge for discipline. Thrall believed his people needed to earn their survival through honest hardship rather than claiming fertile lands by conquest, ensuring they would not slide back into bloodthirsty complacency.",al={"why settle here","why durotar","why durotar barren"}},{q="Who was Durotar named after?",a="The land was named in honor of Durotan, Thrall's late father and the former chieftain of the Frostwolf clan. Durotan had opposed the demonic corruption of the orcish clans and was murdered on the orders of the warlock Gul'dan.",al={"who is durotar named for","durotan","origin of durotar name"}},{q="Why are there human soldiers inside Tiragarde Keep?",a="The soldiers at Tiragarde Keep are surviving Kul Tiran marines under Lieutenant Benedict, left over from Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's invasion fleet. Even after Proudmoore was slain, these troops refused to surrender or withdraw, maintaining an entrenched hostile outpost right on Durotar's southern coast.",al={"why humans in durotar","tiragarde keep humans","proudmoore troops durotar"}},{q="What is the conflict on the Echo Isles?",a="The Darkspear trolls originally established their Kalimdor home on the Echo Isles. However, a powerful witch doctor named Zalazane succumbed to madness and turned his dark magic against his brethren, enslaving their minds. The survivors fled to the mainland to establish Sen'jin Village, from which they launch raids to break his hold.",al={"what happened to echo isles","why sen'jin village","zalazane lore"}},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade is a subversive demonic cult loyal to the Shadow Council and the Burning Legion. Operatives lurk in secluded spots like Skull Rock and the Burning Blade Coven, attempting to undermine Thrall's leadership and tempt impressionable orcs back into demonic servitude.",al={"burning blade durotar","skull rock cultists","demons in durotar"}},{q="What connects Durotar to other regions?",a="A bridge over the Southfury River leads west into the Barrens, while a path through northern Orgrimmar crosses into Azshara. Outside Orgrimmar, twin zeppelin towers provide transcontinental air travel directly to Tirisfal Glades, Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale, and Thunder Bluff.",al={"how to leave durotar","durotar travel","durotar exits"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Durotar is your people's new promised land, won through sweat and blood after years of demonic lethargy and internment. Proving your worth in the Valley of Trials is the first rite of passage for every new champion of the Horde.",["race:Troll"]="After escaping the sea witch in the Great Sea, the Darkspear found refuge alongside Thrall in Durotar, but the traitor Zalazane took the Echo Isles from within. Retaking the isles and defending Sen'jin Village is personal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Durotar is the beating heart of the Horde's military strength. Any Alliance traveler found wandering its sun-scorched canyons will be hunted down on sight by aggressive patrols and native beasts alike.",["class:Shaman"]="The arid terrain is steeped in raw elemental spirits. Young shamans visit sacred sites like the Spirit Rock and the Shrine of the Dormant Flame to attune themselves to earth and fire.",["class:Warlock"]="Thrall strictly polices dark magic, forcing the Shadow Council's covens into hiding within places like Skull Rock and beneath the city in the winding caverns of Ragefire Chasm."},kw={"durotan","durotar","echo isles","orgrimmar","razor hill","sen'jin village","skull rock","southfury river","thrall","tiragarde keep","valley of trials","zalazane"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:tiragarde-keep","zone:barrens","zone:ragefire"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Durotar (Classic)","Durotar"}}
